<node id="6c9bf964-aa5d-4b85-a8d8-abeb9d987bc1">
  <data key="d0">{"name":"Survivorship Life Insurance Policy","text":"───────────\n1.1 This is a joint life insurance policy insuring two lives.\n\n1.2 DEATH BENEFIT TRIGGER: The death benefit is payable only upon \n    the death of the SECOND insured to die (survivorship basis).\n\n1.3 If the first insured dies, no death benefit is paid and the \n    policy continues in force covering the surviving insured.\n\n1.4 The death benefit is paid only after both insureds have died.\n\n1.5 PURPOSE: This policy is designed for estate planning and \n    estate tax liquidity purposes.\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE II - DEATH BENEFIT PROVISIONS\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2.1 Upon the death of the second insured, we will pay $2,500,000 \n    to the designated beneficiary, minus any outstanding loans.\n\n2.2 Proof of both deaths must be submitted:\n    • Death certificate of first insured\n    • Death certificate of second insured\n    • Completed claim forms\n\n2.3 Payment will be made within 30 days of receiving complete \n    documentation.\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE III - FIRST DEATH BENEFITS\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n3.1 When the first insured dies, no death benefit is paid, but:\n    (a) Policy continues in force\n    (b) Premium payment obligation continues\n    (c) Policy owner receives written confirmation\n    (d) Death certificate must be filed with us\n\n3.2 The surviving insured becomes a single-life whole life policy \n    for administrative purposes only. Coverage amount and premium \n    remain unchanged.\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE IV - PREMIUM STRUCTURE\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4.1 PREMIUM GUARANTEE PERIOD: Annual premium of $32,400 is \n    guaranteed level for the first 10 policy years.\n\n4.2 AFTER YEAR 10: Premium may increase but will never exceed \n    the maximum guaranteed premium of $48,600 per year.\n\n4.3 Premiums are payable annually on August 20th.\n\n4.4 FIRST DEATH PREMIUM CONTINUATION: Premiums continue after \n    the first death at the","summary":"This is a joint life insurance policy structured on a survivorship basis, paying a $2.5 million death benefit only after both insured individuals have passed away. No benefit is paid upon the first death; however, the policy remains active, premiums continue, and the surviving insured’s status transitions administratively to a single-life policy. The annual premium is guaranteed at $32,400 for the first decade and can rise up to $48,600 thereafter. Claims require proof of both deaths and are processed within 30 days of full documentation submission.","topics":["Joint Life Insurance","Survivorship Benefit","Estate Planning","Premium Structure"],"facts":[{"name":"Joint Life Insurance Policy","sentence":"This is a joint life insurance policy.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["joint life insurance","survivorship basis","two-insured policy"],"entities":[{"name":"joint life insurance policy","type":"POLICY","role":"insures two lives under survivorship clause","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"DEATH BENEFIT TRIGGER","type":"CONCEPT","role":"defines condition for payout eligibility","relational_anchors":["death of the SECOND insured to die"]},{"name":"first insured","type":"PERSON","role":"person who dies first; triggers no payout","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"second insured","type":"PERSON","role":"person whose death triggers final payout","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"we","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"insurance provider making payments","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"the designated beneficiary","type":"BENEFICIARY","role":"recipient of death benefit payment","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"$2,500,000","type":"AMOUNT","role":"amount of death benefit payable","relational_anchors":["minus any outstanding loans"]},{"name":"Death certificate of first insured","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"proof required for claim processing","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Death certificate of second insured","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"proof required for claim processing","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Completed claim forms","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"mandatory submission for benefit disbursement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"within 30 days","type":"DATE","role":"timeframe for payment post-document receipt","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"August 20th","type":"DATE","role":"due date for annual premium payment","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"$32,400","type":"AMOUNT","role":"guaranteed annual premium for first 10 years","relational_anchors":["PREMIUM GUARANTEE PERIOD"]},{"name":"$48,600","type":"AMOUNT","role":"maximum allowed annual premium after Year 10","relational_anchors":["after Year 10"]}]},{"name":"Joint Life Insurance Coverage","sentence":"The policy insures two lives.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["joint life insurance","two-insured policy","survivorship basis"],"entities":[{"name":"joint life insurance policy","type":"POLICY","role":"insures two lives under survivorship clause","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"DEATH BENEFIT TRIGGER","type":"CONCEPT","role":"defines condition for payout eligibility","relational_anchors":["death of the SECOND insured to die"]},{"name":"first insured","type":"PERSON","role":"person who dies first; triggers no payout","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"second insured","type":"PERSON","role":"person whose death triggers final payout","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"we","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"insurance provider making payments","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"the designated beneficiary","type":"BENEFICIARY","role":"recipient of death benefit payment","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"$2,500,000","type":"AMOUNT","role":"amount of death benefit payable","relational_anchors":["minus any outstanding loans"]},{"name":"Death certificate of first insured","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"proof required for claim processing","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Death certificate of second insured","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"proof required for claim processing","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Completed claim forms","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"mandatory submission for benefit disbursement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"within 30 days","type":"DATE","role":"timeframe for payment post-document receipt","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"August 20th","type":"DATE","role":"due date for annual premium payment","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"$32,400","type":"AMOUNT","role":"guaranteed annual premium for first 10 years","relational_anchors":["PREMIUM GUARANTEE PERIOD"]},{"name":"$48,600","type":"AMOUNT","role":"maximum allowed annual premium after Year 10","relational_anchors":["after Year 10"]}]},{"name":"Survivorship Benefit Trigger","sentence":"The death benefit is payable only upon the death of the second insured to die.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["survivorship basis","second death payout","death benefit timing"],"entities":[{"name":"joint life insurance policy","type":"POLICY","role":"insures two lives under survivorship clause","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"DEATH BENEFIT TRIGGER","type":"CONCEPT","role":"defines condition for payout eligibility","relational_anchors":["death of the SECOND insured to die"]},{"name":"first insured","type":"PERSON","role":"person who dies first; triggers no payout","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"second insured","type":"PERSON","role":"person whose death triggers final payout","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"we","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"insurance provider making payments","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"the designated beneficiary","type":"BENEFICIARY","role":"recipient of death benefit payment","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"$2,500,000","type":"AMOUNT","role":"amount of death benefit payable","relational_anchors":["minus any outstanding loans"]},{"name":"Death certificate of first insured","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"proof required for claim processing","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Death certificate of second insured","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"proof required for claim processing","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Completed claim forms","type":"DOCUMENT","role":"mandatory submission for benefit disbursement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"within 30 days","type":"DATE","role":"timeframe for payment post-document receipt","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"August 20th","type":"DATE","role":"due date for annual premium payment","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"$32,400","type":"AMOUNT","role":"guaranteed annual premium for first 10 years","relational_anchors":["PREMIUM GUARANTEE PERIOD"]},{"name":"$48,600","type":"AMOUNT","role":"maximum allowed annual premium after Year 10","relational_anchors":["after Year 10"]}]},{"name":"Survivorship Basis Trigger","sentence":"The policy uses a survivorship basis for triggering the death benefit.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["survivorship basis","death benefit trigger","second death payout"],"entities":[{"name":"joint life insurance policy","type":"POLICY","role":"insures two lives under survivorship clause","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"DEATH BENEFIT TRIGGER","type":"CONCEPT","role":"defines condition for payout eligibility","relational_anchors":["death of the SECOND insured to die"]},{"name":"first insured","type":"PERSON","role":"person who dies first; triggers no payout","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"second insured","type":"PERSON","role":"person whose death triggers final payout","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"we","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"insurance provider making payments","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"the designated beneficiary","type":"BENEFICIARY","role":"recipient of death benefit payment","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"$2,500,000","type":"AMOUNT","role":"amount of death benefit payable","relationa