<node id="b2104e17-8341-4347-99c9-7bd45c9f437e">
  <data key="d0">{"name":"Joint Life Insurance Policy Terms","text":" of $48,600 per year.\n\n4.3 Premiums are payable annually on August 20th.\n\n4.4 FIRST DEATH PREMIUM CONTINUATION: Premiums continue after \n    the first death at the same rate.\n\n4.5 WAIVER OPTION: Premium waiver is not available on joint \n    survivorship policies.\n\n4.6 GRACE PERIOD: If payment is not received, you have 60 days \n    to pay before the policy cancels.\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE V - CASH VALUE AND LOANS\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n5.1 This policy accumulates cash value on a guaranteed schedule.\n\n5.2 Projected cash value (based on current assumptions):\n    End of Year 10: $285,000\n    End of Year 20: $712,000\n\n5.3 POLICY LOANS:\n    • Available after policy has been in force for 2 years\n    • Maximum: 90% of cash surrender value\n    • Interest rate: Variable, currently 5.5% per annum\n    • Loans reduce death benefit dollar-for-dollar\n    • Available before or after first death\n\n5.4 WITHDRAWALS: Partial withdrawals are not permitted under \n    this policy type.\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE VI - SPLIT OPTION\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n6.1 Upon the first death, the policy owner may elect to split \n    this policy into two separate single-life policies, one on \n    each insured.\n\n6.2 Requirements for split:\n    • Must elect within 2 years of first death\n    • Each policy's face amount determined by actuarial allocation\n    • Both insureds must be alive at time of first death \n      (available only in rare simultaneous death situations with \n      medical uncertainty)\n    • Evidence of insurability may be required\n\n6.3 This option is rarely exercised and primarily exists for \n    divorce or trust modification situations.\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE VII - EXCLUSIONS\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n7.1 SUICIDE CLAUSE: If either insured commits suicide within \n    2 years of the issue date, the death benefit","summary":"This life insurance policy features annual premiums of $48,600 due on August 20th, continuing at the same rate after the first death. Cash value grows guaranteeedly, projected at $285,000 after 10 years and $712,000 after 20 years, with loans allowed up to 90% of cash surrender value after two years, though they reduce the death benefit. Withdrawals are prohibited, but the policy can be split into two single-life policies within two years of the first death if both individuals survive and evidence of insurability is provided—primarily used in estate planning scenarios like divorce or trust changes. Suicide within two years of issuance voids the death benefit.","topics":["Life Insurance","Premium Payments","Cash Value Accumulation","Policy Splitting"],"facts":[{"name":"Annual Premium Amount","sentence":"The annual premium is $48,600.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["annual premium","payment schedule","policy cost"],"entities":[{"name":"FIRST DEATH PREMIUM CONTINUATION","type":"CONCEPT","role":"premium continuation rule post-first-death","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"WAIVER OPTION","type":"CONCEPT","role":"premium waiver availability condition","relational_anchors":["not available on joint survivorship policies"]},{"name":"August 20th","type":"DATE","role":"annual premium due date","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"GRACE PERIOD","type":"CONCEPT","role":"payment extension period before cancellation","relational_anchors":["60 days"]},{"name":"$48,600 per year","type":"MONETARY_VALUE","role":"annual premium amount","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"CASH VALUE ACCUMULATION","type":"CONCEPT","role":"guaranteed growth mechanism","relational_anchors":["on a guaranteed schedule"]},{"name":"$285,000","type":"MONETARY_VALUE","role":"p