<node id="2bbc528c-e6e5-4ddb-abd6-a424cd92c465">
  <data key="d0">{"name":"SUICIDE CLAUSE","type":"EXCLUSION","role":"death benefit limitation for early suicide","relational_anchors":["within 2 years of the issue date"]}</data>
  <data key="d1">entity</data>
</node>
<node id="88260d12-29af-4348-b3aa-07401be39748">
  <data key="d0">{"name":"Insurance Policy Legal Framework","text":"───\nARTICLE VII - EXCLUSIONS\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n7.1 SUICIDE CLAUSE: If either insured commits suicide within \n    2 years of the issue date, the death benefit is limited to \n    return of premiums paid.\n\n7.2 This suicide clause resets if the policy is reinstated.\n\n7.3 CONTESTABILITY: We may contest this policy for material \n    misrepresentation within 2 years of issue while both insureds \n    are living.\n\n7.4 NO OTHER EXCLUSIONS: No war, aviation, or travel exclusions \n    apply to this policy.\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE VIII - ESTATE TAX PLANNING PROVISIONS\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n8.1 This policy is owned by an irrevocable trust to exclude \n    proceeds from the insureds' taxable estates.\n\n8.2 IMPORTANT TAX NOTE: Proceeds paid to the trust should not be \n    includable in either insured's estate if the trust is properly \n    structured and maintained.\n\n8.3 Consult with estate planning attorney regarding:\n    • Three-year lookback rule if policy transferred to trust\n    • Crummey power requirements\n    • Annual exclusion gift planning\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE IX - SIMULTANEOUS DEATH\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n9.1 If both insureds die in the same accident or incident and it \n    cannot be determined who died first, the death benefit will \n    be paid immediately.\n\n9.2 If deaths occur within 30 days of each other, this will be \n    treated as simultaneous for claim purposes.\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE X - OWNERSHIP AND ASSIGNMENT\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n10.1 The policy owner (the Trust) has all ownership rights \n     including the right to:\n     • Designate and change beneficiaries\n     • Assign the policy\n     • Take policy loans\n     • Surrender the policy\n\n10.2 Neither insured has ownership rights unless specified in \n     the trust document.\n\n10.3 Policy may not be assigned without trustee authorization.\n\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nARTICLE XI - FREE LOOK PERIOD\n────────────────","summary":"This policy includes a two-year suicide clause that limits benefits to returned premiums; the clause resets upon reinstatement. Contestability applies for two years due to material misrepresentation. There are no war, aviation, or travel exclusions. The policy is held in an irrevocable trust to exclude proceeds from taxable estates, contingent on proper structuring—requiring attention to the three-year lookback rule, Crummey powers, and annual gifts. In cases of simultaneous death (within 30 days or indeterminate order), the full benefit pays out immediately. Ownership resides solely with the trust, which controls assignments, designations, loans, and surrenders, with no individual insured having direct ownership rights.","topics":["Life Insurance Exclusions","Estate Planning","Trust Ownership","Death Benefit Provisions"],"facts":[{"name":"Suicide Clause Trigger","sentence":"The suicide clause applies if either insured commits suicide within two years of the issue date.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["suicide clause","two-year period","death benefit limit"],"entities":[{"name":"Suicide Clause","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Exclusion trigger for early death","relational_anchors":["within 2 years of the issue date"]},{"name":"Contestability","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Ground for challenging policy validity","relational_anchors":["within 2 years of issue","while both insureds are living"]},{"name":"Simultaneous Death","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Determines payout timing when joint deaths occur","relational_anchors":["within 30 days of each other","cannot be determined who died first"]},{"name":"Trust","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"Owner of the policy and beneficiary recipient","relational_anchors":["irrevocable trust","properly structured and maintained"]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"Individual covered under the policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Free Look Period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Window for policy review and cancellation","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Return of Premiums Paid","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Maximum payout amount upon suicide","relational_anchors":["if either insured commits suicide within 2 years"]},{"name":"Three-Year Lookback Rule","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Tax compliance requirement after transfer","relational_anchors":["if policy transferred to trust"]},{"name":"Crummey Power Requirements","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Legal condition for gift tax exemption","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Annual Exclusion Gift Planning","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Strategy to minimize estate taxes","relational_anchors":[]}]},{"name":"Suicide Benefit Limitation","sentence":"If the suicide clause applies, the death benefit is limited to the return of premiums paid.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["suicide clause","death benefit limit","premium refund"],"entities":[{"name":"Suicide Clause","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Exclusion trigger for early death","relational_anchors":["within 2 years of the issue date"]},{"name":"Contestability","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Ground for challenging policy validity","relational_anchors":["within 2 years of issue","while both insureds are living"]},{"name":"Simultaneous Death","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Determines payout timing when joint deaths occur","relational_anchors":["within 30 days of each other","cannot be determined who died first"]},{"name":"Trust","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"Owner of the policy and beneficiary recipient","relational_anchors":["irrevocable trust","properly structured and maintained"]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"Individual covered under the policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Free Look Period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Window for policy review and cancellation","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Return of Premiums Paid","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Maximum payout amount upon suicide","relational_anchors":["if either insured commits suicide within 2 years"]},{"name":"Three-Year Lookback Rule","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Tax compliance requirement after transfer","relational_anchors":["if policy transferred to trust"]},{"name":"Crummey Power Requirements","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Legal condition for gift tax exemption","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Annual Exclusion Gift Planning","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Strategy to minimize estate taxes","relational_anchors":[]}]},{"name":"Suicide Clause Reset on Reinstatement","sentence":"The suicide clause resets if the policy is reinstated.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["suicide clause","policy reinstatement","two-year limit"],"entities":[{"name":"Suicide Clause","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Exclusion trigger for early death","relational_anchors":["within 2 years of the issue date"]},{"name":"Contestability","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Ground for challenging policy validity","relational_anchors":["within 2 years of issue","while both insureds are living"]},{"name":"Simultaneous Death","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Determines payout timing when joint deaths occur","relational_anchors":["within 30 days of each other","cannot be determined who died first"]},{"name":"Trust","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"Owner of the policy and beneficiary recipient","relational_anchors":["irrevocable trust","properly structured and maintained"]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"Individual covered under the policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Free Look Period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Window for policy review and cancellation","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Return of Premiums Paid","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Maximum payout amount upon suicide","relational_anchors":["if either insured commits suicide within 2 years"]},{"name":"Three-Year Lookback Rule","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Tax compliance requirement after transfer","relational_anchors":["if policy transferred to trust"]},{"name":"Crummey Power Requirements","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Legal condition for gift tax exemption","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Annual Exclusion Gift Planning","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Strategy to minimize estate taxes","relational_anchors":[]}]},{"name":"Contestability Period","sentence":"This policy may be contested for material misrepresentation within two years of the issue date.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["contestability","material misrepresentation","two-year window"],"entities":[{"name":"Suicide Clause","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Exclusion trigger for early death","relational_anchors":["within 2 years of the issue date"]},{"name":"Contestability","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Ground for challenging policy validity","relational_anchors":["within 2 years of issue","while both insureds are living"]},{"name":"Simultaneous Death","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Determines payout timing when joint deaths occur","relational_anchors":["within 30 days of each other","cannot be determined who died first"]},{"name":"Trust","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"Owner of the policy and beneficiary recipient","relational_anchors":["irrevocable trust","properly structured and maintained"]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"Individual covered under the policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Free Look Period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Window for policy review and cancellation","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Return of Premiums Paid","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Maximum payout amount upon suicide","relational_anchors":["if either insured commits suicide within 2 years"]},{"name":"Three-Year Lookback Rule","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Tax compliance requirement after transfer","relational_anchors":["if policy transferred to trust"]},{"name":"Crummey Power Requirements","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Legal condition for gift tax exemption","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Annual Exclusion Gift Planning","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Strategy to minimize estate taxes","relational_anchors":[]}]},{"name":"Contestability While Both Alive","sentence":"Contestability only applies while both insureds are alive.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["contestability","both insureds alive","policy validity period"],"entities":[{"name":"Suicide Clause","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Exclusion trigger for early death","relational_anchors":["within 2 years of the issue date"]},{"name":"Contestability","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Ground for challenging policy validity","relational_anchors":["within 2 years of issue","while both insureds are living"]},{"name":"Simultaneous Death","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Determines payout timing when joint deaths occur","relational_anchors":["within 30 days of each other","cannot be determined who died first"]},{"name":"Trust","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"Owner of the policy and beneficiary recipient","relational_anchors":["irrevocable trust","properly structured and maintained"]},{"name":"Insured","type":"PERSON","role":"Individual covered under the policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Free Look Period","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Window for policy review and cancellation","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Return of Premiums Paid","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Maximum payout amount upon suicide","relational_anchors":["if either insured commits suicide within 2 years"]},{"name":"Three-Year Lookback Rule","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Tax compliance requirement after transfer","relational_anchors":["if policy transferred to trust"]},{"name":"Crummey Power Requirements","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Legal condition for gift tax exemption","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Annual Exclusion Gift Planning","type":"CONCEPT","role":"Strategy to minimize estate taxes","relational_anchors":[]}]},{"name":"No War Exclusions","sentence":"No war exclusions ap