  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="b88d0ce3-428e-4cb8-adc0-8526b7d088da">
  <data key="d3">The policy being classified as Second-to-Die Whole Life indicates its structure for joint coverage, but this detail stands independently from specific biographical data like William Hartford’s birthdate.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="e514cae1-517d-4147-b68b-73630549696a">
  <data key="d3">The policy being a Second-to-Die Whole Life indicates it covers two individuals; this context makes the identification of William Alexander Hartford as the first insured relevant but not dependent on the policy’s classification.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="05c110b1-28a6-4585-aeeb-e280113a301a">
  <data key="d3">The policy being a Second-to-Die Whole Life type defines its payout condition based on the later death of either spouse. This structural detail does not depend on William’s specific age but informs how longevity impacts benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="4ad78d17-c886-4565-bbc0-103b53d1d1f4">
  <data key="d3">The policy being a Second-to-Die Whole Life type defines its payout conditions based on the later death of either insured party. This structural detail does not affect how individuals like William are categorized in terms of health-based risk classes used for underwriting.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="79983b88-b902-4a9a-8364-943758b77dce">
  <data key="d3">The policy being classified as Second-to-Die Whole Life implies coverage for two individuals, making Elizabeth Anne Hartford’s role as the second insured consistent with the policy's design.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="70b3ef60-9864-48d8-850f-5f71428d1690">
  <data key="d3">The policy being classified as Second-to-Die Whole Life indicates its structure based on joint coverage for two lives, but it does not require or explain Elizabeth’s date of birth.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="15216199-99bf-4a2d-8c0d-b4cc387e52a4">
  <data key="d3">The policy being a Second-to-Die Whole Life type does not relate to Elizabeth Anne Hartford's gender. This detail stands independently within the context of the summary.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="ae12e889-3208-43a4-a6f8-f8e170834ef3">
  <data key="d3">The policy being a Second-to-Die Whole Life defines its payout condition based on the later death of either insured party. This structural detail does not influence or relate directly to Elizabeth’s personal risk class designation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="c5842115-5c9a-48a3-a9d0-06731e7773bf">
  <data key="d3">The policy being a Second-to-Die Whole Life type defines its payout condition based on the later death of either spouse, but does not depend directly on Elizabeth’s specific age.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="eb6fcda1-6a00-45e2-a278-6ecbfce50c86">
  <data key="d3">The policy's second-to-die nature defines its payout condition, but it does not determine who manages the owning trust. This information about the policy type stands independently from details regarding the trustee’s identity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="f0afe120-e789-4e90-bc04-4eea01f53901">
  <data key="d3">The policy being a Second-to-Die Whole Life establishes its purpose and payout conditions, providing context for why the specified annual premium applies.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUALIZES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="958e1286-1e8f-48a3-a9cb-4bd70a403cc3">
  <data key="d3">The policy being classified as Second-to-Die Whole Life pertains to its structure and payout conditions. This characteristic is independent of when the trust governing it was established.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="2c0afdf7-25f1-4c84-88a2-08afcc4de210">
  <data key="d3">The "Second-to-Die" policy structure determines when the death benefit is payable, which complements the role of the trustee-owned policy in facilitating smooth asset transfer without probate.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="2d52cf57-58c0-4a1e-a4dd-d5e01496d174">
  <data key="d3">The policy being classified as Second-to-Die Whole Life explains why the $2.5 million death benefit is payable only after the later of the two insured individuals passes away.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="edb99df4-3b1e-4a19-8c3f-a96551b750c2">
  <data key="d3">The designation of the policy as "Second-to-Die Whole Life" establishes its purpose and payout mechanism, which underpins why a guaranteed level premium over ten years enhances predictability and stability in long-term estate planning.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="d0df87eb-7dd4-43af-b61a-1acb35f2067f">
  <data key="d3">The Second-to-Die Whole Life policy requires ongoing funding to remain active; the Hartford Family Irrevocable Trust ensures continuity by serving as the premium payor, thus maintaining the policy’s validity and alignment with estate planning goals.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUSTAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="2d075601-ee57-47c1-9e7a-50f0b163454b">
  <data key="d3">The "Second-to-Die Whole Life" policy form indicates that coverage applies to two individuals and triggers payment only after the second death, confirming its classification as a joint life insurance policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13">
  <data key="d3">The "Second-to-Die" policy designation specifies that coverage remains active until the second insured individual dies, making it the basis for when the death benefit becomes payable.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="288469c9-a76a-4bf8-b17b-752662f3a1f6">
  <data key="d3">The second-to-die nature of the policy ensures the death benefit is paid only after both insured individuals have passed away, making the choice of an irrevocable trust as beneficiary consistent with its role in estate planning and asset transfer without probate.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">The policy being classified as Second-to-Die Whole Life means it pays benefits only after both insureds have died, confirming its use of a survivorship basis as stated in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies the policy is Second-to-Die Whole Life, directly supporting the condition stated in fact_sentence_2 that the death benefit is paid only after the second insured dies. This reflects the fundamental design of such policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">The policy being Second-to-Die Whole Life means it stays active after the first insured dies, providing ongoing coverage for the surviving spouse, as confirmed by the continuation of premiums and administrative transition noted in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the policy as a second-to-die whole life plan, and fact_sentence_2 specifies that the death benefit is payable only after both insureds have died, confirming the core mechanism described in the initial statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">The policy being a Second-to-Die Whole Life plan inherently supports estate planning goals, as confirmed by the statement that it is designed for such purposes. This alignment underscores the functional rationale behind its structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">The Second-to-Die Whole Life policy provides a substantial death benefit that supports estate tax liquidity needs by generating cash flow when both spouses have died, enabling timely payment of estate taxes without liquidating assets.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 identifies the policy type and its structural features, while fact_sentence_2 provides confirmation that the annual premium of $32,400 is guaranteed for the initial ten-year term—supporting the long-term stability described in the summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">The second-to-die nature of the policy implies that premiums remain payable even after one insured passes, leading to potential increases post-Year 10 when the guaranteed rate expires.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the policy type and core features, while fact_sentence_2 provides critical detail about post-Year 10 premium limits, clarifying the upper bound of ongoing costs beyond the initial guaranteed term.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
