  <data key="d3">The $2.5 million death benefit is specifically designed to be paid when the second insured person dies under a joint life insurance arrangement.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2d52cf57-58c0-4a1e-a4dd-d5e01496d174" target="d0df87eb-7dd4-43af-b61a-1acb35f2067f">
  <data key="d3">The $2.5 million death benefit depends on consistent premium payments being made to keep the policy active; without such funding, the benefit would not be payable at the time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
