  <data key="d3">As a joint life insurance policy covering two individuals, the policy incurs a fixed annual premium of $32,400, consistent with its dual-insured structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIES_COST</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2d075601-ee57-47c1-9e7a-50f0b163454b" target="edb99df4-3b1e-4a19-8c3f-a96551b750c2">
  <data key="d3">Being a joint life policy means coverage extends across two individuals, which contextualizes why the premium is structured over time, though the two facts operate independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2d075601-ee57-47c1-9e7a-50f0b163454b" target="d0df87eb-7dd4-43af-b61a-1acb35f2067f">
  <data key="d3">As a joint life insurance policy, it requires consistent funding through designated payors like the Hartford Family Irrevocable Trust to maintain coverage until the later of the two insureds’ deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">FUNDING_SOURCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2d075601-ee57-47c1-9e7a-50f0b163454b" target="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy insures two lives, it necessitates a payout only when the second insured individual passes away, making the timing of the death benefit contingent on the sequence of deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2d075601-ee57-47c1-9e7a-50f0b163454b" target="288469c9-a76a-4bf8-b17b-752662f3a1f6">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy insures two lives under one contract, designating the Hartford Family Irrevocable Life Insurance Trust as the sole beneficiary ensures that proceeds are distributed according to estate plan intentions without probate.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
