  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 clarifies that the death benefit activates when the second insured passes away, aligning directly with fact_sentence_2, which specifies payment occurs solely after both insureds have died. Together, they emphasize the survivorship nature of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">The trigger for the death benefit occurring at the second death ensures liquidity precisely when it is most critical for estate taxes, making the policy well-suited for its intended financial purpose.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">The condition that the death benefit triggers only after the second insured dies confirms the policy’s design for estate planning, ensuring funds are available when both spouses have passed, thus fulfilling long-term wealth transfer goals.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit being payable only after the second insured dies depends on the policy remaining active through its duration, which is supported by the guaranteed-level premiums over the first 10 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">The condition that the death benefit triggers only after the second insured dies establishes the purpose of the policy, underpinning why ongoing premium payments—potentially increasing after Year 10—are necessary to maintain coverage until both lives end.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit being payable only after the second insured dies depends on the policy remaining active, which requires ongoing premium payments—even after Year 10 when rates may rise to a maximum of $48,600 annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13" target="cfb8aedd-4fff-4a62-9b3c-d67d3494a301">
  <data key="d3">The condition under which the death benefit triggers depends on the trust being correctly structured so the proceeds do not become part of the insureds’ taxable estates.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13" target="a08544cf-1d57-4a48-8d71-04334028f70e">
  <data key="d3">The condition that the death benefit triggers only after the second insured dies relies on the policy being held in an irrevocable trust, which ensures control and tax advantages without individual ownership interference.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13" target="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a">
  <data key="d3">The trigger for the death benefit—the second-to-die condition—is strategically designed to support the goal of excluding proceeds from taxable estates via trust ownership, enabling efficient wealth transfer without estate taxes.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13" target="c9ecaa63-c7f5-4e1a-97c6-6bbc471e2191">
  <data key="d3">The condition that the death benefit triggers only after the second insured dies supports the goal of excluding proceeds from both estates, as it allows the trust to receive funds without triggering inclusion under IRS rules tied to earlier distributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13" target="0a3b7fc9-2243-4755-a015-279702ce91e9">
  <data key="d3">The condition triggering the death benefit depends on proper estate planning structures, including timely annual gifting, to maintain the trust’s validity and avoid adverse tax consequences.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13" target="6855c874-b03e-4cfa-b68c-37e56182aa7f">
  <data key="d3">The timing of the death benefit payment depends on the second insured's passing, which is central to the policy’s purpose. However, placing the policy in a trust triggers the need to comply with the three-year lookback rule, potentially invalidating the transfer if the grantor dies within three years of setting up the trust.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13" target="99362e2f-7a54-4ae7-98a5-155295fe1f90">
  <data key="d3">The condition that the death benefit triggers only after the second insured dies aligns with the estate planning goal served by placing the policy in an irrevocable trust, but achieving that goal requires adherence to specific legal formalities like Crummey powers during transfer.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
