<edge source="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">The statement identifies the policy type as joint life insurance, which inherently implies coverage for multiple individuals. This sets the context for fact_sentence_2, which clarifies that the policy specifically insures two lives.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">A joint life insurance policy is defined by its structure where coverage applies until both insureds pass away. Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that the death benefit is contingent solely on the second death occurring, aligning with the core mechanism of such policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">A joint life insurance policy operates under a survivorship model where coverage continues after one insured passes away, ensuring ongoing protection for the remaining individual.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">A joint life insurance policy is defined by its structure, and using a survivorship basis determines when the death benefit is triggered. This specific feature distinguishes it from other types of joint policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">The statement that this is a joint life insurance policy sets the context for understanding why no death benefit is paid upon the first insured's passing—it aligns with the survivorship design where benefits are contingent on both lives ending.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
