<edge source="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">A joint life insurance policy implies coverage for two individuals, and the specified payout condition—that the death benefit is payable only after both insured persons die—is a direct consequence of this structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
