  <data key="d3">The statement that it is a joint life insurance policy sets the foundational context for why a $2.5 million payout occurs only after the second insured's death. Without this structural definition, the purpose of the delayed claim would not be understandable.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
