  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">The policy's dual-insured structure necessitates formal documentation for each death event, including a death certificate for the first deceased individual, to initiate the claims process.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">The policy covers two individuals, creating a survivorship structure that affects how claims are handled. To initiate a payout under this structure, completed claim forms must be submitted as part of the required process.</data>
  <data key="d4">RELATED_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy pays only after both insureds pass away, confirming the second death through a certified document is necessary to trigger claims processing. Thus, the existence of two insured individuals directly necessitates submitting evidence of the second death.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">The existence of two insured individuals ensures that the policy remains active post-first-death, necessitating continued premium payments despite one individual’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy insures two lives, it naturally allows for continued coverage even after one individual passes away, ensuring the policy stays in effect until both insureds die.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">The policy's coverage of two lives necessitates verification of both deaths before any payment occurs, making timely documentation crucial for triggering the 30-day processing window described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUALIZES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy insures two lives, it operates on a survivorship basis where benefits are contingent on both individuals passing away. This structural design means that when one insured dies, no immediate payment is made because the condition for payout has not yet been met.</data>
  <data key="d4">SURVIVORSHIP IMPLIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy covers two lives, it necessitates tracking individual mortality events. Upon the first death, the insurer issues written confirmation to inform the policyowner of the event, marking a key step in updating the policy’s administrative state.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy covers two lives, it necessitates formal documentation when one dies, including the filing of a death certificate to update the policy's administrative state.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy covers two lives, when one passes away, the remaining insured undergoes a formal reclassification to maintain coverage under a single-life structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">The existence of two insured individuals defines the policy's structure, but does not determine or influence the guarantee of a stable annual premium during the initial ten years.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy covers two lives, it ensures continued coverage even after one dies, allowing the remaining insured to maintain protection under the same terms—hence the premium stays constant post-first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy is structured on a survivorship basis covering two lives, it naturally maintains the same coverage amount even after the first death occurs, ensuring the benefit remains intact until both insureds pass.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">The policy covers two individuals, establishing its survivorship structure. This foundational detail sets the stage for understanding long-term provisions like potential premium adjustments after Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">The policy covers two individuals, establishing its survivorship structure. This foundational detail does not influence the later specification that premiums after Year 10 will not exceed $48,600 annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy covers two lives, it ensures ongoing obligations even after one individual dies. Therefore, premiums remain due post-first-death to maintain the policy’s validity until both insured persons have passed.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501" target="3d46018a-fc19-4870-ba86-8b6a02b20a34">
  <data key="d3">The policy's dual-insured nature defines its purpose, while the annual premium due date ensures consistent funding. These elements operate independently within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
