</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b">
  <data key="d3">The use of a survivorship basis is what characterizes this particular joint life insurance policy, specifying that benefits are payable only after both insureds pass away.</data>
  <data key="d4">IS_DEFINED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">A survivorship basis requires coverage of more than one individual, so the design of the policy inherently depends on having two insured persons.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">A survivorship basis means the policy pays out only after both insured individuals pass away, which directly justifies why the death benefit in fact_sentence_1 is contingent on the second death.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis means that benefits are contingent on both lives ending. Therefore, if one individual passes before the other, no claim is triggered because the condition for payment has not been met.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis ensures the death benefit is not triggered by the first death, allowing the policy to remain active and provide continued coverage for the surviving insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis means the payout depends on both insured individuals passing away. This ensures the death benefit is only released after the second death occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis ensures that the death benefit is deferred until both insureds have died, making it suitable for coordinating large asset transfers in estate planning.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis ensures the death benefit is payable only after both insured persons die, which makes the payout event in fact_sentence_2 contingent on the condition stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_TRIGGER</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis ensures that the death benefit is payable only after both insureds pass, aligning with the need for large liquid assets at the time of dual demise, which is essential for satisfying estate tax obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis determines when the death benefit becomes payable, while outstanding loans affect the final payout amount if benefits are triggered under that condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis means the death benefit is contingent on both insureds passing away. This necessitates submitting proof of both deaths to validate eligibility for the payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis mandates that both insureds must die before any payout occurs, making it essential to verify the second death through official documentation like a death certificate.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis determines when the death benefit becomes payable, requiring official documentation such as completed claim forms to initiate payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis means that benefits are contingent on both lives ending. Therefore, when the first insured passes, the condition for payment has not been met, so no death benefit is issued.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy operates on a survivorship basis, it does not pay out upon the first death but instead maintains coverage for the remaining insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis defines when the death benefit becomes payable, while the 30-day processing window outlines how quickly the insurer acts after documentation is received. Together, they describe key aspects of the claim lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_PROCESSING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis requires confirmation of both deaths, so submitting a death certificate for the first insured is a prerequisite step in gathering required documentation for the final payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy pays out only after both insureds pass away, the continuation of premium payments after the first death ensures the policy remains intact until the second death occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENSURES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis defines that benefits are payable only after both insured persons pass away. This structural rule has no direct impact on whether the policy owner receives written confirmation upon the first death, which is purely an administrative step.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy operates on a survivorship basis, when one insured dies, the remaining individual’s coverage is administratively converted into a single-life whole life policy to reflect the changed risk profile and contractual terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis determines that benefits are payable only after both insureds die. Filing the first death certificate is required as an administrative step toward verifying the sequence of events, though it alone cannot initiate a claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis determines when the death benefit is payable, while the guaranteed premium ensures stable costs during the initial decade regardless of that trigger condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis determines when the death benefit is payable, while the post-Year 10 premium increase affects ongoing costs. These elements operate independently within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis ensures the death benefit is payable only after both insureds pass, meaning the policy's financial obligations persist beyond the first death. As such, the premium remains fixed even after one insured dies, maintaining coverage integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy operates on a survivorship basis, the death benefit remains fully intact even after the first insured passes away, ensuring the promised $2.5 million is still payable upon the second death.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="3d46018a-fc19-4870-ba86-8b6a02b20a34">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis determines when the death benefit is paid, while the annual premium due date is part of the ongoing financial obligation. These elements pertain to different aspects of the policy's design.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis defines when the death benefit is payable, while the premium cap sets an upper limit on costs after Year 10. These elements describe distinct features of the policy without direct interaction.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy operates on a survivorship basis, it does not pay out after the first death. As a result, premiums remain due to keep the policy active until both insured parties pass away.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis specified in fact_sentence_2 defines the payout condition consistent with a Second-to-Die Whole Life policy, explaining why the death benefit triggers only after the latter of the two insured's deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="2d075601-ee57-47c1-9e7a-50f0b163454b">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship basis ensures the policy pays out only when both insured persons have passed, which aligns with the definition of a joint life insurance policy covering two lives.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFIRMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8" target="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies the policy uses a survivorship basis, meaning benefits are paid only after both insureds die—this precisely matches the condition stated in fact_sentence_1 about the second death triggering the payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
