<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy pays out only after both insured individuals die, the absence of a death benefit upon the first death is a direct consequence of being a joint life insurance policy under a survivorship structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">The rule that no death benefit is paid upon the first death arises because the policy is designed to cover two lives jointly, requiring both deaths before any claim can be made.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 confirms that no death benefit is issued upon the first death, reinforcing the necessity described in fact_sentence_1—that the benefit requires both deaths before being payable.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy pays only when both insureds have died, it logically implies that no benefit is issued upon the first death, aligning with the survivorship design principle.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">When the first insured dies, no benefit is issued, allowing the policy to persist for the remaining individual under modified terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">The lack of a payout upon the first death ensures funds remain available for later distribution, supporting long-term estate objectives such as tax-efficient wealth transfer.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a death benefit upon the first death ensures that the policy's primary condition—that both lives must end—is preserved. This restriction directly enables the delayed payout described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a death benefit after the first insured's passing ensures the policy continues until both parties have died. This condition directly enables the eventual payout specified in fact_sentence_2 when the second insured passes.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a death benefit upon the first death underscores the need for definitive proof of both deaths before any claim can proceed. This ensures compliance with the policy's survivorship terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">The policy does not pay out upon the first death, which ensures that the $2.5 million proceeds remain intact until both insured individuals have died. This delayed payout is essential for fulfilling its role in providing liquidity specifically for estate taxes after both lives end.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a payout upon the first death sets the stage for the eventual claim process, during which any existing loans would affect the final death benefit amount. This describes how initial conditions influence later financial outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS PAYMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a payout upon the first death necessitates formal verification through document submission, ensuring accurate recordkeeping and eligibility tracking for the ultimate survivorship claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a payout after the first death necessitates confirmation of the second death through official documentation before any claim can proceed.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a payout upon the first death sets the stage for when the final benefit becomes eligible. This triggers the requirement for documentation, leading to a timely resolution within 30 days if all evidence is submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS PAYMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a payout upon the first death sets the stage for future claim processing, making it essential to submit complete claim forms once both insureds have died. This ensures proper verification before the benefit is disbursed.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">When the first insured dies without triggering a payout, the policy's survival mechanism activates, ensuring ongoing coverage for the remaining individual under adjusted conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that no death benefit is paid if the first insured dies. This idea is reiterated in fact sentence 2 using slightly different wording, confirming consistency in the policy's payout rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">REITERATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">When the first insured dies, no benefit is issued, but the policy persists under new terms. As a result, the surviving individual remains covered, requiring continued premium payments to maintain coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">When the first insured passes away, no payout occurs, but the insurer requires official verification through the submission of the death certificate to update the policy's administrative state.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">When the first insured passes away without triggering a payout, the remaining insured’s coverage undergoes an administrative transformation into a standalone single-life policy, ensuring continued protection under modified terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">When the first insured dies, no death benefit is paid due to the survivorship clause. As part of the administrative process, the policy owner receives written confirmation of this event.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">When the first insured passes away, the policy continues without issuing a death benefit, but the face value of the policy remains intact. This ensures that the full $2.5 million benefit is still available upon the second death.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO PAYOUT → PRESERVES COVERAGE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">When the first insured dies, no death benefit is issued, but the policy continues under modified terms. As a result, the premium stays fixed, reflecting ongoing coverage obligations even though benefits remain deferred until both lives end.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a death benefit upon the first death does not influence the guarantee of the annual premium over the first ten years. These clauses operate independently within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a death benefit upon the first death establishes the core payout mechanism of the survivorship policy. This structural feature operates independently of later changes in premium rates after Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="3d46018a-fc19-4870-ba86-8b6a02b20a34">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a death benefit upon the first insured's passing does not influence the requirement to pay premiums annually on August 20th. Premium payments remain obligatory regardless of claim events.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d">
  <data key="d3">When the first insured passes away, the policy does not trigger a death benefit payment. However, since the policy continues in force until both lives have ended, premiums must still be paid by the surviving insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES AND CONTINUES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">The rule that no death benefit is paid upon the first death ensures the policy functions as a survivorship instrument, maintaining coverage until both lives end. This structural feature supports the longevity of the contract, allowing for stable premium guarantees like those specified after Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="52e1761a-4689-4e00-ba52-9b7c72d1ebfb" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">not activated when first insured dies</data>
</edge>
