  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="91a9088b-c76a-41a0-b4e9-0de95682d7cc">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ORGANIZATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="bbb4fbf8-e3b6-41b5-8f90-f435affad6ad">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">BENEFICIARY</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="2d36a2cc-257f-4dce-8281-d4e317b7a525">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AMOUNT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="a48000a4-fdea-41ff-ab48-1c5f3882209f">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="219af199-3d3f-4f8f-bbf5-2ef8ed5b2f11">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="288b1b40-5d75-4d4b-9b9b-cbc1d491387c">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DOCUMENT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="b75d4048-73a1-4d51-a09c-3e2de261af8d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="6c049bc6-1b50-48b2-927f-56a655f380e1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="3198bf6b-d506-4239-8f5a-39cc9302ef41">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AMOUNT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="0a2eeefc-215d-4cea-85b9-240f067eb9af">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AMOUNT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b">
  <data key="d3">The rule that the death benefit is paid only after both insureds pass away defines the core operational feature of a joint life insurance policy, making it distinct from individual or first-to-die policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEFINED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">Since the death benefit is contingent on both insureds dying, it necessitates that the policy cover two people, making the existence of two lives a prerequisite for this clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes that the benefit requires both deaths, which inherently means it depends on one person dying last—the "second" death described in fact_sentence_1—making the timing logically consistent.</data>
  <data key="d4">EQUIVALENT_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">Because the death benefit requires both insureds to pass away, the policy operates under a survivorship basis to enforce this dual-death requirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">Since the death benefit requires both insureds to pass away, it follows that no claim can be made if only one has died, making fact_sentence_1 a necessary precondition for understanding when benefits apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that both insureds die before any benefit is paid necessitates that the policy remain in effect even after the first death, preserving coverage until the second event.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit be paid only after both insureds die makes this policy suitable for long-term estate planning, ensuring funds are available when needed most.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit be paid only after both insureds pass ensures funds are available precisely when needed for estate settlement, supporting the policy’s role in providing estate tax liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS PURPOSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that both insureds must pass away before any payment occurs sets the stage for the $2.5 million payout upon the second death. This ensures the claim is contingent solely on the completion of the dual-death condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is contingent on both insureds passing away, and any existing policy loans will decrease the total amount distributed when the claim is made.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit proof of both deaths ensures that the condition specified in the first fact—that both insureds must have died—is verified before any payout occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_REQUIREMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">The claim requires confirmation of the first death via a death certificate, which initiates the processing timeline toward fulfilling the ultimate condition that both insureds have died.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a death certificate for the second insured ensures compliance with the condition that both deaths must occur before any benefit is released.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_REQUIREMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is only payable after both insureds pass away, but this payout requires submitting completed claim forms as part of the claims procedure.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states the policy pays only after both insureds die, which directly explains why no benefit is issued upon the first death—a key operational detail emphasized in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that both insureds must pass away triggers the eligibility for the death benefit, which then initiates the claims process. Payment occurs within 30 days after submitting complete documentation, ensuring timely disbursement once the triggering event has occurred.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_PAYMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit is payable only after both insureds pass necessitates that the policy remain active post-first-death, ensuring eligibility for future claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">Since the death benefit is payable only after both insureds pass away, the policy remains active post-first-death, requiring continued premium payments to maintain coverage until the second death occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">The policy pays out only after both insureds pass away, ensuring that benefits are distributed solely under dual-death conditions. Upon the first death, the policyholder receives formal notice, marking a transition in administrative handling without altering the payout criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to file the first death certificate enables the insurer to begin verifying eligibility for the eventual death benefit, aligning with the policy’s survivorship clause that mandates both deaths before payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">After the first death occurs, the policy does not pay out but instead reclassifies the remaining insured into a single-life whole life policy for ongoing coverage. This change reflects an administrative adaptation based on the initial condition that benefits are payable only after both lives end.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy pays only after both insureds pass away, it makes sense that premiums remain fixed post-first-death to maintain coverage until the final claim event.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that both insureds must die for the benefit to be paid implies that the policy retains its original coverage amount even after the first death occurs, ensuring the final payout remains consistent.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that both insureds must pass before the death benefit is paid defines the policy's survival-based nature, while the fixed premium ensures predictable costs during the initial term regardless of claim timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">The rule that the death benefit is payable only after both insureds pass away sets the conditions under which claims occur. This timing has no bearing on the maximum premium amount set to increase after Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for both insureds to pass before payment occurs does not influence when premiums may increase after Year 10. This clause governs claim eligibility independently of future premium adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d">
  <data key="d3">Since the death benefit is contingent on both insureds passing, the policy continues after the first death, requiring ongoing premium payments to maintain coverage until the second death occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="3d46018a-fc19-4870-ba86-8b6a02b20a34">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is contingent on the simultaneous passing of both insured parties, while premiums are required annually regardless of claims. This sentence outlines a key eligibility criterion for payouts that does not influence or depend on the scheduled premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that the death benefit is triggered solely by the second death, which directly supports and contextualizes the nature of the policy mentioned in fact_sentence_1 as a second-to-die arrangement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFIRMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="2d075601-ee57-47c1-9e7a-50f0b163454b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 clarifies that the death benefit is payable only after both insureds die, confirming the second-to-die structure implied by fact_sentence_1's reference to a joint life policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="3f6d4cab-62b6-49d1-b92d-102a4aed9d13">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 reinforces the timing condition stated in fact_sentence_1—that the benefit is not paid until both insureds have died—providing additional clarity about claim processing requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="a08544cf-1d57-4a48-8d71-04334028f70e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit be paid only after both insureds have died complements the use of an irrevocable trust, as the trust ensures the proceeds avoid inclusion in any individual’s taxable estate while maintaining administrative control over distribution timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that both insureds must die before the death benefit is paid ensures that the proceeds are distributed according to the terms of the irrevocable trust, thereby achieving estate exclusion objectives without premature payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="cd2b5513-fe2d-4b70-b48a-c2748515cd09">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes the general rule requiring both deaths before payout, while fact_sentence_2 provides a critical exception when simultaneity prevents determining the order of death, triggering immediate payment instead.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEPTION_TO_RULE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="f8fdda5e-551c-4714-929d-a06d99b71f24">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s survivorship structure ensures the death benefit is payable only after both insureds die, but during this period, the trust retains full control over the policy, including the right to take loans against it.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSISTENT_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="115deb5a-9af7-4024-bf11-8dba457cef0b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that both insureds must die before the death benefit is paid is consistent with the trust holding sole ownership and management rights, ensuring controlled transfer and administration post-death.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf" target="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s ability to surrender the policy means it can terminate coverage before both insureds pass, potentially preventing the death benefit from being paid even if both eventually die. This introduces administrative control over the fulfillment of the payout condition described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0a30ac24-2a1a-44a5-b03d-c8a632852f8b" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has_condition_for_payout</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e017ea8-4992-4625-a9dd-02fce069f1a6" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">depends_on</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a863083e-0942-4645-9d6a-ed5f0717c927" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
