<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b">
  <data key="d3">Estate tax liquidity is achieved through a joint life insurance policy that pays out only after both insured individuals die. This payout mechanism ensures sufficient cash availability without requiring asset liquidation during probate.</data>
  <data key="d4">USED_TO_FUND</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">Estate tax liquidity purposes justify using a policy that covers two lives, ensuring payout occurs only after both insureds pass away.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Estate tax liquidity requires timely access to cash upon the final death, making the second-to-die payment clause essential for fulfilling this purpose effectively.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">Estate tax liquidity requires substantial cash availability shortly after the last insured dies, which makes the survivorship-based payout structure particularly suitable and strategically aligned.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">Estate tax liquidity requires substantial funds to become available precisely after both insured individuals die. Therefore, structuring the policy so that no payment occurs at the first death ensures the death benefit accumulates and is reserved exclusively for post-mortem estate obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">The policy was designed to address estate tax liabilities by guaranteeing a lump sum payout after both insureds die. To fulfill this function, it must remain active even after one insured passes, preserving eligibility for the final payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES FUNCTION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s use for estate tax liquidity justifies its survivorship structure, where benefits are deferred until both lives end, ensuring capital availability at critical moments.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES OBJECTIVE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Estate tax liquidity refers to having sufficient cash on hand to pay inheritance or estate taxes without liquidating assets. Since such liquidity is often required in estate planning, this function directly serves that overarching goal.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">The policy's intent to provide estate tax liquidity is realized through the $2.5 million payout triggered by the death of the second insured, ensuring immediate financial resources are available post-mortem.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s intent to fund estate taxes may be undermined if outstanding loans reduce the available death benefit, affecting its ability to meet liquidity needs.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8">
  <data key="d3">The policy's use for estate tax liquidity provides context for why such a large death benefit is needed, while the requirement to submit proof of both deaths ensures proper validation before disbursement. These elements support different aspects of the policy’s design—one functional, one administrative.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">The policy serves an estate tax liquidity goal, and its timely payout—within 30 days of full documents—is essential to fulfilling that financial need efficiently.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">The policy's intent to provide estate tax liquidity depends on verifying the second death through official documentation like a death certificate, ensuring proper claim validation before disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">The policy serves estate tax liquidity needs, requiring documented claims to fulfill its financial objectives. Submitting completed claim forms ensures that the death benefit can be accessed when needed for estate settlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">The policy's lack of a payout upon the first death ensures that funds remain available for estate tax liabilities only after both insured individuals have died, fulfilling its primary function in estate planning.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">The policy serves an estate planning function by providing funds for taxes when both insureds pass. This requires formal verification of each death, including submission of a death certificate for the first deceased individual.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s role in providing estate tax liquidity depends on it remaining active after the first death, ensuring funds are available when both insureds pass away.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s intent for estate tax liquidity depends on maintaining coverage beyond the first death, requiring continued premium payments to preserve the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">The policy's primary function is to provide funds for estate taxes, but receiving written confirmation after the first death serves merely as an internal administrative update unrelated to that fiscal goal.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">The policy serves estate tax liquidity needs by ensuring funds are available post-death. Filing the first death certificate initiates the claims process required before final payment can be made.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">The policy's purpose in providing estate tax liquidity does not directly influence its administrative reclassification when one insured passes. This shift occurs regardless of the policy’s financial goal.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">The policy's purpose is estate tax liquidity, but this does not influence or depend on whether premiums increase after Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">The policy's intent is to provide liquidity for estate taxes, but this does not influence or relate to the maximum premium amount set after Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s design to provide estate tax liquidity relies on stable financial commitments, such as maintaining a consistent premium after the first death, ensuring funds remain available when needed most.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s fixed $2.5 million coverage after the first death ensures sufficient funds are available to meet estate tax liabilities, fulfilling its primary purpose. This stability directly enables effective estate planning despite the delayed payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s use for estate tax liquidity underscores its long-term planning function, which aligns with the importance of stable premiums during initial decades. This context makes the guaranteed premium more meaningful in sustaining the policy’s intended purpose.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="3d46018a-fc19-4870-ba86-8b6a02b20a34">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 explains the primary financial intent behind the policy: providing funds to cover estate taxes. Fact sentence 2 specifies when premiums are due each year. There is no direct connection between the policy's purpose and the date of premium payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s intent to provide estate tax liquidity depends on maintaining coverage until both insured individuals pass away, requiring sustained premium payments even after the first death to preserve the payout mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="dc5e7101-a50d-4b25-8d7d-9d2fc8fab9fc">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s estate tax liquidity purpose is reinforced by restrictions on assignment, ensuring it remains under controlled trust management until distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s estate tax liquidity purpose relies on clear ownership rules established by the trust, ensuring funds are available when needed. Without defined ownership in the trust, the policy may fail to fulfill its intended financial role.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c" target="0e404f06-62de-4907-9ecb-1ee9ca03ea3f">
  <data key="d3">A Second-to-Die Whole Life policy is specifically designed to provide estate tax liquidity, making it an ideal instrument for long-term estate planning goals such as those outlined in the trust-based ownership structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
