<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">The $2.5 million death benefit is payable only after the second insured's passing, but requires documented claims procedures to initiate disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is triggered by the second insured's passing, and once complete documentation is submitted, the insurer processes the claim promptly within 30 days.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is contingent on both insureds passing, so maintaining premium payments after the first death preserves the policy's validity and enables future claim settlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">The $2.5 million payout upon the second death depends on the prior event where no benefit was issued after the first death, ensuring the policy remains active until both insureds pass.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">The policy remains active after the first death, ensuring that the conditions for the $2.5M payout upon the second death are preserved. This continuity allows the insurer to process claims once both insureds have died.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is triggered solely by the passing of the second insured, independent of any notifications sent after the first death. This event occurs later in the timeline and requires distinct documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">The $2.5 million payout occurs only after both insureds die, requiring verification that the first death has occurred before proceeding toward final claim resolution.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">The payment of the death benefit occurs only after both insureds pass away, and prior to that point, if one survives, the policy's administration shifts so the remaining individual is treated under a single-life framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">After the first insured dies, the policy continues with the same $2.5 million coverage, ensuring eligibility for the death benefit when the second insured passes. This consistency maintains the policy’s intended purpose.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENSURES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is triggered solely by the passing of the second insured individual, independent of any changes in premium rates that occur later in the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is triggered solely by the passing of the second insured individual, independent of the premium schedule. This outcome does not rely on whether premiums remain level during the initial ten years.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">After the first insured dies, the policy continues without changing its premium rate, maintaining financial commitment even though the death benefit has not yet been triggered. This ensures the policy remains intact until the second death occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">The payment of the death benefit upon the second insured's passing does not influence or relate to the maximum premium amount that may apply post-Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d">
  <data key="d3">The $2.5 million death benefit is contingent on the second insured's passing, but the policy stays active afterward due to continued premium payments, ensuring eligibility for the payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="3d46018a-fc19-4870-ba86-8b6a02b20a34">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes when the death benefit is triggered—the second death—and who receives it. Fact sentence 2 states the recurring obligation to pay premiums annually on a fixed date, unrelated to claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c">
  <data key="d3">The payout condition depends on the identity and authority of the policy's owner, which is governed by the trust document referenced in fact_sentence_2. Without clear ownership rules, administering the $2.5M benefit could face delays or disputes.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="dc5e7101-a50d-4b25-8d7d-9d2fc8fab9fc">
  <data key="d3">The payout rule in fact_sentence_1 depends on the survival of both insured parties, while fact_sentence_2 restricts assignment of the policy unless authorized by a trustee, adding an administrative layer that could affect future claims handling.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">The ability to take policy loans after two years complements the long-term nature of the survivorship policy, enabling liquidity during its extended term before the final payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit specified in fact_sentence_1 may be reduced by any outstanding policy loans, meaning the $2.5 million payout depends on whether loans have been drawn against the policy's cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">The first fact outlines the default payout mechanism contingent on both deaths, while the second fact provides an alternative path where the policy can be converted post-first-death, altering its future obligations and benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">ALTERNATIVE_PATH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit trigger depends solely on both insureds passing, while the cash value projection reflects internal fund growth over time. Although the cash value increases annually, it has no direct impact on when or whether the $2.5M payout is made.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit clause ensures payout only after both insured persons die, aligning with the long-term nature implied by the projected $712,000 cash value at year 20, suggesting sustained policy performance and funding capacity.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit clause in fact_sentence_1 specifies when the payout occurs under the policy, while fact_sentence_2 highlights that the policy also builds guaranteed cash value over time, enhancing its overall financial profile despite the delayed claim timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit trigger in fact_sentence_1 depends on sustained policy performance over time, which aligns with the accumulation of cash value referenced in fact_sentence_2. Loan provisions do not affect the final payout unless outstanding balances reduce it.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to elect splitting within two years of the first death creates a time-sensitive opportunity to alter the survivorship structure described in fact_sentence_1, potentially allowing beneficiaries to access benefits earlier under new terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">The trigger for the $2.5M payout (both deaths) sets the stage for possible policy splitting after the first death, which depends on providing evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">The survival-based payout rule in fact_sentence_1 sets the stage for the split option, which allows converting the joint policy into individual policies after the first death—a key provision enabling estate adjustments such as those during divorce or trust restructuring.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
