<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b">
  <data key="d3">While the policy being joint life defines its overall framework, the reduction of the death benefit due to outstanding loans applies regardless of the policy type—this detail depends more on terms than structural classification.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans diminish the death benefit, so knowing that two lives are insured helps clarify why such reductions matter when calculating what beneficiaries receive post-mortem.</data>
  <data key="d4">FINANCIAL_IMPLICATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans decrease the total death benefit available, meaning even if the second death has occurred (a prerequisite for payout), the actual amount received may be reduced by prior debt obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES AMOUNT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the death benefit, which is only paid out after both insureds pass, per the survivorship basis.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans impact the size of the death benefit, even though no benefit is paid until both insureds pass away—a condition established by the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES AMOUNT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the eventual death benefit, even though the policy stays active and provides continued coverage for the surviving insured after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the death benefit, which is itself only paid out after both insured individuals have died.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans that reduce the death benefit affect the effectiveness of the policy in achieving its intended estate planning goals by lowering the total inheritance transferred.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">A reduction in the death benefit due to unpaid loans could compromise the policy’s primary function of providing estate tax liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">PURPOSE_DEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans directly impact the final death benefit, so they modify the $2.5 million payout promised when both insureds pass away.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans decrease the total death benefit available, regardless of whether claims are initiated. Proof of both deaths is required before any claim processing begins, irrespective of loan balances.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">The presence of outstanding loans reduces the total death benefit but does not impact the requirement to submit a death certificate for the first insured individual.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans decrease the total death benefit available, but this does not impact the requirement to submit completed claim forms for processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">The presence of unpaid loans reduces the total death benefit available, but this does not impact the 30-day timeframe for processing claims once documents are received.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">The presence of outstanding loans reduces the total death benefit payable, but this adjustment does not impact the requirement to submit a death certificate for the second insured. Both elements pertain to claim fulfillment but operate independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">The presence of outstanding loans reduces the eventual death benefit but does not influence when benefits are paid. This statement stands independently from the rule about no payout upon the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">Loan balances impact the ultimate death benefit amount but do not influence the continuation of premium payments after the first death. This statement stands independently from the timing or requirement of future premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the ultimate death benefit, which becomes relevant only after both insureds pass, including after the policy has continued past the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTS_FINAL_PAYOUT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans decrease the final payout but do not influence the administrative shift in policy status when one insured passes away.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">Loan balances influence the final death benefit but do not alter the stated coverage amount after the first death. This means the face value remains intact until both deaths occur, regardless of any loan activity.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans diminish the eventual death benefit amount payable after both insureds pass, regardless of notifications about the first death. This reduction occurs at claim settlement, independent of administrative confirmations received earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the total death benefit payable when both insureds pass away, independent of document submissions. Filing the first death certificate initiates the claims process but does not directly impact loan deductions from the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans decrease the total payout at death but do not influence the premium guarantees during the first decade.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the eventual death benefit but do not influence whether premiums stay fixed after the first death. This statement stands independently from the premium continuity claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 explains how existing loans diminish the final payout amount. This does not affect the timing or magnitude of premium increases described in fact sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 explains how existing loans impact the final payout amount. This information does not relate to the premium cap established in fact sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans diminish the eventual death benefit when both insured persons pass away. This financial adjustment occurs independently of ongoing premium payments required after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="3d46018a-fc19-4870-ba86-8b6a02b20a34">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes how existing loans diminish the final death benefit amount. Fact sentence 2 outlines the fixed date when annual premiums must be paid. These elements operate independently within the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">The presence of guaranteed cash value allows for policy loans, which directly impact the death benefit by reducing it when outstanding.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">The projected cash value increase supports the possibility of taking loans, which would subsequently reduce the death benefit as stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans, permitted after two years, diminish the death benefit payable under the policy. Since loans are not available before year two, no reduction occurs prior to that point.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans, capped at 90% of the cash surrender value, directly diminish the death benefit payable under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that loans diminish the death benefit, which is further clarified by fact_sentence_2 stating the reduction happens on a one-to-one basis, strengthening the understanding of financial implications.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans reduce the death benefit, and since the projected cash value at year 20 ($712,000) determines the maximum allowable loan amount (up to 90%), it indirectly sets the upper limit on how much the death benefit could be diminished.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans diminish the death benefit regardless of policy splits, while the ability to split the policy after the first death offers an alternative structural path that may influence future loan usage and benefit distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans diminish the final death benefit, which becomes relevant when considering whether splitting the policy is viable under the two-year window, especially since reduced benefits may affect eligibility or desirability of such a move.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans diminish the final death benefit, which impacts the financial viability of splitting the policy later, especially since such splits depend on maintaining sufficient coverage and meeting eligibility criteria including evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans diminish the death benefit, which becomes relevant when the policy is split post-first death, potentially affecting asset allocation in divorce or trust restructuring.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
