<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b">
  <data key="d3">The necessity to submit proof of both deaths arises specifically because the policy is structured as a joint life insurance product, where payouts occur only after both insured parties have died.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">The necessity to submit proof of both deaths stems from the policy being designed for two insured individuals, ensuring benefits are released only when both have deceased.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Submitting proof of both deaths enables the processing of the claim, which is permissible only when both insured parties have deceased, aligning with the payout condition stated earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_PAYOUT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy pays only when both individuals have died, verifying both deaths through documented proof is essential before any claim can proceed under the survivorship terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">Submitting proof of both deaths is required precisely because the policy pays only when both insured individuals have died, so the initial death alone triggers no benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED FOR PAYMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">To trigger the payout, proof of both deaths is required, which necessitates that the policy remain active after the first death—a condition ensured by the policy’s survivorship design.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">Submitting proof of both deaths is necessary because the death benefit is contingent solely on the simultaneous passing of both insured individuals, as defined by the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_PAYOUT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Requiring proof of both deaths enables the policy to fulfill its primary role in estate planning by preventing premature or incorrect payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">Submitting proof of both deaths is necessary to trigger the claim process, which ultimately serves the policy’s primary goal of providing estate tax liquidity when both insureds pass away.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS_PURPOSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">Submitting proof of both deaths initiates the claim process, leading to the eventual disbursement of the $2.5 million death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">To begin the claim process, proof of both deaths must be submitted. This step occurs prior to determining the net benefit, including reductions due to any outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">The claim process requires evidence of both deaths, and submitting the first insured's death certificate fulfills part of that necessary documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">Proof of both deaths provides the factual foundation needed to support the claim forms. Without verified mortality events, the forms cannot be considered valid or actionable by the insurer.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">The need to submit proof of both deaths includes providing the death certificate of the second insured, making this document essential for initiating the claim process described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit proof of both deaths triggers the start of the claims process, leading directly into the timeframe for finalizing the payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">The need to submit proof of both deaths ensures that the insurer verifies the completion of the survival period required by the policy's terms, which explicitly state no payment occurs until both insured parties have died.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">Claim initiation requires evidence of both deaths, ensuring the policy's survival-based structure is honored. This condition supports the continued premium obligations even after one insured has died.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">Claim initiation requires documented proof of both deaths, but receiving notice of the first death does not affect this requirement—it merely informs the policyholder about a milestone in the process.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit proof of both deaths follows logically from the policy's design where benefits are payable only after both insureds die. This ensures that payouts occur only under the correct conditions, even though the policy survives the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">POSTCONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 requires proof of both deaths to start the claims process, and fact_sentence_2 specifies that the death certificate of the first insured is one such required document.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">Submitting proof of both deaths initiates the claims process, while the transition of the surviving insured into a single-life policy reflects an administrative adjustment made after the first death, independent of claim documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">The need to submit proof of both deaths initiates the claim process but does not influence future premium increases. Premiums may rise after Year 10 regardless of claim activity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">Claim initiation requires evidence of both deaths due to the survivorship nature of the policy, where benefits are contingent on the simultaneous demise of both insureds. Since the coverage amount stays fixed even after the first death, maintaining accurate records and ensuring proper documentation becomes essential for final settlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">Proof of both deaths is required to begin the claim process, ensuring benefits are only released after both insureds pass. This condition operates independently of whether premiums increase or stay fixed after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">Claim initiation requires documented evidence of both insureds’ deaths, ensuring proper verification before payment. This step occurs independently of the premium schedule, which governs cost over time regardless of claims activity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">The need to submit proof of both deaths initiates the claims procedure but does not affect premium levels. Premiums remain capped at $48,600 annually after Year 10 regardless of claim submissions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8" target="3d46018a-fc19-4870-ba86-8b6a02b20a34">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit proof of both deaths initiates the claims process but does not influence or depend on the annual premium due date of August 20th.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
