  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the first insured is part of the claims process, but this administrative step is independent of identifying the policy as a joint life insurance product.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the first insured supports the ongoing validity tracking required by the joint survivorship policy design.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Since the death benefit is only paid after both insureds have died, proving the first death through official documentation like a death certificate is foundational to validating the sequence of events leading to eligibility for the claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy pays only after both insureds die, verifying the first death via a death certificate supports the overall process needed to confirm dual mortality under the survivorship clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the first insured enables proper administrative transition and confirms the event that triggers ongoing policy maintenance without immediate benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the first insured is essential to verify the event and allow the policy to remain in effect for the surviving insured, ensuring continued coverage under updated administrative conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the first insured is a prerequisite step required to verify one half of the dual-death condition mandated by the policy’s payout rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the first insured supports the administrative process that aligns with the policy’s intended use in estate planning.</data>
  <data key="d4">USED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the first insured is necessary to initiate claim processing under the survivorship policy. This supports the broader goal of ensuring sufficient liquidity for estate obligations like taxes.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSARY_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the first insured supports the verification process essential for triggering the eventual $2.5 million payout after the second death.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the first insured is necessary for initiating claims processing, regardless of any existing policy loans that may later reduce the payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the first insured's death certificate is essential because it contributes directly to satisfying the overall requirement of proving both deaths for a claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit the first insured's death certificate supports the validation process that leads to confirming eligibility for the final payout. It serves as foundational evidence needed before proceeding to verify the second death.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a death certificate for the first insured provides critical evidence that triggers the need for formal claim initiation. This document supports the validity of the event leading to potential benefits under the survivorship policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">The submission of the first insured's death certificate triggers the administrative transition allowing the policy to remain in force despite one insured passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the first insured confirms the event triggering administrative changes, though it does not activate any payment due to the survivorship nature of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">The submission of the first insured's death certificate initiates the claims process by fulfilling an essential component of the required documentation. This action sets the stage for the insurer to begin evaluating the claim and ultimately issue payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the first insured initiates administrative updates, including transitioning the policy’s status while maintaining ongoing premium payments due to the survivorship structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate initiates the formal verification process for the first death, which may lead to administrative actions such as notifying the policy owner. This step supports transparency but is independent of whether confirmation is issued.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the first insured's death certificate initiates the administrative reclassification of the surviving insured into a single-life policy. This step ensures proper policy status update post-first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that the death certificate of the first insured must be submitted, which directly corresponds to the action described in fact sentence 2 where it must be filed with the insurer. Both convey the same essential step in claim processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">EQUIVALENT TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the first insured’s death certificate activates administrative updates while maintaining the original premium level under the guaranteed term.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate is required to initiate the claims process but does not influence or relate to the guaranteed premium amount during the first decade.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the first insured activates administrative updates, yet the policy's financial terms remain intact, preserving the original $2.5 million benefit until both insureds pass.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="3d46018a-fc19-4870-ba86-8b6a02b20a34">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a death certificate for the first insured relates to claims initiation but does not influence or relate to the scheduled date for annual premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the first insured is part of the claim process required before any payout occurs. This step does not influence or depend on the premium rate that may apply after Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the first insured is required during the claims process when both insureds have died. This step does not influence or affect the premium rate changes that occur after Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9" target="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the first insured verifies the occurrence of the initial death event, enabling the transition to an updated policy state where premiums remain due despite no immediate claim payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
