<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a death certificate for the second insured logically follows from the nature of a joint survivorship policy, where payment depends on the sequential occurrence of both deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a death certificate for the second insured implies that the policy involves more than one individual, reinforcing the foundational condition that two lives are covered under the agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the second insured enables confirmation of the qualifying event—the passing of the last surviving individual—which activates the payment clause outlined in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the second insured is a procedural necessity to validate the fulfillment of the survivorship condition outlined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the second insured confirms the final eligibility criterion required for triggering the death benefit under the survivorship clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the second insured is required to trigger the payout process, which depends on the policy remaining active post-first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the second insured's death certificate is necessary because the death benefit is contingent on both insureds having deceased, as specified in the primary claim rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_PAYOUT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the second insured enables the fulfillment of the policy’s estate planning goal by confirming eligibility for the lump-sum death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the second insured enables the fulfillment of the policy’s primary function—to deliver funds for estate tax liquidity once both insured parties have died.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the second insured is essential to confirm the triggering event that enables the $2.5 million payout under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the second insured is necessary to initiate the claim process, regardless of whether any loans exist against the policy. Loan balances influence the final payout amount but do not alter the need for documentary evidence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the death certificate of the second insured is a specific action required to meet the overall condition of proving both deaths, which is mandated before any claim can proceed.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSARY_PART</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the second insured's death certificate completes the necessary documentation set, enabling confirmation that both conditions for payment have been met, thereby allowing claims processing to proceed.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit the second insured's death certificate enables the processing of the claim, which directly leads to the timely disbursement of the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a death certificate for the second insured enables proper validation of eligibility, which supports the processing of completed claim forms. Without verified proof of the second death, claim forms would lack essential substantiation.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSARY_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">The need to submit a death certificate for the second insured arises because the policy pays out only after both insureds have died, meaning confirmation of the second death is essential before any claim can proceed.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">The need to submit a death certificate for the second insured arises because the policy does not pay out until both insureds have died, requiring confirmation of the final death before any benefits are released.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_REQUIREMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a death certificate for the second insured follows the initial event where the first insured has already died, making it part of the later stage needed to trigger the final payout under the survivorship clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">POSTCEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">Proof of the second insured’s death is essential to finalize the claim process, ensuring the policy’s survival condition is met. This confirmation allows the continued enforcement of premium obligations during the interim period.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a death certificate for the second insured enables the processing of the final payout and initiates the administrative change in policy status. Without verified proof of the second death, the policy cannot proceed to reclassification.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that the second death must be verified through a death certificate before any claim proceeds. This requirement depends on prior confirmation of the first death, making it contingent on the completion of earlier administrative steps involving the initial deceased individual.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">The need to submit a death certificate for the second insured is justified by the policy’s design to preserve the full $2.5 million benefit until both lives have ended, ensuring accurate claim validation against unaltered coverage terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">Submitting a death certificate for the second insured is required to initiate a claim, but this requirement does not affect or rely on the premium being guaranteed during the initial decade.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">Proof of the second insured’s death via a death certificate is required to trigger the payout condition, ensuring the policy’s survival-based structure is met. This requirement aligns with the continuation of fixed premiums even after the first death, maintaining financial stability during the waiting period.</data>
  <data key="d4">NEEDS_VERIFICATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a death certificate for the second insured pertains to claims validation, whereas the potential premium increase after Year 10 relates to long-term cost adjustments. These elements operate independently within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a death certificate for the second insured is part of the claims process but does not influence or relate to the premium rate limits established after Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d">
  <data key="d3">The need to submit a death certificate for the second insured depends on the policy remaining active post-first-death, which is sustained by continued premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593" target="3d46018a-fc19-4870-ba86-8b6a02b20a34">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to submit a death certificate for the second insured pertains solely to initiating a claim under the survivorship policy. This obligation has no connection to the scheduled annual premium payments due on August 20th.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
