<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is required when filing a claim under any life insurance policy, including this joint survivorship policy. This action is independent of whether the policy is jointly held or structured on a survivorship basis.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is necessary to trigger the claims process, which applies specifically to policies covering two lives where benefits are payable only after both deaths occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms enables the insurer to verify the fulfillment of the condition—that both insureds have died—and proceed with payout accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_PAYOUT_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is necessary to activate the payout mechanism governed by the survivorship clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is a prerequisite for claiming the death benefit after both insureds pass, even though such a claim cannot be made until both deaths are confirmed, consistent with the policy’s survivorship terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is required when initiating a payout process after both insureds have died. This step occurs after the policy has already transitioned into its final phase post-first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is required before the death benefit can be issued, which occurs exclusively after both insured individuals have died.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREREQUISITE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is necessary to initiate the payout process, which aligns with the policy’s primary purpose of facilitating estate planning through delayed benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms enables the payout process necessary to achieve the policy’s primary goal of providing estate tax liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is essential to trigger the $2.5 million payout upon the second insured's death.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is necessary to trigger the claims process, regardless of whether any loans exist against the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is the procedural step that formally triggers the claims process once proof of both deaths has been gathered and validated.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">Completing claim forms serves as the procedural mechanism through which the verified death of the first insured—and eventually the second—is formally documented and processed by the insurer, ensuring compliance with administrative requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms provides the formal mechanism through which the death certificate for the second insured is formally reviewed and accepted by the insurer during the claims adjudication process.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_PROCESSING_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms initiates the claims process, enabling the insurer to begin evaluating eligibility and scheduling payment. Without this step, the subsequent timing for payout cannot commence.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is required before any payout can be processed, which occurs only after both insureds have died. This step follows the administrative transition described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">Claim forms must be submitted once both deaths have occurred, making them relevant after the first death has taken place. This step ensures that the insurer can verify eligibility based on dual mortality evidence.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">Completing the claim forms is a prerequisite for initiating the claims process, and providing the death certificate of the first insured is an essential supporting document required during this phase.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">Claim form completion is necessary to initiate the benefits process, which occurs after both insureds pass. This step follows the continuation of premium payments despite the first death, reflecting ongoing policy administration.</data>
  <data key="d4">POSTCONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is required to initiate the payout process after both insured individuals have died. This step comes well after the initial confirmation of the first death but is part of the broader claims procedure.</data>
  <data key="d4">POSTPONED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms initiates the payout process after both insureds pass. This action occurs independently of whether premiums remain stable after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is required to initiate the payout process after both insureds pass away. This step occurs independently of any change in the coverage amount, which remains fixed even after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSARY_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is part of the process required to trigger payout eligibility, but it does not influence or rely on the fixed premium amount during the first decade.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms initiates the formal claims process required after both insureds pass away. After the first death, the surviving insured’s policy status changes to a single-life whole life policy for administrative continuity.</data>
  <data key="d4">POST-DEATH PROCESSING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is part of the process required when both insureds have died, but it does not influence or affect any potential premium increase after Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">Submitting completed claim forms is a prerequisite for initiating a payout but does not influence or depend on the premium rate that applies after Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="3d46018a-fc19-4870-ba86-8b6a02b20a34">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes a requirement for initiating a claim, specifically that completed forms must be submitted. This step is unrelated to the timing of premium payments outlined in fact sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146" target="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d">
  <data key="d3">Claim forms must be submitted to initiate the payout process after both insured persons pass away. This requirement operates independently of whether premiums continue being paid after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
