</edge>
<edge source="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to process payments within 30 days of complete documentation implies a system designed to handle cases involving multiple insureds, consistent with the dual-life nature established by fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Once both deaths are confirmed and documented, the insurer has 30 days to process the claim, fulfilling the obligation established by fact_sentence_1 that the benefit is only payable after the second death occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that payments occur within 30 days relies on the existence of a defined trigger—the dual death event established by the survivorship basis. Without this trigger, the 30-day rule would not apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">The promise of a 30-day payout window assumes that both deaths have been confirmed, meaning it applies specifically after the first death has already occurred without triggering any immediate benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON_FIRST_DEATH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is payable within 30 days of submitting full documentation. This timeline applies only after the policy has remained active through the first death, ensuring continued coverage for the surviving insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">Once both insured individuals have died, the claim becomes eligible for processing. The insurer commits to issuing payment within 30 days of receiving fully documented evidence of both deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS_PROCESSING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">The prompt payment of the death benefit within 30 days supports efficient execution of the policy’s intended use in estate planning, enabling swift distribution of assets without delay.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">Timely claim settlement within 30 days supports the policy’s primary use case: providing immediate liquidity for estate taxes.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">The 30-day processing window applies specifically after the second insured has died and the required documents are fully submitted, ensuring timely disbursement of the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
