  <data key="d3">Once the death certificate from the first insured is included in the complete documentation package, it triggers the timeline during which the insurer processes the claim and makes the death benefit payment within 30 days.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">The promise of payment within 30 days depends on having fully documented evidence, including the death certificate of the second insured, making it contingent on its submission.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">The promise of payment within 30 days hinges entirely on having fully completed documentation, meaning that timely submission is essential to trigger the defined response window.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that no death benefit is paid upon the first death sets the stage for when the subsequent claims process begins, ensuring that payments occur only after both insured parties pass.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
