<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b">
  <data key="d3">Since no death benefit is paid upon the first death, this behavior confirms the policy's classification as a survivorship joint life insurance plan, where payouts occur only after both insured parties have died.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">The reason no death benefit is paid upon the first death is because the policy requires both insured individuals to pass away before any claim can be settled, reflecting its fundamental structure as a joint survivorship policy covering two lives.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL ON TWO DEATHS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies that no death benefit is paid upon the first death, which directly supports and contextualizes fact_sentence_1's claim that benefits are reserved exclusively for the event of the second death.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy pays only after both insureds pass, the absence of a payout upon the first death is a direct result of its survivorship design.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPLIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 reiterates that no death benefit is paid upon the first death, aligning directly with the statement made in fact sentence 1, reinforcing the same conditional outcome under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REITERATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">Because no death benefit is payable upon the first death, the policy persists for the surviving insured, ensuring continued coverage under modified administrative terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTINUES_COVERAGE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">Since the death benefit requires both insureds to pass away, it follows that if only one has died, the condition for payout is not met, making fact_sentence_2 a direct implication of fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy pays out only after both insured persons die, the lack of a payout at the first death directly enables its use in estate planning by maintaining financial control over asset transfer timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy is designed for estate tax liquidity, it intentionally delays the death benefit until both insured persons have passed, avoiding premature disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">No death benefit is paid when the first insured dies, which ensures the policy continues toward eventual payout upon the second death, fulfilling its survivorship purpose.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">No death benefit is paid when the first insured passes away, regardless of any existing loans. Loan balances may later reduce the final payout but do not alter the initial non-payment condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8">
  <data key="d3">Since no death benefit is paid when the first insured passes, it logically follows that claims cannot begin until both deaths are confirmed, requiring formal documentation before processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a death benefit upon the first insured's passing necessitates formal documentation like a death certificate to verify the occurrence and update policy status accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">Since no benefit is paid upon the first death, it becomes necessary to wait for the second death and provide official verification through a death certificate to trigger the payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a payout upon the first death necessitates continued administrative tracking and eventual claim filing, ensuring that the final benefit is issued only after both parties have died.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">Since no benefit is paid at the time of the first death, it directly justifies why the processing window described in sentence 1 applies only after both deaths are confirmed.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">The lack of a death benefit payment after the first insured’s death ensures the policy stays active, allowing coverage to persist until both insureds pass away.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">Upon the first insured's death, no payout occurs due to the survivorship clause, but the policy remains in force, requiring continued premium payments from the surviving insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">Upon the first insured's death, no payout occurs, but the insurer issues written confirmation to acknowledge the event and initiate post-first-death procedures.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a payout upon the first death leads to the reclassification of the surviving insured into a single-life policy for administrative continuity.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">After the first insured passes, the absence of a death benefit payment ensures the policy maintains its full coverage amount, preserving the intended payout condition for when both insureds die.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">Upon the first insured's death, no payout occurs under the policy terms. To initiate the transition from a joint survivorship policy to an ongoing administrative state, the insurer requires official verification via the deceased’s death certificate.</data>
  <data key="d4">ADMINISTERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">After the first insured passes, no death benefit is issued, but the policy continues with the same premium amount due to its guaranteed terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_PAYOUT → CONTINUES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a death benefit upon the first insured's passing does not affect the fixed premium rate for the initial ten years. This ensures predictable costs regardless of when or if claims occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a death benefit upon the first death defines the core feature of a survivorship policy. This structural detail has no bearing on whether premiums increase after Year 10, which relates solely to long-term pricing terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="3d46018a-fc19-4870-ba86-8b6a02b20a34">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a death benefit upon the first insured's passing has no bearing on when premiums are required to be paid each year.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d">
  <data key="d3">Upon the first insured person’s death, no death benefit is issued, but the policy continues in force, requiring ongoing premium payments from the surviving insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 explains that the death benefit is not triggered by the first death, maintaining the policy's survivorship nature. Fact sentence 2 states the upper limit of future premiums beyond the initial ten years, independent of claim conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="cd2b5513-fe2d-4b70-b48a-c2748515cd09">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes that the death benefit is deferred until both insureds pass, but fact_sentence_2 provides an exception: if both die simultaneously, payment occurs immediately despite the survivorship structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEPTION_TO_RULE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="a08544cf-1d57-4a48-8d71-04334028f70e">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a death benefit upon the first insured's passing is unaffected by the policy being held in an irrevocable trust, but the trust ownership enables estate exclusion strategies without impacting payout rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="f8fdda5e-551c-4714-929d-a06d99b71f24">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a death benefit upon the first insured's passing does not prevent the trust from exercising its right to take policy loans, as the policy remains active and under trust control post-first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY_PERMITTED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship payout feature ensures that the death benefit is deferred until both insureds pass, enabling the irrevocable trust to hold the policy without triggering immediate taxation, thereby achieving estate tax avoidance.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_TAX_EXCLUSION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a death benefit upon the first insured's passing does not affect the trust’s legal right to terminate the policy via surrender, as ownership lies exclusively with the trust regardless of payout timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066" target="115deb5a-9af7-4024-bf11-8dba457cef0b">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a death benefit upon the first insured's passing is governed by the policy’s structure, but the trust retains full authority to assign the policy despite this restriction. This ensures continuity of ownership even when claims are deferred.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="24bfd692-e3cf-442c-83ad-5b63b014a174" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">governs</data>
</edge>
