<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b">
  <data key="d3">The fact that the policy continues in force after the first death supports the characterization of it as a joint life insurance policy under a survivorship arrangement.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">The policy continuing in force after the first death implies that it was originally designed to cover two lives, establishing the foundational condition for such administrative continuity.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">The policy continuing in force after the first death allows time for the second death to occur, making it possible to meet the condition required for the death benefit payment specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">The continued validity of the policy after the first death is directly enabled by its survivorship structure, ensuring benefits are only triggered when both insureds pass.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">The policy continuing in force after the first death is a direct result of the rule that no benefit is paid until both insureds pass away.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 asserts that the policy persists after the first death, which aligns with and reinforces the claim made in fact_sentence_1 regarding continued coverage for the surviving insured.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy stays in effect after the first death, it maintains its ability to pay the death benefit once the second insured dies, fulfilling the primary purpose of the contract.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">The policy continuing after the first death allows it to serve its primary purpose—providing a lump sum for estate settlement once both insured individuals have passed, making it suitable for estate planning.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">Continuing the policy after the first death enables it to fulfill its primary purpose of generating liquidity for estate taxes upon the second death.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy stays in effect after the first death, it maintains eligibility for the final death benefit when the second insured passes away, making the initial event necessary for triggering the later outcome.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">The policy's continuation after the first death ensures that claims—including those affected by existing loans—are still eligible when both insureds have died.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_EVENTUAL_CLAIM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8">
  <data key="d3">Even though the policy continues after the first death, it cannot pay out until both deaths are verified through documented proof, meaning the continuation of coverage enables but does not trigger immediate payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">The policy continuing in force after the first death depends on formal verification through the submission of the first insured's death certificate.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy stays active after the first death, it enables the processing of claims once the second death occurs, ensuring eligibility for the payout based on documented evidence.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_CLAIM_PROCESSING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">The policy continuing in force after the first death enables the process leading to eventual claim filing, making the ongoing policy status a prerequisite for later claim submissions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">The policy continuing after the first death enables future claim processing, allowing the 30-day deadline for benefits to apply once documentation is submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">Because no benefit is paid upon the first death, the policy continues in force rather than terminating prematurely.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">Following the first death, the policy stays in effect, necessitating continued premium payments despite the absence of an immediate payout. The survival of one insured does not terminate coverage or financial responsibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">After the first insured's death, the policy stays active, and the insurer issues written confirmation to the policy owner acknowledging this change in status.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">After the first insured dies, the policy stays active, requiring formal verification through the submission of the death certificate to ensure accurate administrative tracking and compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">The policy's continued validity after the first death allows for an administrative transition of the surviving insured into a single-life whole life policy. This ensures ongoing coverage under updated terms while maintaining the original policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">Following the first death, the policy remains active, ensuring continuity of coverage. As a result, the premium amount stays fixed despite the change in insured status.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">After the first insured dies, the policy remains active, ensuring that the original $2.5 million death benefit is preserved until both insureds pass away. This continuity maintains the financial commitment without reduction.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTINUES TO SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
