  <data key="d3">The policy stays active after the first death, necessitating ongoing premium payments to maintain coverage until the second death occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">After the first insured dies, the policy stays in effect due to continued premium obligations. The $32,400 annual premium is locked in for the first decade, ensuring financial predictability during this phase.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">The policy remains active after the first death, ensuring coverage continuity. This ongoing status allows for potential premium increases after Year 10 based on policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">The policy stays active after the first death, ensuring coverage persists for the second insured. This ongoing validity allows the long-term premium ceiling established after Year 10 to remain relevant.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTINUES TO APPLY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="3d46018a-fc19-4870-ba86-8b6a02b20a34">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that the policy remains active after the first death, ensuring continued coverage until both insured parties pass. This persistence allows for future claims but does not affect when premiums are due.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="a08544cf-1d57-4a48-8d71-04334028f70e">
  <data key="d3">The policy continuing after the first death supports the rationale for holding it in an irrevocable trust, ensuring the death benefit avoids inclusion in taxable estates while maintaining compliance with trust governance rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4" target="cd2b5513-fe2d-4b70-b48a-c2748515cd09">
  <data key="d3">The continuation of the policy post-first-death ensures administrative continuity, enabling the eventual payout if both insureds die simultaneously—a scenario explicitly covered by the second fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
