  <data key="d3">Since the policy persists beyond the first death, it inherently implies that the initial classification as a joint life insurance policy necessitates ongoing premium responsibilities.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">Continued premium obligations after the first death are contingent upon the initial arrangement of covering two lives under a survivorship policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Continued premium obligations after the first death support the structural integrity of the survivorship policy, enabling the eventual payout when the second insured passes away, thus fulfilling the condition stated in the primary fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to keep paying premiums after the first death supports the survivorship basis by maintaining coverage validity until both lives end.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">Continued premium obligations after the first death ensure the policy stays active, enabling eventual payout upon the second death—thus justifying why no benefit is paid initially.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy remains in effect after the first death, the surviving insured must keep making premium payments to maintain coverage, reflecting an ongoing financial commitment tied to sustained policy validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">Continued premium obligations after the first death ensure the policy stays in force so that the $2.5 million benefit can eventually be paid when both insureds have deceased, fulfilling the core purpose of the survivorship clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Continued premium obligations ensure that the policy remains intact for estate planning, allowing the final death benefit to be distributed according to prearranged intentions.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
