  <data key="d3">Continued premium obligations ensure the policy survives the first death, enabling it to meet its primary function of providing estate tax liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">Continued premium obligations ensure the policy stays in force beyond the first death, allowing the $2.5M benefit to be payable when the second insured dies.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">Premiums remain due even after one insured passes, ensuring policy continuity, regardless of any loan balance that may later reduce the payout. The obligation to pay premiums exists separately from loan-related deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8">
  <data key="d3">Premium payments persist after the first death, maintaining the policy’s validity so that the required proof of both deaths can eventually trigger the final payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">Continued premium payments after the first insured’s death reflect the policy’s survival-based design, necessitating formal verification via a death certificate before finalizing any adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
