  <data key="d3">Continued premium payments after the first death maintain the policy’s validity, enabling the eventual processing of claims once the second death is verified through official documentation such as a death certificate.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">Premiums remain due after the first death, maintaining the policy's validity until both lives end. This ongoing obligation supports the eventual need to submit claim forms when both deaths are confirmed.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">Continued premium payments ensure the policy stays in force, allowing the insurer to process the final death benefit claim within 30 days once both deaths are verified.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">Continued premium payments after the first death reflect the ongoing validity of the policy, which inherently means no death benefit is triggered until both insured parties pass.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONSEQUENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">Continued premium payments are required because the policy remains active after the first death, ensuring the contract's validity until both insured parties pass away.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">After the first insured passes, the policyholder must still pay premiums to maintain coverage. This continued obligation occurs independently of whether formal confirmation has been received about the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">After the first insured dies, the policyholder must submit the death certificate to formally update the policy status, enabling the continuation of premium payments under the new administrative framework.</data>
