  <data key="d3">After the first insured dies, the policyholder must still pay premiums, but the amount does not change from its original level during the initial guarantee period.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTINUES WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that the obligation to pay premiums persists after the first death. This is directly reflected in fact sentence 2, which confirms that premiums continue to be payable under the same condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">REINFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">After the first insured dies, the surviving individual remains obligated to pay premiums, which are guaranteed at $32,400 annually for the next ten years under the original terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">The continuation of premium payments after the first death ensures policy continuity, while the possible increase after Year 10 reflects long-term cost adjustments under the same policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">POSTPONED_IMPLICATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
