<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b">
  <data key="d3">Receiving written confirmation after the first death implies some administrative process tied to the policy's continuation, yet this specific detail is absent from the original summary despite being relevant to policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">The receipt of written confirmation after the first death implies that the policy involves more than one insured individual, reinforcing the foundational condition stated in fact_sentence_1—that the policy insures two lives.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Receiving written confirmation after the first death initiates procedural updates, but since benefits are contingent only on the second death, this step has no impact on the final payout criteria defined by the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">Receiving written confirmation after the first death reflects procedural handling by the insurer but does not alter the fundamental requirement that both deaths must occur before any benefit is triggered under the survivorship clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">Upon receiving written confirmation about the first death, it confirms that the initial condition of the survivorship policy has been triggered, meaning no death benefit was payable.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">Upon the first insured’s death, the policy owner receives official written confirmation, signaling the change in policy status from joint survivorship to a transitional phase where the surviving insured remains covered under modified terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">IS_CONFIRMED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">Upon the first insured's death, the policyowner is notified via written confirmation, signaling a shift in policy administration. This event occurs independently of the final payout, which still requires both deaths before any benefit is issued.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Receiving written confirmation upon the first death supports ongoing recordkeeping relevant to estate planning, though it does not define or alter the primary purpose of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">ADMINISTRATIVE_SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">Receiving written confirmation upon the first death is a routine step in managing the policy transition, though it has no bearing on the underlying purpose of providing estate tax liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">Notification of the first insured's death serves an administrative purpose but has no impact on whether the final death benefit will eventually be paid upon the second death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">Receiving written confirmation upon the first insured's death serves as an administrative milestone that updates the policy status but does not influence how loans impact the final death benefit calculation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8">
  <data key="d3">Receiving written confirmation of the first death provides awareness of the policy's progression toward eventual settlement, though it has no bearing on the formal claim requirements involving dual-death verification.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">Receiving written confirmation that the first insured has died informs the policy owner of the change in status, potentially prompting them to prepare necessary documents like a death certificate for future claim processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">POSTPONES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">Upon the first insured’s death, the policy owner is notified, setting off the timeline during which the second death must eventually be documented to activate the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">Receiving written confirmation of the first insured's death serves as an administrative milestone, informing the policyholder that one stage has been reached, although formal claim processing begins only after both deaths are confirmed.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">Upon the first insured's death, the policyowner receives written confirmation, which serves an informational purpose separate from the claims process that triggers the final payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">The issuance of written confirmation upon the first death depends on the occurrence of that death, serving as formal notice of the policy’s transition phase.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">Upon receiving written confirmation from the insurer about the first death, the policy owner learns that the policy continues in force under modified terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">Upon the first insured’s death, the policyowner receives official notification confirming the event. This step happens regardless of future premium payment responsibilities but marks a key administrative milestone.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">Upon the first insured's death, the policyholder receives formal notice, initiating administrative changes that result in the surviving individual being treated under a single-life policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">Upon the first insured's death, the policyholder receives official written confirmation, which typically requires prior filing of the death certificate with the insurer to validate the claim initiation.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">Upon the first insured person’s death, the policyholder receives official notice, confirming the change in status. Despite this event, the policy retains its original $2.5 million coverage amount until both insureds pass.</data>
  <data key="d4">HAS_CONSEQUENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">Receipt of written confirmation about the first death does not influence or relate to the guaranteed premium rate during the initial decade. This event is administrative rather than financial.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">Upon the first insured’s death, the policy owner is notified via written confirmation, ensuring awareness of the transition. Afterward, the premium continues unchanged, maintaining the original guaranteed rate despite the change in policy status.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">Receiving written confirmation of the first death does not influence or relate to the timing or amount of any future premium increases beyond Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">The receipt of written confirmation after the first death does not affect the maximum premium rate that may apply after Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83" target="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d">
  <data key="d3">Upon the first insured person’s death, the policy owner is formally notified via written confirmation, initiating the transition phase where the policy continues without payout but requires continued premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
