  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="0a5720bc-d64e-4990-8f4f-eabea88b6428">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AMOUNT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="d929e395-5808-4cad-b896-85a89eedd982">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AMOUNT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b">
  <data key="d3">Knowing that the first death’s certificate must be submitted supports understanding how the joint nature of the policy triggers procedural steps post-first demise.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">Filing the death certificate of the first insured requires that the policy cover more than one person, making the multi-lives nature of the policy foundational to this step.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Filing the first insured’s death certificate provides foundational evidence needed to validate the occurrence of the first death, which is essential for determining whether the second death has now triggered the payout condition specified in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">Filing the first death certificate is a prerequisite document needed during claims processing, consistent with the policy's requirement that both deaths be confirmed before any benefit is issued under the survivorship clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the death certificate of the first insured is required to formally acknowledge the event, enabling the policy to remain active under modified terms despite no immediate benefit payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the death certificate of the first insured is essential because it triggers the administrative update allowing the policy to remain in effect for the surviving insured, ensuring uninterrupted coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">Filing the first death certificate is a prerequisite step in confirming the sequence of events leading to the dual-death condition needed for the payout described in the primary fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Filing the first death certificate is a required action during claim processing, independent of whether the policy was created for estate planning.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">Filing the first death certificate is a procedural prerequisite needed to begin processing the claim, which ultimately fulfills the policy’s purpose of providing estate tax liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRELIMINARY_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">Filing the first insured’s death certificate initiates the process needed to eventually confirm eligibility for the death benefit upon the second death.</data>
  <data key="d4">PREPARES_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the first death certificate triggers the start of the claims procedure, which later includes evaluating any existing loans that would reduce the final payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8">
  <data key="d3">The filing of the first insured’s death certificate is essential to meet the overall requirement in fact_sentence_1, which mandates proof of both deaths before any claim processing begins.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSARY_PART</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 specifies that the death certificate of the first insured must be filed with the insurer, which aligns precisely with the requirement stated in fact sentence 1 to submit the document. This reflects a consistent administrative procedure.</data>
  <data key="d4">EQUIVALENT TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 mandates filing the death certificate of the first insured, which serves as an essential prerequisite for initiating the claims process. Without this document, the verification of the first death cannot occur, thereby blocking progress toward submitting evidence for the second death.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the death certificate of the first insured enables proper validation and supports the completeness of the claim forms being submitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the first death certificate enables the insurer to begin processing the claim, triggering the 30-day deadline specified in fact_sentence_1 for finalizing the death benefit payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the death certificate of the first insured enables the insurer to update the policyholder status and begin tracking eligibility for future payouts contingent on the second death. This action ensures compliance with claims procedures despite no immediate benefit being issued.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">Filing the death certificate of the first insured enables the insurer to update records and uphold the ongoing validity of the policy beyond the initial death.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the death certificate of the first insured is required before the policy enters its post-first-death phase, during which premium payments remain obligatory.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">The death certificate of the first insured must be filed with the insurer before any formal acknowledgment or written confirmation can be issued to the policyholder regarding the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the death certificate initiates the administrative transition that converts the survivorship policy into a single-life policy for the remaining insured individual.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">Filing the first insured’s death certificate is required for administrative tracking, though it has no impact on premium adjustments. Premium stability is governed by the contract term, independent of individual death events.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the death certificate of the first insured initiates the claim process, ensuring accurate recordkeeping while preserving the policy's original terms. This administrative act supports continuity without altering the payout conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">HAS_NO_EFFECT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the first death certificate initiates the claims process but does not affect premium guarantees. This step is independent of the duration-based premium stability described in the second sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the first insured's death certificate initiates the claims process but does not affect premium adjustments. Premium increases after Year 10 occur independently based on policy terms, regardless of claim submissions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the first insured's death certificate initiates the claims process but does not affect premium rates. This step is independent of long-term premium adjustments beyond Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="3d46018a-fc19-4870-ba86-8b6a02b20a34">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the first death certificate initiates the claims process but does not affect the timing of premium payments, which remain fixed by calendar date regardless of mortality events.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962" target="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d">
  <data key="d3">Submitting the death certificate of the first insured confirms the occurrence of the initial death event, triggering administrative updates while ensuring that premium obligations remain active pending the second death.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29fe092-4fe1-47c8-badd-51016498616e" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">death_certificate_required</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8d09e760-2d5b-4bff-bd98-606539cb6c78" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">Must be filed with insurer</data>
</edge>
