  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AMOUNT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="0e843f97-728e-4410-995b-d3c4f455aa32">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">AMOUNT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy operates on a survivorship basis, the change in the surviving insured’s status to a single-life policy arises directly from the original designation of the contract as a joint life insurance policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULTS_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">The administrative shift to a single-life policy occurs because the original policy was designed for two lives, requiring structural adjustment after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Because the death benefit is contingent on both lives ending, the surviving insured’s change to a single-life policy ensures ongoing coverage under new terms once the original dual-insured arrangement ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">The administrative conversion of the surviving insured into a single-life policy arises directly from the survivorship basis that defines how the death benefit is triggered under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">The shift to a single-life policy occurs specifically because the initial condition—no death benefit being paid after the first death—is met, making it a direct consequence of that event.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESULT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy remains in force post-first death, the surviving insured undergoes an administrative shift to become a single-life policyholder.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">Because the death benefit requires both insureds to pass away, the system allows the surviving insured to remain covered under a modified policy type, ensuring continuity even though payout eligibility has not yet been met.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">The administrative conversion of the surviving insured into a single-life policy ensures the policy continues serving its original estate planning purpose by preserving financial security through sustained coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">The administrative conversion to a single-life policy reflects internal structuring but does not determine or affect the policy’s original intent for estate tax liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">After the first death, the surviving insured’s policy is reclassified into a single-life whole life policy, setting the stage for eventual claim eligibility when the second death occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">After the first death, the policy's administrative status changes to a single-life policy, independent of any existing loans that may later reduce the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8">
  <data key="d3">The surviving insured automatically assumes a single-life policy status after the first death, which sets the stage for when proof of both deaths may later be required to finalize the payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">The surviving insured becoming a single-life policy necessitates confirmation via the first insured's death certificate, making document submission a prerequisite for this administrative shift.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">Once the surviving insured's status changes to a single-life policy, it confirms that the second death has been officially recognized and documented, necessitating the submission of the relevant death certificate.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
