  <data key="d3">After the first death, the surviving insured’s policy is administratively converted into a single-life whole life policy. This structural update may influence future actions such as claiming benefits, including the need to submit claim forms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ADMINISTRATIVE CONSEQUENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">The administrative shift to a single-life policy has no bearing on how quickly the death benefit is paid once documents are received. It pertains strictly to policy status changes rather than payout mechanics.</data>
