<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of a premium increase after Year 10 implies an ongoing commitment beyond the initial guarantee period, consistent with the nature of a multi-lifetime joint policy rather than a standard individual term plan.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">Premiums remain fixed for ten years but may rise afterward, reflecting an evolving cost assumption that applies regardless of the number of insured lives covered under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">TIME_DEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Premiums remain fixed for ten years but may rise afterward. This potential increase has no bearing on whether the death benefit is paid solely upon the second death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="43d8caa1-4fa2-4bcc-9598-cb51dcf031e8">
  <data key="d3">While the premium may rise after Year 10, this change does not affect how or when the death benefit is triggered under the survivorship clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">Premium rate adjustments after Year 10 reflect long-term cost projections and do not affect when or if the death benefit is triggered by the first death event.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="e3ba5ff9-a204-4af4-850d-38d792f8f557">
  <data key="d3">Premiums may rise after Year 10, reflecting long-term cost considerations even though the policy remains active post-first death. This timing does not affect the survival-based continuation of coverage described earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">TEMPORAL_CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">An increase in premiums after Year 10 has no bearing on the condition that both insureds must die for the benefit to be paid. Premium changes occur regardless of claim triggers.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Premiums may rise after Year 10 due to changing risk factors, though this change is independent of the policy’s primary role in estate planning.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">Premiums may increase after Year 10, regardless of the policy being used for estate tax liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">A potential premium increase after Year 10 does not affect when or whether the death benefit is paid upon the second death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 indicates that premiums could rise after Year 10, but this change has no bearing on whether loans reduce the death benefit, as outlined in fact sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="00523b0d-56f9-449b-a7f2-e7f02fe9d7d8">
  <data key="d3">Premium increases after Year 10 do not affect the requirement to provide proof of both deaths when filing a claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="8bb98441-7fce-4a4a-aaed-255a79d72dc9">
  <data key="d3">The premium may increase after Year 10 based on policy terms, independent of any requirement to submit a death certificate for the first insured. This administrative adjustment has no bearing on the document submission needed for claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="58074012-c329-4400-8d8b-4167293c8593">
  <data key="d3">Premiums may rise after Year 10 based on policy terms, but this does not affect the necessity of providing a death certificate for the second insured when filing a claim. The timing of premium changes has no bearing on document submission requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="b139e470-7b32-4675-85c3-cec60a1f5146">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of a premium increase after Year 10 has no bearing on the need to submit completed claim forms during the claims process.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="539e1a9d-20b3-4a9d-906a-7f04bb12c255">
  <data key="d3">Premium increases after Year 10 occur regardless of when claims are settled. The timing of payments has no bearing on the rate adjustment clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">Premium increases after Year 10 reflect changes in policy costs beyond the initial guarantee period. These adjustments do not affect when or if a death benefit is paid, which depends exclusively on both insureds’ passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">Premiums may rise after Year 10 due to long-term cost projections, regardless of whether one or both insured persons remain alive, reflecting an independent financial provision from post-first-death conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="b917e56c-f863-4041-b852-b34740f1b439">
  <data key="d3">A potential premium hike after Year 10 occurs independently but affects the financial commitment already established by continuing payments even after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">TEMPORAL_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="25f4e64b-7adb-4f44-892f-2d9bd49fdc83">
  <data key="d3">A premium increase after Year 10 has no impact on whether the policy owner receives written confirmation upon the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="a9ec20a6-7d7d-487c-a092-216f40615962">
  <data key="d3">Premiums increasing after Year 10 do not influence the need to file the first death's death certificate. Claim requirements remain unchanged by future rate hikes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="a4c41a3b-9c7f-4b98-a6b4-986121ed83de">
  <data key="d3">Premium increases after Year 10 reflect long-term cost adjustments that apply regardless of the policy’s administrative shift post-first death, though such changes affect the ongoing obligation of the now-single-life policyholder.</data>
  <data key="d4">POSTERIOR_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="fe6ae23c-acf1-4ce0-b10a-d43f8f1cd48e">
  <data key="d3">Premiums may rise after Year 10 regardless of whether the coverage amount has changed due to prior deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">Although the premium remains constant after the first death, it could eventually rise after the tenth year, meaning the initial stability does not extend indefinitely into the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON_TIME</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">Following the end of the 10-year guaranteed period, the premium is no longer fixed and may rise, implying that the earlier stability was temporary and subject to future changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3c7d76f-bcfb-4c2d-988d-e3fa8983ae3e" target="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of increased premiums after Year 10 relies on the continued obligation to pay premiums beyond the first death, ensuring the policy's longevity and financial viability over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
