  <data key="d3">The second sentence sets an upper limit on future premiums, ensuring they do not surpass $48,600 annually after Year 10. This financial ceiling operates independently of the requirement that both insureds must die before any benefit is issued, as stated in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
