  <data key="d3">The premium ceiling ensures predictable costs beyond Year 10, enabling the Trust to assess whether continuing coverage outweighs expenses when deciding to surrender the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f" target="f8fdda5e-551c-4714-929d-a06d99b71f24">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s premium ceiling does not affect the Trust’s ability to access funds via policy loans, as loan rights stem from ownership rather than pricing terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f" target="cd2b5513-fe2d-4b70-b48a-c2748515cd09">
  <data key="d3">The premium ceiling established in fact_sentence_1 ensures long-term affordability regardless of payout timing, including scenarios where simultaneous death triggers immediate payment as described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f" target="115deb5a-9af7-4024-bf11-8dba457cef0b">
  <data key="d3">The premium ceiling established in Year 11 does not restrict the Trust’s ability to assign the policy, but the assignment could impact who bears future premium responsibilities. This reflects ongoing governance flexibility despite fixed cost parameters.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
