<edge source="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d" target="ac80f582-a994-43e3-a0c9-7da66f0fc96b">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy is structured to pay out only after both insured persons die, it necessitates ongoing premium payments even after the first death, maintaining coverage for the remaining individual.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d" target="f7b2d174-40c9-40e2-a0f1-fafef35a9501">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for continued premium payments after the first death arises because the policy is designed to cover two lives, meaning the financial commitment persists until both insured individuals have died.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">Continued payment of premiums after the first death supports the policy's purpose of ensuring the death benefit is available when the second insured passes, aligning with the conditional payout rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
