  <data key="d3">Continuing to pay premiums after the first death ensures the survival-based policy remains intact, allowing the death benefit to be triggered only when both insured individuals have died.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b9253ffc-7436-4d11-a036-5b41d8c8e66d" target="45022529-c9d1-42d4-978a-0e7ff593425f">
  <data key="d3">Although no death benefit is issued upon the first death, the continuation of premium payments reflects the policy’s survival beyond that event, maintaining coverage until the second death occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
