  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="d75850ff-57f1-4d33-b71f-2aff9432dff6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">The annual premium of $48,600 must be paid by August 20th each year, establishing the required deadline for fulfillment of the financial commitment.</data>
  <data key="d4">PAYMENT_DEADLINE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">The $48,600 annual premium sets the baseline cost, which continues unchanged after the first death, ensuring predictable financial commitment throughout the policy's duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">The $48,600 annual premium establishes the financial obligation that triggers the 60-day grace period if unpaid. This grace period serves as a buffer allowing delayed payment without immediate cancellation.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">The $48,600 annual premium provides the necessary funding that enables the policy’s guaranteed cash value accumulation over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">The high annual premium of $48,600 reflects the cost of coverage under a joint survivorship policy, where such policies typically do not offer premium waivers upon disability or other events, making financial obligations rigid even during hardship.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">The annual premium of $48,600 contributes to the policy's cash value buildup, enabling the projected growth to $285,000 after ten years through guaranteed compounding mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">The consistent payment of the $48,600 annual premium ensures the policy remains active over time, enabling it to satisfy the minimum duration requirement necessary for loan access after two years.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">The $48,600 annual premium ensures steady funding of the policy, enabling the guaranteed growth of its cash value over time, including the projected $712,000 by year 20 under current assumptions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">The $48,600 annual premium supports the buildup of cash value over time, enabling future eligibility for policy loans based on that accumulated value.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">The annual premium of $48,600 establishes the cost of maintaining coverage, while the loan interest rate of 5.5% applies only when borrowing against the accumulated cash value. The premium does not influence or determine the loan's interest rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">The $48,600 annual premium establishes the baseline cost of maintaining coverage, which enables access to policy features such as loans. These loans, once taken, directly diminish the death benefit, linking the initial financial obligation to future reductions in payout capacity.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">The $48,600 annual premium ensures continued policy coverage and contributes to the growth of cash value, enabling future access to policy loans. Loan availability hinges on sufficient cash accumulation, which results from sustained premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">The annual premium of $48,600 establishes the recurring financial commitment required from the policyholder. This payment requirement operates independently of the restriction against partial withdrawals, which limits access to accumulated cash value regardless of premium payments made.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">The consistent $48,600 annual premium maintains the policy’s validity, enabling the continuation of benefits including the potential to split the policy after the first death, assuming other criteria are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">The fixed annual premium ensures continued coverage necessary for maintaining eligibility to exercise the split option after the first death. Without consistent payment, the policy could lapse before the split window opens.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">The annual premium of $48,600 ensures continued coverage necessary for the policy to remain active long enough to allow splitting into two single-life policies. This structural requirement enables the subsequent actuarial distribution of face amounts upon division.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">The annual premium of $48,600 establishes the cost of maintaining coverage but has no bearing on the availability of the split option during rare simultaneous death scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">The consistent annual premium of $48,600 ensures ongoing coverage necessary to maintain eligibility for later options such as policy splitting. Evidence of insurability becomes relevant only if one seeks to split the policy under specified conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">The annual premium of $48,600 establishes the ongoing financial commitment for the policy, while the requirement that both individuals remain alive at the time of the first death determines eligibility for converting the joint policy into two separate ones. These elements operate independently within different aspects of policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">The high annual premium reflects the policy’s comprehensive benefits and flexibility, including the split option designed for complex legal transitions like divorce or trust modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">The high annual premium of $48,600 establishes the policy’s significant ongoing cost, but this figure has no direct bearing on whether the split option is utilized. The low usage of the split option reflects behavioral or situational factors unrelated to premium levels.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">The annual premium of $48,600 sets the financial obligation for maintaining coverage, whereas the suicide clause specifies that if an insured dies by suicide within two years of issuance, the death benefit may be forfeited. These are independent policy provisions addressing different aspects of risk and cost.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="884e87fe-743e-4185-9ec7-342eab307b3e" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">annual premium amount</data>
</edge>
