</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d3">Payments of $48,600 are due annually on August 20th, specifying the schedule tied to the stated premium amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">PAYMENT_AMOUNT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for annual premiums on August 20th sets the baseline payment condition, ensuring consistent funding. After the first death, this fixed payment continues without change, maintaining financial stability despite the loss of one insured individual.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for annual premium payments on August 20th does not imply anything about the availability of premium waivers. This statement stands independently regarding payment scheduling without referencing exceptions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that premiums be paid annually on August 20th sets the timeline for potential delinquency, triggering the 60-day grace period if payments are not made by that date.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments on August 20th provide the financial foundation that allows the policy’s cash value to grow according to its guaranteed schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments on August 20th fund the policy’s growth mechanism, contributing to the guaranteed increase in cash value over time, including the projected $285,000 by year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRIBUTES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments begin upon policy issuance and continue each year on August 20th; after two full years have passed since initiation, borrowers gain access to policy loans based on accumulated cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">Annual premiums paid on August 20th provide the ongoing funding that supports the accumulation of cash value over time, contributing to its projection at $712,000 by year 20.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments on August 20th ensure ongoing coverage, enabling the accumulation of cash value that underpins the policy’s loan capacity. This accumulated value determines the basis for calculating the maximum allowable loan.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that premiums are paid annually on August 20th, establishing a recurring financial obligation. Fact sentence 2 describes the current variable interest rate applicable to policy loans, which is unrelated to the premium payment schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments ensure ongoing coverage, enabling access to policy features such as loans. When loans are taken, they directly decrease the available death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments ensure continued coverage necessary for the policy’s survival past the first death, enabling eligibility for the split option under specified conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for annual premium payments on August 20th establishes a recurring financial obligation, reinforcing why partial withdrawals are restricted—to maintain policy integrity and ensure consistent funding toward cash value growth.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments on August 20th ensure ongoing coverage, enabling continued access to policy benefits such as loans even after the first death. Loan availability relies on accumulated cash value rather than payment dates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments on August 20th maintain policy validity, enabling future options like splitting upon the first death. This ongoing obligation supports the conditions under which later decisions—such as electing to split—are viable.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments ensure sustained funding of the policy, enabling its continued operation and supporting future actions like splitting it. This financial stability allows for an actuarial determination of each new policy's face amount upon division.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">The annual premium due date has no bearing on the conditions governing the policy’s split option, which is restricted to rare instances such as uncertain cause of simultaneous deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">Annual premiums due on August 20th establish the financial obligation tied to the policy, but this does not influence the low frequency of exercising the split option.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">The annual premium obligation sets the financial commitment period, creating a timeframe during which the conditions for policy modification—including the split option—may become relevant. This context helps frame when the survivorship clause applies.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">Annual premium payments ensure ongoing coverage necessary for the policy’s long-term viability, enabling the availability of the split option when triggered by major life events like divorce or trust changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">The annual premium obligation establishes ongoing financial commitment, ensuring continued coverage necessary before any future actions like policy splitting can occur. This structural stability supports eligibility requirements later in the policy’s term.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for annual premium payments by August 20th sets the ongoing financial obligation tied to maintaining coverage, which remains relevant even when other clauses—like the suicide exclusion—are triggered.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5dca668b-6681-4daa-ba69-54dc74f669d1" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">due_date</data>
</edge>
