  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="ee52efc2-a58a-4b88-8470-99970539e1b3">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d3">Continuity of the $48,600 annual premium after the first death relies on the initially established premium rate being maintained without change.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">Even after the first death, the original annual premium schedule persists, meaning the payment obligation established by the August 20th deadline remains intact regardless of mortality events.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTINUES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">The continued payment of premiums after the first death implies an unwaivable obligation, consistent with the absence of premium waiver benefits in joint survivorship policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">The continuation of fixed premiums after the first death ensures sustained funding for the policy’s longevity, enabling consistent growth of its guaranteed cash value over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">The continuation of fixed premiums after the first death establishes an ongoing financial commitment. This creates context for why a grace period may apply even post-first-death, ensuring coverage isn't instantly lost despite continued liability.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">The continued payment of premiums after the first death is independent of when policy loans become available. This clause ensures consistent funding regardless of loan access timelines.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">The continued payment of premiums after the first death enables steady growth of the policy’s cash value, supporting the projected figure of $285,000 by year 10 under current assumptions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">The continuation of premiums after the first death has no bearing on the variable interest rate applied to policy loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">The continued payment of premiums after the first death sustains the policy’s funding mechanism, enabling the guaranteed growth of cash value toward the projected $712,000 by year 20.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">The continuation of fixed premiums after the first death sets the financial context for long-term policy maintenance, which indirectly influences how much liquidity may be available through loans tied to accumulated cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">The continuation of fixed premiums after the first death does not affect when policy loans become available. Loan eligibility begins after two years from issuance and remains unaffected by mortality events.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">After the first death, premiums stay constant, maintaining the policy’s viability so that borrowers may access funds via loans, which subsequently lower the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">The continuation of fixed premiums after the first death pertains to ongoing financial commitments, whereas the prohibition on partial withdrawals relates to fund accessibility. The two clauses operate independently regarding policyholder benefits and obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">After the first death occurs, the ongoing payment of premiums ensures continued coverage stability, enabling the policyholder to exercise the option to split the policy into two individual policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">After the first death, premiums stay constant, creating a stable financial obligation that sets the stage for subsequent actions such as policy splitting. This continuity enables the window for splitting to begin, requiring decisions within two years of the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">After the first death, premiums stay constant, allowing the original joint policy to transition into two separate single-life policies. This continuity supports the actuarial calculation needed to determine each new policy's face amount based on risk and funding distribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES AND ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">Premiums continue at the same rate after the first death regardless of any special circumstances. This clause operates independently of whether a split occurs due to unusual dual-death events.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">After the first death, the premium remains constant, enabling continuation of coverage under conditions that include potential policy splitting. This triggers the need for evidence of insurability to exercise the split option.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">The continuation of fixed premiums after the first death ensures stable funding for the remaining coverage, enabling potential future actions like policy splitting. However, the ability to split depends on both parties surviving the first death, meaning premium stability alone does not trigger the split—it only enables its feasibility under specific conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">Premiums remaining constant after the first death ensures continued coverage stability, while the infrequent use of the split option indicates limited real-world adoption of this specific feature, even when available under the terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">MINOR IMPACT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">The ongoing payment of premiums after the first death does not influence whether suicide within two years affects the death benefit. This clause stands independently as a separate exclusionary rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.2</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">Premiums remaining constant after the first death ensures sustained policy functionality, enabling future actions like splitting the policy during estate transitions such as divorce or trust modifications.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="87d3f292-0015-456f-a584-e257d51d0e6b" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">continues</data>
</edge>
