  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="508aac37-ccb0-404d-8bc0-26bcb809bbfb">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="2a9b94d0-ffef-4488-8d51-ea71f275e847">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="d565b9ec-bcc6-480e-ab03-fdaa8b19a0f9">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="2a863ed2-f7f3-4d99-bfb6-873ae275cacb">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="9406c263-2cb7-4749-a044-516cb52ef8e6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="b7779b5c-2f45-4da5-af98-209fb9dcab03">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="98981990-30fb-4710-af46-82dfe5e471b1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d3">Since premium waiver is unavailable on joint survivorship policies, the insured must continue paying the full annual premium of $48,600 regardless of health status, emphasizing the non-discretionary payment obligation tied to this policy type.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of premium waivers in joint survivorship policies has no bearing on when premiums are due. It only restricts potential relief options unrelated to payment dates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">Because premium waiver is unavailable, premiums must persist even after the first death, ensuring continuous coverage under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">The lack of premium waiver availability in joint survivorship policies does not influence the existence of a 60-day grace period for late payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">The absence of premium waiver coverage in joint survivorship policies does not influence the projected cash value accumulation over ten years.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of premium waiver does not affect how cash value accumulates; it pertains to payment relief under disability, whereas cash value growth is independent of such riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of premium waiver does not affect when policy loans become accessible; loan eligibility depends solely on the duration of the policy's existence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">The lack of premium waiver availability in joint survivorship policies is unrelated to the projected cash value accumulation over 20 years. The former concerns benefit exclusions, while the latter reflects long-term investment performance under assumed conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that premium waivers are unavailable on joint survivorship policies, which relates to payment relief under certain conditions. Fact sentence 2 describes the current variable interest rate applied to policy loans, which affects borrowing costs. These topics do not interact directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of premium waiver does not affect the calculation or limit of policy loans, which depend solely on cash surrender value. This statement stands independently from considerations about loan eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of premium waiver in joint survivorship policies relates to ongoing payment obligations, whereas policy loans reducing the death benefit pertain to withdrawal mechanics. The two concepts operate independently in determining financial outcomes under different conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of premium waiver does not affect the timing or eligibility of policy loans, which remain accessible regardless of claim events. This reflects separate mechanisms governing financial flexibility versus protection against payment failure.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of premium waiver means beneficiaries cannot avoid future premiums after the first death; thus, splitting the policy becomes a strategic alternative to maintain coverage independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL LINK</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">The absence of premium waiver availability limits financial protection against disability, while the prohibition on partial withdrawals restricts access to accumulated cash value; together, these provisions reinforce the policy's inflexibility regarding financial support during hardship.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTARY LIMITATIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">The absence of premium waiver in joint survivorship policies does not affect the timing requirement for splitting the policy after the first death. This condition pertains to financial relief during incapacity, whereas the split deadline relates to administrative action post-death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">The absence of a premium waiver means ongoing payment responsibility remains unchanged even if one insured becomes disabled, directly affecting whether the policyholder can sustain coverage long enough to qualify for splitting. This necessity influences how the final face amounts are allocated when dividing the policy, ensuring equitable distribution based on risk assessment.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS ALLOCATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of premium waiver does not affect the requirement that both insured parties remain alive at the time of the first death for the split option. This rule ensures continuity of coverage terms regardless of claim-related benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of premium waiver does not influence the eligibility criteria for splitting the policy after a death event. The split provision remains restricted based on specific mortality events rather than coverage terms related to waivers.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">The unavailability of premium waiver on joint survivorship policies relates to financial protections during incapacity, whereas the low usage of the split option pertains to administrative flexibility post-first-death. The two facts describe distinct operational features without mutual dependence.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">The lack of premium waiver availability affects overall policy flexibility, particularly in cases where one insured becomes disabled. This does not directly impact the need for evidence of insurability when splitting the policy, which remains a separate condition tied to post-first-death actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">The absence of premium waiver means beneficiaries may still face financial obligations even if an insured becomes disabled; however, this does not affect the suicide clause, which independently invalidates benefits if one party dies by suicide within two years.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">The lack of premium waiver availability affects overall policy cost protection, but does not directly influence the reason why the policy can be split into two single-life policies. This split function serves specific estate planning needs unrelated to premium relief mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
