  <data key="d3">The 60-day grace period exists specifically to accommodate potential delays in paying the required $48,600 annual premium, ensuring continuity unless the deadline passes.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESPONDS_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">A failure to pay the premium by the August 20th due date activates a 60-day grace period, providing temporary protection against immediate cancellation.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">A 60-day grace period allows delayed payment without immediate cancellation, providing flexibility that supports the sustained premium requirement stated after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
