  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes the grace period for missed payments, ensuring temporary coverage continuity. Fact sentence 2 provides a forward-looking estimate of accumulated cash value under assumed conditions. These elements operate independently within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 60-day grace period ensures that missed payments do not immediately terminate coverage, allowing continued accrual of cash value toward its projected level of $712,000 after 20 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
