</edge>
<edge source="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures continued coverage despite late payment, allowing time to rectify delinquency; however, access to policy loans only becomes possible after two full years of continuous coverage, regardless of whether the grace period was utilized.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a grace period allows time to pay overdue premiums without immediate cancellation, indirectly supporting continued access to policy benefits—including maintaining full death benefit eligibility when considering future loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes a buffer against cancellation due to missed payments, ensuring continued coverage during temporary delays. This stability supports long-term accumulation of cash value, enabling higher future loan amounts as referenced in fact sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
