  <data key="d3">Guaranteed cash value growth depends on sustained premium payments, such as the $48,600 annual premium specified in the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed accumulation of cash value depends on sustained premium payments, such as those required annually on August 20th.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed cash value accumulation supports the policy's long-term viability, making it feasible to maintain premium payments even after the first death without altering rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed cash value accumulation occurs regardless of whether premium waivers apply; the presence or absence of this rider has no bearing on the policy’s internal cash buildup mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed cash value growth depends on continued premium payments, making the grace period essential for preserving long-term benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">The policy's guaranteed cash value accumulation is demonstrated through its projected value of $285,000 after 10 years, reflecting the reliability of the growth mechanism described.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">The policy's guaranteed cash value accumulation supports the projection of $712,000 after 20 years, making it a direct consequence of the guaranteed growth mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed growth of cash value over time enables the policyholder to access loans after two years, making the timing of loan availability contingent upon the established cash value accumulation.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed accumulation of cash value provides the foundation for determining the maximum loanable amount under the policy, ensuring financial flexibility based on predictable growth.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">The policy's guaranteed cash value accumulation occurs independently of the variable interest rate applied to policy loans. Loan terms do not influence the guaranteed growth mechanism described in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed growth of cash value provides the financial foundation necessary for policyholders to access loans, making loan availability possible over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed growth of cash value allows borrowers to access funds via policy loans, which subsequently diminish the available death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed growth of cash value depends on restrictions preventing premature access; since withdrawals are disallowed, the accumulated funds remain intact, supporting long-term projections.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed accumulation of cash value enables the policyholder to meet eligibility requirements for splitting the policy, supporting the necessity of acting within two years of the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed accumulation of cash value enables the structural feasibility of dividing the policy into two separate policies, forming the basis for determining each new policy's face amount through actuarial methods.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed growth of cash value ensures sufficient policy equity to support future restructuring options, such as splitting the policy after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed accumulation of cash value ensures sufficient policy equity to support the conditional split provision, which requires both lives to remain active at the time of the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed accumulation of cash value ensures the policy maintains sufficient equity over time, enabling qualification for the split option, which requires proof of continued insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed growth of cash value supports long-term policy value, which enables certain options like splits, although the split itself depends on exceptional circumstances unrelated to cash value mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">The policy's guaranteed cash value growth provides long-term financial backing, while the split option’s infrequent usage reflects low practical demand despite being available under specific conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed accumulation of cash value reflects the policy’s financial performance feature, whereas the suicide clause outlines an exception affecting payout eligibility. These elements together inform the conditions under which benefits are payable.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed growth of cash value ensures financial stability over time, enabling future options like policy splits. However, the split's main purpose remains focused on estate planning needs unrelated to cash value mechanics.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">Outstanding loans based on accumulated cash value reduce the final death benefit payout, making cash value growth relevant to benefit calculations.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 emphasizes the growing cash value component of the policy, fact_sentence_1 clarifies that benefits are contingent on both lives terminating, ensuring the cash value serves as a secondary financial instrument separate from immediate payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">FINANCIAL_SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed cash value growth complements the policy’s primary function of supporting estate tax liquidity, ensuring funds are available when needed post-death.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES_PURPOSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
