  <data key="d3">The projected cash value reaching $285,000 by year 10 has no bearing on whether premium waiver benefits are offered under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 outlines the expected cash value growth over ten years based on guaranteed rates. Fact sentence 1 explains that failure to pay premiums triggers a 60-day grace period before cancellation. The timing of payments affects overall policy performance, but the specific cash value projection is unaffected by the grace period clause itself.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
