<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="caf723e6-ddcc-43d4-a184-03d6a3e4c2ac">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="1751440d-454a-40ca-b991-a1a63a4cda04">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="a6c92705-7fee-4b1a-8119-870c9a9e9533">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="3aab17c4-1487-4a97-9a3c-7b91bbd8f1d3">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="95703051-a6c5-46b9-8453-35d5f3a248c3">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="47d0dd95-0952-47fa-a5d1-005576c63f80">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="4b15d669-f81d-4abf-88b8-7b04ae13c2b4">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="71b8668a-5c99-4fd8-a85b-e4c7ee613dd8">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="7c41a8b6-d289-4b72-87d5-185fc2f91e28">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="ea0c953d-6e85-467f-99d0-0c3563285357">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="46a80231-ec06-4991-aa15-39f963d8f868">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d3">Loan benefits becoming accessible after two years depend on the policy having remained in force through regular premium payments, such as the $48,600 annual installment.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">The ability to take out policy loans becomes effective only after the second anniversary of the policy’s start date, meaning that the initial premium payment cycle must complete one full year before this feature activates.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">Loan eligibility beginning after two years of policy duration is unrelated to whether premiums remain unchanged after the first death occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability after two years does not influence whether premium waivers apply; the presence or absence of such waivers is independent of loan terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability after two years depends on sustained policy maintenance over that period, meaning consistent premium payments—even under the grace period—are necessary to meet the duration threshold required for borrowing privileges.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability after two years relies on the existence of accumulated cash value, which is ensured by the policy’s guaranteed growth mechanism described in the earlier statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">Loan eligibility beginning after two years sets a timing constraint that precedes long-term cash value milestones such as the $285,000 target at year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">POSTDATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability after two years allows policyholders to manage cash needs while preserving coverage, enabling continued contributions toward achieving the projected $712,000 cash value at year 20 under stable assumptions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">After two years of policy duration, borrowers gain access to loans; at that point, the maximum allowable loan size is capped at 90% of the cash surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">After two years, policyholders gain access to loans, which subsequently decrease the death benefit by the same amount borrowed.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES AND CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">The availability of policy loans begins after two years of policy duration, creating the opportunity for borrowing under specific conditions. Interest accrues on such loans at a current rate of 5.5% annually, applying once funds are accessed.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">Loan access becomes possible after two years of policy duration, independent of withdrawal restrictions. Since withdrawals are explicitly disallowed, the policy's financial flexibility relies solely on borrowing against accumulated cash value rather than accessing funds through withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">Loan eligibility begins after two years of policy duration, regardless of whether the first death has occurred. This means loans may not be accessible prior to the second anniversary, even if the first death happened earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">Access to policy loans begins after two years of coverage, enabling liquidity support that could assist in managing financial obligations tied to splitting the policy after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">Loan eligibility begins after two years of policy existence, establishing an initial timeframe during which financial options open. This creates a window where the decision to split the policy may later be exercised, contingent upon surviving beyond the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">The availability of policy loans after two years depends solely on the passage of time since issuance, regardless of who survives the first death. This timing requirement does not influence whether both individuals must still be alive for the split option.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">After two years, policyholders gain access to loans against the cash value, enabling financial flexibility during transitions such as splitting the policy. This timing allows for the subsequent division of the policy into two single-life policies, where each recipient's face amount is calculated using actuarial methods.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">Loan access becomes possible after two years of policy existence, independent of whether the split option is pursued. The rarity of exercising the split feature does not affect when loans become available.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">The ability to take policy loans after two years coincides with the timeframe in which the policy may be split, potentially influencing decisions around financial flexibility before splitting.</data>
  <data key="d4">TEMPORALLY RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">Loan access becomes permissible after two years of policy duration, independent of any special event related to dual deaths. This timeline does not influence nor depend on the extremely limited scenario where a split might occur due to ambiguous cause-of-death situations.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">Loan eligibility begins after two years of policy duration, enabling financial flexibility during the term. This timing aligns with when the split option may also be exercised, supporting long-term estate planning needs such as divorce or trust adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">TIMING_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">The availability of policy loans after two years is independent of whether suicide occurs within that timeframe. The second fact concerns an exception to coverage based on intent, unrelated to financial access provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">Loans becoming accessible after two years enable actions that subsequently reduce the death benefit, making the timing of loan use critical to the ultimate payout amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">While the death benefit is contingent on both insured persons dying, the policy allows financial flexibility through loans after two years, supporting interim use without affecting the ultimate claim.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">Access to policy loans after two years supports the policy’s design for estate tax liquidity, enabling beneficiaries to manage tax obligations before receiving the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS_OBJECTIVE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Estate planning is facilitated by the loan provision after two years, allowing beneficiaries or trustees to manage assets more effectively while preserving the policy’s death benefit through controlled borrowing.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPRTS_PURPOSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1751440d-454a-40ca-b991-a1a63a4cda04" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">start_date_for_loan_eligibility</data>
</edge>
<edge source="71b8668a-5c99-4fd8-a85b-e4c7ee613dd8" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">become available after 2 years</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="696711db-eeca-4cd8-a66f-b3f79293472e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="d3eabdf9-a44a-4923-8447-4e53286a6b36">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="6eedf5f5-e3c1-4498-b71b-b459b30137c2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="6f0ff0a4-9f99-44f8-b3e5-41af82bc059a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="876cfbd3-9323-4f7e-ad88-009dbaa1b7a1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="0c9d7f52-3a26-4e77-a874-0db96d0ebfe9">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="ef94cd77-0b97-4a30-a5c3-2e5579637791">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="fd79e77b-d9c0-4e7c-84dd-d7d41e87bfeb">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="f9de8c9b-bdfe-4550-8aaa-d178eb868c09">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="d37f57c8-1f29-4ef9-ae6e-c917a95ee872">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="33735938-adba-407d-b25b-0b0a9de736e1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="d2fd78d0-fb19-41a8-b6b8-d664df2c3d40">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d3">The availability of loans up to 90% of the cash surrender value relies on sufficient cash value being generated through ongoing premium payments, such as the $48,600 annual premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">The ability to borrow up to 90% of the cash surrender value depends on sufficient cash buildup over time, which results from consistent premium payments made annually on August 20th.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">The availability of loans up to 90% of the cash surrender value provides a financial mechanism during the post-first-death phase, potentially affecting whether premium payments can still be sustained despite reduced coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">FINANCIAL_SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">While the maximum loan amount is capped at 90% of cash surrender value, this restriction has no bearing on whether premium waivers apply, as those are governed by separate rider terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 specifies that policyholders may borrow up to 90% of the cash surrender value, which depends on sustained premium payments and growth over time. Without timely payments—even with a grace period—the cash value might stagnate, reducing potential loan capacity.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDENT ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">The ability to borrow up to 90% of the cash surrender value is contingent upon the policy’s guaranteed cash value buildup over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">The rule that loans may reach up to 90% of the cash surrender value implies that such a limit would apply when the cash value reaches $285,000 after ten years, assuming consistent growth.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">The rule allowing loans up to 90% of the cash surrender value implies that such projections must be reliable to calculate feasible borrowing limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">The availability of policy loans is contingent upon the policy being in force for at least two years, ensuring that the 90% ceiling on loan amounts only applies post-eligibility period.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount is capped at 90% of the cash surrender value, and any loan taken incurs an interest charge based on a current variable rate of 5.5% annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount is capped at 90% of the cash surrender value, and any loan taken reduces the death benefit equally, meaning borrowers trade future payout for immediate liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable loan amount is capped at 90% of the cash surrender value, ensuring that even after the first death, borrowers cannot exceed this percentage when accessing funds from the policy’s accumulated value.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable loan is capped at 90% of the cash surrender value, providing a mechanism for liquidity without triggering withdrawal penalties; however, since partial withdrawals are disallowed, borrowers cannot use direct payouts from the policy's cash value even when eligible for loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable loan is determined by the cash surrender value, regardless of when the policy may be split. This provision operates independently of any deadline related to splitting the policy after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">The availability of policy loans up to 90% of cash surrender value supports financial liquidity during transitions, potentially enabling the funding needed to maintain coverage when splitting the policy after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_LINK</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount being limited to 90% of the cash surrender value supports the structural integrity needed for future splits, enabling flexible distribution of benefits during division. This financial mechanism underpins the feasibility of allocating separate face amounts via actuarial methods post-split.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount is determined by the cash surrender value, enabling liquidity access; however, using the split option requires additional underwriting proof regardless of loan capacity.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan limit tied to cash surrender value does not influence or relate to the conditions under which the policy may be split due to uncertain causes of simultaneous deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan limit of 90% of cash surrender value relates to financial flexibility during the policy term, whereas the requirement that both individuals remain alive at the first death governs eligibility for policy splitting—a structural change unrelated to borrowing rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable loan is set at 90% of the cash surrender value, providing liquidity options during the policy term. This provision exists independently of how often the policy might be split into two separate policies post-first-death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">The ability to take loans up to 90% of cash surrender value supports liquidity needs that might arise when restructuring coverage via the split option, especially in complex estate planning cases involving divorce or trusts.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan limit tied to cash surrender value does not influence whether suicide affects the death benefit. This clause operates independently regarding claim eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">The reduction in death benefit caused by loans depends on the available cash surrender value, which determines the maximum loan size permitted.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 enables liquidity through policy loans based on accumulated cash value, which indirectly supports the feasibility of maintaining coverage until both insured persons pass—a prerequisite for the $2.5M payout in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPRTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan provision enables flexible use of built-up cash value, supporting the primary intent of the policy: ensuring sufficient liquidity for estate tax payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">DIRECTLY_SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Estate planning uses include leveraging policy loans and potential splitting of the policy post-first-death, making the financial mechanics directly relevant to long-term wealth transfer goals.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0c9d7f52-3a26-4e77-a874-0db96d0ebfe9" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">determines maximum loan amount via 90%</data>
</edge>
