<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d3">The loan interest rate of 5.5% reflects the cost of accessing funds via policy loans, independent of the fixed annual premium of $48,600, which governs regular payments rather than financing options.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 mentions that policy loans carry a variable interest rate of 5.5%, independent of when premiums are due. Fact sentence 1 outlines the fixed annual deadline for premium payments, which has no bearing on loan interest rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">The current 5.5% annual interest rate on policy loans does not affect the ongoing premium obligation after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 specifies the variable interest rate of 5.5% annually for policy loans, impacting how costly borrowing against the policy may be. Fact sentence 1 notes the absence of premium waiver benefits on such policies, affecting coverage continuity during disability. The two statements address distinct policy provisions without overlap.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 states that policy loans carry a variable interest rate of 5.5%, which applies regardless of whether a grace period was utilized for premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">While the policy allows loans based on cash surrender value, the variable interest rate on those loans does not impact the guaranteed growth of cash value over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">The variable interest rate on policy loans affects borrowing costs but has no direct bearing on the predetermined projection of cash value growth outlined in year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">The variable loan interest rate of 5.5% applies when funds are borrowed from the policy's cash value, but it has no direct bearing on the projected cash value amount specified for year 20.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">A variable interest rate of 5.5% applies to policy loans, which only become accessible after the policy has been active for two years, meaning borrowers incur interest charges upon withdrawal from that point forward.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">A policy allows loans up to 90% of its cash surrender value, with interest charged at a variable rate now set at 5.5% per year.</data>
  <data key="d4">APPLIES_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">The interest rate on policy loans does not influence the ability to split the policy after the first death. This provision remains independent of loan financing terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">The interest rate on policy loans is independent of how the face amounts are allocated when the original policy splits into two single-life policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">The policy allows loans against its cash value, subject to a current variable interest rate of 5.5%, but it explicitly prohibits any form of partial withdrawals regardless of loan activity.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">The current 5.5% annual interest rate on policy loans increases the financial burden of borrowing against the policy’s cash value, thereby amplifying the reduction in the death benefit when loans are taken.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">The current variable interest rate of 5.5% applies to any policy loan taken out, regardless of whether it occurs before or after the first death, influencing the cost of borrowing under that condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">The interest rate on policy loans (currently 5.5%) pertains to borrowing against the cash value, while the requirement to elect splitting within two years of the first death relates to restructuring coverage post-death. These are independent operational rules without mutual impact.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">The interest rate on policy loans (currently 5.5%) affects the cost of borrowing against the policy's cash value, while the requirement that both individuals remain alive at the time of the first death governs access to the split option. Although both pertain to policy provisions, one relates to financing costs and the other to structural flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">The current variable interest rate on policy loans is 5.5%, but this does not influence the infrequent use of the split option.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">The loan interest rate does not influence eligibility or conditions for splitting the policy after the first death. The availability of the split option depends solely on exceptional circumstances like uncertain timing of simultaneous deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">The interest rate on policy loans affects borrowing cost, which could influence decisions around using the split option later. However, the need for evidence of insurability during a split remains independent of current loan rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">The interest rate on policy loans does not influence whether suicide within two years affects the death benefit. These are independent provisions governing different aspects of the policy's terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">The interest rate on policy loans (currently 5.5%) affects the cost of borrowing against the policy’s cash value, while the split option enables restructuring the policy for legal or estate planning events such as divorce or trust changes. These elements together support advanced estate management strategies.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
