<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="1f6911a4-327b-4507-9279-9f4040f93c5d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="467a20c8-b261-4dfa-b40d-0fc32f664830">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="816e1fda-51c5-427c-a590-aee56b5b7b17">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="cf450104-d701-46b2-9789-9cffdf71af5c">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="9763e6d7-ce40-4ea5-bebe-349742abf827">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="1c37e440-e266-43a3-b01e-6a0056fe4b03">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d3">Loans drawn from the policy reduce the death benefit dollar-for-dollar, meaning the high annual premium ($48,600) supports a larger base value upon which such deductions occur, ensuring the policy’s long-term financial integrity remains intact unless withdrawals or borrowing intervene.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is reduced dollar-for-dollar by any policy loans, meaning the timing and amount of premium payments indirectly support the stability of the death benefit before loan usage.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">Loans reduce the death benefit dollar-for-dollar, meaning that even after the first death when premiums continue, borrowed amounts decrease the final payout, affecting overall policy value.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans diminish the death benefit by the amount borrowed, affecting final payouts. This stands apart from the lack of premium waiver coverage, which concerns continuation of payments upon disability—not related to loan effects.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">Loan activity reduces the death benefit directly, so even if a borrower uses the grace period to avoid lapse, any subsequent loans diminish the final payout regardless of timely payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">Since policy loans reduce the death benefit dollar-for-dollar, the existence of such a mechanism depends on the presence of accumulated cash value, which is guaranteed under the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">Since policy loans reduce the death benefit dollar-for-dollar, the actual net benefit available upon claim may be significantly lower than the projected cash value of $285,000 after 10 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">IMPACTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">Since policy loans reduce the death benefit dollar-for-dollar, the substantial cash value accumulation described in fact_sentence_1 increases the amount available for such loans, thereby impacting future payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is reduced dollar-for-dollar when loans are taken, but such loans only become accessible after the policy has been active for two years.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES DUE TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">Taking a loan up to 90% of the cash surrender value results in a direct dollar-for-dollar decrease in the death benefit, so the ability to borrow hinges on this financial trade-off.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">Since policy loans reduce the death benefit dollar-for-dollar, any borrowed amount diminishes the payout proportionally, making the associated 5.5% interest rate a significant factor in long-term policy value erosion.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">The ability to take policy loans after the first death allows borrowers to access funds while affecting the remaining death benefit, reinforcing the impact outlined in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">Loan activity reduces the death benefit, but since withdrawals are not allowed, this limitation doesn't interact with the loan provision beyond general constraints on cash access.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">Loan reductions directly impact the remaining death benefit, which becomes relevant when considering whether to exercise the policy-splitting option after the first death, especially since splits require continued coverage and financial viability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">Loan provisions diminish the death benefit, which may affect the decision-making around splitting the policy post-first-death. This creates an indirect incentive to act quickly before loan impacts compound.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">Loan provisions diminish the death benefit, influencing the financial framework under which future splits occur. This sets constraints that inform how actuarial allocations determine individual policy values during division.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">Loan reductions impact the death benefit amount, but the eligibility to split the policy depends solely on whether both individuals are still alive when the first death occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">Loan activity reduces the death benefit amount; however, this has no bearing on the eligibility criteria for splitting the policy after the first death, which depends solely on exceptional circumstances such as uncertain cause of concurrent deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">Loan usage impacts the remaining death benefit, which could influence eligibility or terms when considering future splits. However, the need for evidence of insurability upon splitting remains independent of existing loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">Loan provisions impact the net death benefit available to beneficiaries, influencing the rationale behind using the split feature in sensitive transitions such as divorce or trust restructuring.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">Loan provisions diminish the death benefit, affecting payout outcomes. The low utilization of the split option suggests it's seldom needed despite being available under specific conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">Loan activity reduces the death benefit directly, while suicide within two years nullifies the benefit entirely. Both conditions affect the payout but operate through different triggers.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains the precise nature of loan impacts—dollar-for-dollar reductions—which directly supports and elaborates on the general claim made in fact_sentence_1 about reduced payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">Any policy loans diminish the ultimate death benefit described in fact_sentence_1, so the $2.5 million payout is subject to reduction based on prior borrowing activity.</data>
  <data key="d4">REDUCES_BENEFIT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">Loans against the policy decrease its ability to fulfill its core function of providing estate tax liquidity, making it less effective for its intended use.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNDERMINES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Loan usage reduces the death benefit, which is critical for estate planning where precise beneficiary outcomes depend on maintaining sufficient coverage post-loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="816e1fda-51c5-427c-a590-aee56b5b7b17" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">reduce_death_benefit</data>
</edge>
