  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d3">Access to policy loans after two years depends on the buildup of cash value, which is driven by regular premium payments such as the $48,600 annual fee.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">The ability to take policy loans before or after the first death provides liquidity regardless of when premiums are paid, meaning the payment date has minimal impact on loan accessibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability beginning after two years applies irrespective of the first death event, so it does not depend on premium continuity post-death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">Access to policy loans prior to or after the first death does not impact whether a premium waiver would apply, as those benefits are governed by distinct terms unrelated to borrowing rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability prior to or after the first death depends on maintaining active policy status, which is supported by the grace period preventing immediate lapse upon missed payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability relies on sufficient accumulated cash value; therefore, the existence of such loans implies that cash value has been growing according to the guaranteed schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans are permissible anytime after two years from issue, irrespective of when the first death occurs; however, this access does not affect the predetermined cash value projections such as the $285,000 target at year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability prior to or after the first death relies on accumulated cash value, making the long-term cash value projection relevant to understanding borrowing capacity.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">The statement that loans are available before or after the first death implies broader access, but it conflicts with the requirement that loans require at least two years of policy existence, limiting actual availability based on timeline rather than event sequence alone.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFLICTS_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">Loan access remains possible both before and after the first death, subject to the constraint that amounts borrowed do not surpass 90% of the current cash surrender value, maintaining consistency with the policy's financial limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability prior to or after the first death enables borrowers to access funds based on accumulated cash value, subject to an applicable interest rate of 5.5%, which determines the repayment burden.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">Since policy loans reduce the death benefit dollar-for-dollar, their availability both before and after the first death ensures ongoing financial implications tied to the policy’s payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability is permitted regardless of the timing relative to the first death, but this provision operates independently of the restriction against partial withdrawals, which remains absolute throughout the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans are permitted regardless of whether the first death has occurred, providing financial flexibility early on. This stands independently from the later option to split the policy upon the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans may be taken at any point after two years, including after the first death, but the ability to split the policy depends on both lives being intact at the moment of the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans may be accessed either prior to or after the first death, offering financial flexibility during transition periods. This option exists independently of the deadline for electing policy splits, which requires action within two years of the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">TEMPORAL CONSTRAINT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans being permitted after the first death enable financial flexibility during transition periods, potentially influencing decisions around splitting the policy. This contextual support sets the stage for subsequent actions such as allocating benefits via actuarial methods when dividing the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability regardless of the first death event is unrelated to the specific estate planning purposes behind the split option.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability pertains to financial flexibility during the policy term, while the split option applies exclusively under extreme circumstances involving dual fatalities. These provisions serve different purposes and operate independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability applies regardless of timing relative to the first death, whereas the requirement for evidence of insurability arises specifically during the exercise of the split option after the first death. These provisions operate independently within different procedural contexts.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">Loan provisions allow policyholders to access funds pre- or post-first death, offering liquidity without terminating coverage. This feature operates independently of whether the split option is utilized, which remains uncommon despite being an available restructuring tool.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">Loan availability is not contingent upon the occurrence of suicide, nor does it affect the suicide clause’s applicability. These provisions function separately within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="88aa87d8-80b9-4dde-a8fb-f63088913005" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">timing_of_loan_availability</data>
</edge>
<edge source="71752e80-d276-4d29-b381-fde537a69837" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">available_before_or_after_first_death</data>
</edge>
