</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="6b7fdb34-3c77-42fa-bec9-34f7ad7de54e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="e1865c29-7535-469c-9c68-1715ddc76f55">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy post-first-death depends on maintaining active coverage through timely payments, making the $48,600 annual premium a prerequisite for accessing that feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of splitting the policy after the first death depends on sustained premium payments maintaining active coverage over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">The availability of splitting the policy into two single-life policies hinges on the first death occurring, which triggers the need for sustained premium payments to maintain eligibility for such restructuring.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">Splitting the policy allows each surviving party to retain coverage individually, making it especially valuable when premium waivers are absent and continued payment would otherwise burden them financially.</data>
  <data key="d4">STRATEGIC ALTERNATIVE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">Splitting the policy after the first death depends on it remaining active, which relies on timely premium payments—or use of the grace period—to avoid termination prior to triggering the event.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">The availability of splitting the policy after the first death implies that the policy's built-up cash value must have reached a level capable of supporting new individual coverage, reinforcing the importance of guaranteed cash value accumulation.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">The option to split the policy after the first death depends on having enough built-up cash value, making the projected $285,000 figure relevant as it indicates potential liquidity that could support such restructuring.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy into two single-life policies after the first death depends on survival and insurability proof, but this action has no impact on the pre-calculated cash value projections made over 20 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy after the first death depends on survival past the two-year mark, making prior loan availability relevant for potential interim funding needs.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">The option to split the policy after the first death creates a scenario where borrowers might access higher loan limits tied to increased individual cash values, making the loan provision more relevant post-split.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLING_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">The option to split the policy after the first death has no bearing on the applicable interest rate for policy loans, which is governed by different contractual conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy after the first death introduces potential use cases where borrowers might consider taking loans before splitting, knowing that such actions would diminish the payout each surviving insured receives.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">After the first death, the policyholder may choose to convert the joint policy into two individual policies, contingent on surviving health proof. This action is unrelated to the availability of policy loans prior to or after the event.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy post-first-death depends on the policy retaining sufficient value and compliance with rules such as prohibiting withdrawals, which helps maintain financial stability for the new individual policies.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">The right to split the policy after the first death depends on making the election within two years; without meeting this deadline, the option becomes unavailable.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">After the first death, the policyholder may choose to split the policy; each resulting policy's face amount is calculated using actuarial methods based on risk and value assumptions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">The option to split the policy after the first death depends on both insured individuals surviving until that event. Without both being alive, the split cannot occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy post-first-death applies generally, but this particular clause specifies an extremely limited scenario where such a split might still occur despite ambiguity in timing of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">The option to split the policy after the first death depends on providing proof of insurability, ensuring the surviving individual meets underwriting standards.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_REQUIREMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">The policy allows splitting into two single-life policies upon the first death, primarily to facilitate legal or financial restructuring such as divorce settlements or trust adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS PURPOSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a contractual provision allowing policy splitting after the first death. Fact_sentence_2 notes that this feature is seldom utilized in practice.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy after the first death does not influence whether suicide within two years affects the death benefit. This scenario remains independent of post-mortem policy restructuring options.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of splitting the policy affects long-term financial planning and potential loan impacts, whereas existing loans already reduce the death benefit even before such a split occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">While the second fact enables splitting the policy after the first death, it does not override the primary survivorship clause unless exercised; thus, the initial payout rule still applies unless the split option is elected.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_OVERRIDE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">The option to split the policy post-first-death complements its original design for estate tax liquidity by offering adaptability in managing individual beneficiaries and financial obligations over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES_PURPOSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Estate planning serves as the primary rationale for permitting the policy split, making this feature integral to achieving broader succession goals outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS_OBJECTIVE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c">
  <data key="d3">The option to split the policy after the first death relies on clear ownership provisions established by the trust, meaning the splitting mechanism only applies if the trust allows it.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="dc5e7101-a50d-4b25-8d7d-9d2fc8fab9fc">
  <data key="d3">The right to split the policy after the first death depends on compliance with assignment restrictions requiring trustee authorization, meaning the split action cannot proceed without formal consent.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy after the first death does not affect the initial 30-day cancellation window, nor vice versa. They operate independently across different phases of the policy lifecycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14" target="510a4351-8c5a-44d4-a731-1c1dea4323a8">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy after the first death does not affect the 30-day refund window, which applies only before policy acceptance. One pertains to long-term estate planning; the other to early exit rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="75ca4a8f-d72f-4259-a275-97ac8c159dc9" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">triggered_by_first_death</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6b7fdb34-3c77-42fa-bec9-34f7ad7de54e" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="f9d9d4a2-7331-4254-b042-eef37b62a202">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
