  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="442835dd-3229-435d-9409-c944ffe4c52c">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="afa867a9-36b0-4616-b404-80c6b9b057b6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="ad6d6691-5e14-47b0-af48-8ecaa8ee8b79">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="feec8f21-cec2-4674-9fa9-41758c2e3182">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="683e9a89-fa3d-497a-9bc8-7dd779e071e6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="6ebc8ef4-6626-468a-85de-b88942917e04">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="6fb6db8d-82eb-43b5-a278-75faa66c67d8">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="e6d7150c-a91c-4b46-9e2d-3bf1ef614ea3">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="29d6b500-ea6c-419a-a046-b811b29e2171">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="b728997e-e3dd-4ba2-8a00-7e76f8ec3823">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to elect splitting within two years of the first death implies that the policyholder must remain current on premiums throughout this period to maintain active status and qualify for the split.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to act within two years of the first death relies on prior policy maintenance through timely premium payments, ensuring eligibility for post-death modifications like splitting.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">The deadline to split the policy—within two years of the first death—is contingent upon the continuation of premiums at the original rate post-first-death, ensuring ongoing eligibility and stability during the decision period.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">While the option to split the policy must be exercised within two years of the first death, this timeline has no bearing on whether premium waiver is available, as that feature is independently excluded from such policies regardless of timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to elect splitting within two years of the first death depends on maintaining an active policy during that timeframe. Timely premium payments ensure the policy stays in force through this critical period.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to act within two years of the first death underscores the importance of having sufficient accumulated cash value, which is ensured by the policy's guaranteed growth mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">The need to make the split election within two years of the first death sets a critical timeframe for policy restructuring; however, it has no direct bearing on the projected cash value amount at year 10, which depends solely on assumed interest rates and premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the split election must happen within two years of the first death sets a critical window for action, irrespective of how much cash value has accrued by year 20. This temporal rule governs eligibility rather than being affected by future projections.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">The right to split the policy must be exercised within two years of the first death, requiring prior establishment of policy tenure; thus, it relies on having already satisfied the minimum two-year holding period needed for other benefits like loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to elect splitting within two years of the first death does not influence the percentage cap on policy loans, which remains fixed at 90% of cash surrender value irrespective of timing constraints.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">The deadline for electing to split the policy (within two years of the first death) governs when beneficiaries may restructure coverage; however, it has no bearing on the variable interest rate charged for policy loans, which remains unaffected by this timeline.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">The need to elect splitting within two years of the first death influences when borrowers might consider using policy loans, especially given that such loans reduce the payout amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">TIME_DEPENDENT_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">The right to split the policy into two single-life policies is limited by a window of two years from the first death. This restriction operates separately from when loans might be taken, although both decisions fall under post-first-death provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">TIME-BOUND ACTION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to act within two years of the first death governs when the policy may be divided, regardless of withdrawal restrictions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to act within two years ensures that the decision to split the policy remains timely and enforceable after the first death occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the split election occurs within two years of the first death depends on both individuals surviving until that event, ensuring eligibility remains intact.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">The deadline to elect splitting the policy depends on the timing of the first death; without meeting this timeline, the option becomes unavailable. Evidence of insurability is necessary to confirm continued eligibility under the terms of the split.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to elect splitting within two years of the first death sets the necessary precondition for determining each new policy’s face amount through actuarial allocation.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">Even though the split must occur within two years of the first death, it is only permitted under exceptional circumstances where the cause of death cannot be clearly determined, such as when multiple people die simultaneously.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_RESTRICTION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the split must happen within two years of the first death sets a temporal boundary for an action that is seldom taken, reflecting low real-world utilization despite formal availability.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL USAGE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">The deadline to exercise the split option aligns with key life events like divorce or trust modifications, ensuring timely implementation when needed most.</data>
  <data key="d4">TIMING_FOR_PURPOSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">The timing requirement for splitting the policy after the first death does not depend on whether suicide occurred during the initial two-year period. This condition applies regardless of the cause of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to elect a policy split within two years of the first death creates urgency around managing policy terms—including potential loans—which could otherwise erode the death benefit available during or after the split process.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">The survivorship nature of the policy ensures no payout until both insured persons pass, making the window for splitting critical to avoid forfeiting future flexibility in claim strategy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">Estate tax liquidity goals are enhanced by the ability to split the policy within two years of the first death, allowing reallocation of coverage based on changing financial needs.</data>
  <data key="d4">TIMING_DEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Estate planning objectives justify the existence of the two-year window to split the policy, ensuring flexibility in managing assets after one insured person passes.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS_OBJECTIVE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="dc5e7101-a50d-4b25-8d7d-9d2fc8fab9fc">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to split the policy within two years of the first death aligns with estate planning needs that also necessitate trustee oversight for any assignments, ensuring compliance with trust conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to split the policy within two years of the first death does not impact the right to cancel within 30 days of receipt, as these are distinct temporal phases of policy management.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to split the policy within two years of the first death depends on whether either individual holds ownership rights through the trust, making the timing clause conditional on legal designation rather than automatic entitlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203" target="510a4351-8c5a-44d4-a731-1c1dea4323a8">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to split the policy within two years of the first death does not affect the 30-day window for cancellation and refund. These provisions operate independently—one applies after an insured's death, the other before commitment.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="442835dd-3229-435d-9409-c944ffe4c52c" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is the start date for the 2-year deadline</data>
</edge>
