<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d3">Actuarial allocation determines how the original policy's face value is divided when split; this process only applies under conditions that require prior adherence to premium obligations such as paying the $48,600 annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">The actuarial allocation of face amounts determines how benefits are distributed when the original policy is split, relying on consistent premium payments being made over time to maintain eligibility and validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">The determination of each new policy’s face amount through actuarial allocation relies on the assumption that premiums will continue at the same rate after the first death, ensuring sufficient funds exist to support the division without altering coverage terms prematurely.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">Actuarial allocation determines each new policy's face amount after splitting, reflecting the relative risks and contributions of each individual. Since no premium waiver exists, consistent premium payments become essential to maintain eligibility for such a split, making the allocation dependent on sustained compliance.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS ON PAYMENT OBLIGATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">Actuarial allocation sets the face amounts of newly created policies upon division, contingent on surviving the initial grace period without lapse; thus, timely payment during the grace period enables such restructuring.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">Actuarial allocation of face amounts in the split policies relies on the pre-existing, guaranteed cash value buildup established under the original policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">Actuarial allocation determines how the original policy’s face amount is divided between two new single-life policies upon splitting; this process depends on factors including the accrued cash value, such as the $285,000 projected after 10 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">Actuarial allocation determines how the final face amount is divided between the two new single-life policies after the original policy splits. This process relies on the assumed long-term cash value growth, such as the $712,000 projection at year 20.</data>
  <data key="d4">DERIVED_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">The determination of individual face amounts via actuarial allocation occurs when the original joint-life policy is split into two separate policies. This process typically follows the eligibility window established by the policy terms, including the requirement that loans have already become available after two years.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">Actuarial allocation determines each new policy’s face amount after splitting, ensuring equitable distribution based on risk and value, which relies on the underlying cash value supported by the 90% loan cap provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">How each new policy's face amount is calculated via actuarial methods has no bearing on the current variable interest rate charged for policy loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">Actuarial allocation determines each new policy’s face amount after a split, ensuring equitable distribution based on risk and value, which may reflect prior adjustments such as those caused by loans affecting overall benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">The determination of each new policy’s face amount using actuarial allocation ensures fairness based on risk profiles after the original policy splits. This step logically follows from the possibility of splitting enabled by provisions including access to loans post-first-death.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">Actuarial allocation determines each new policy’s face amount based on predefined criteria, ensuring fairness; this mechanism relies on intact policy terms, including restrictions like the ban on withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy post-first-death depends on actuarially determined allocations that define each new policy’s face amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">Actuarial allocation determines the face amounts of the split policies, but only applies if the election occurs within two years of the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">The ability to allocate face amounts via actuarial methods depends on whether the split occurs under the narrow conditions specified, such as simultaneous deaths with medical uncertainty.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">The determination of each policy's face amount relies on an actuarial process that follows the successful completion of the split condition, including providing evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">The determination of each policy's face amount via actuarial allocation depends on the precondition that both insured individuals remain alive at the time of the first death, ensuring eligibility for the split.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">The split option involves dividing the original policy into two separate policies based on actuarial calculations, yet it is seldom utilized despite being available under specific conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">The actuarial allocation ensures fair distribution of coverage based on individual risk profiles, enabling effective implementation of the policy split for legal or financial restructuring such as divorce or trust adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">The determination of each split policy’s face amount relies on actuarial principles, independent of suicide clauses that affect claim eligibility. This ensures equitable division based on risk profiles regardless of future behavioral risks.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3802ac41-dccc-4dd8-b73b-b865bb299a55" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">determined_by_actuarial_allocation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c5c35849-b9b3-4063-9906-dda53feeb6e9" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
</edge>
