  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">affects</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f6043ab5-033b-4488-a5dd-3515558efb4c" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">affects</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="345bacdf-c40e-4c15-8bf5-2e2379dbd9d6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="d55e4d98-b091-4345-a33a-a403438baa90">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="44c8d817-1ef4-49a3-abd3-e516190a7a77">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="d8575ae0-cefe-4c89-930c-038a31c7b270">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="ab8275a4-f540-490d-a633-3fecf5b3e277">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="10e63265-c69a-4f4e-93c8-8c0cb47a267d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="8149211a-bb6f-4562-a6b1-318d6d2be184">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="b42523f6-bc4e-40ac-bcc5-59f86368b76a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="6d4bd0c9-a029-4cdd-849e-edd66db048d8">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="b392c564-07b1-4126-b86b-41194f71f905">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="f6cacafe-5d3a-4346-9c65-c66588be307b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="93efed67-c6aa-4cd7-9378-a37b9da605b1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d3">The condition requiring both insured individuals to be alive during the first death event governs access to the policy-splitting provision, whereas the $48,600 annual premium defines the recurring cost regardless of such events.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">For the policy to be eligible for splitting after the first death, both individuals must still be alive at that moment, meaning the trigger event occurs before any individual's demise affects the contract’s viability. This condition constrains how early the split process may occur relative to the premium cycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">For the policy to be split into two single-life policies after the first death, both insured individuals must still be alive at that moment; otherwise, the split cannot occur. This requirement constrains how the long-term premium commitment described in fact_sentence_1 may ultimately be utilized.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLING_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">Since both individuals must be alive at the time of the first death to qualify for splitting the policy, it implies that any form of reduced capacity or early termination (like through premium waiver) would not override this structural precondition.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">For the split option to apply, both individuals must still be alive when the first death occurs, meaning timely premium payments—even under a grace period—are necessary to maintain policy validity until that point.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">For the split option to be viable under the policy terms, it depends on the presence of a stable, growing cash value built through guaranteed accumulation.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">For the policy to be split into two single-life policies upon the first death, both individuals must still be alive when the event occurs. This prerequisite has no bearing on the cash value projections made for year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">For the policy to be split into two single-life policies, both insured persons must still be alive at the moment of the first death—an eligibility criterion unrelated to the cash value projection, even though it could affect how future benefits are distributed.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">For the policy to be split into two single-life policies upon the first death, both insured persons must have survived until that point. This condition is independent of when loans become accessible, which hinges only on the policy’s age.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">The rule that both insured persons must survive until the first death ensures the validity of the split option, which could affect future access to funds via loans, although the loan cap itself does not depend on this condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">The condition requiring both insured persons to be alive at the time of the first death determines whether the policy may be split into two single-life policies. This restriction does not directly affect the interest rate charged on policy loans, which remains independent of survivorship criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that both insureds remain alive at the first death governs access to the split option, regardless of any prior loans affecting the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL ON SURVIVAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that both individuals remain alive at the first death is necessary for the policy split option, independent of whether loans have been issued earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">The need for both individuals to survive the first death enables the policy split mechanism, which relies on maintaining sufficient policy value—preserved by disallowing premature withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">For the policy split to be possible after the first death, it requires that both individuals were alive at the time of the initial death, making this a prerequisite condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">For the split option to be exercised within two years of the first death, it is essential that both insured parties were alive at the moment of the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">For an actuarial allocation to determine the new face amounts, it is necessary that both individuals were alive when the first death occurred, making this a required condition for the process to begin.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that both individuals remain alive at the first death ensures the split option remains viable, making it necessary to provide evidence of insurability to proceed legally and under policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that both individuals remain alive at the time of the first death defines when the split option could theoretically be triggered. However, despite this possibility, the split option is seldom utilized in practice.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 requires both individuals to be alive during the first death event for splitting eligibility. However, fact_sentence_2 restricts the split option to extremely rare instances where deaths occur simultaneously and cause medical ambiguity, making it incompatible with the standard interpretation implied by fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INCONSISTENT WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">The split option requires both insured individuals to be alive at the first death, ensuring eligibility for restructuring; this condition enables its use in legal transitions like divorce or trust updates.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITION_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that both insured individuals remain alive at the time of the first death ensures the policy split remains viable. This condition indirectly relates to the suicide clause because if suicide causes the first death, it may trigger the exclusion regardless of survival status.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_DEPENDENCY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c">
  <data key="d3">The viability of splitting the policy after the first death hinges on both insured individuals being alive, but executing such a split may require ownership rights established through the trust document.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="dc5e7101-a50d-4b25-8d7d-9d2fc8fab9fc">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that both insured parties remain alive for the split option to apply interacts with the restriction on assignment without trustee approval, as both limit how the policy’s benefits and ownership can be altered post-issuance, especially in complex estate structures.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that both insured individuals remain alive at the first death does not affect the policyholder’s ability to cancel within 30 days of receipt. Conversely, the 30-day free look allows cancellation regardless of future events involving the insured's lives.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c" target="510a4351-8c5a-44d4-a731-1c1dea4323a8">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for both insured individuals to be alive at the first death does not affect the right to cancel the policy within 30 days for a full refund. These provisions function independently—one applies after the first death, the other before any claims occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="345bacdf-c40e-4c15-8bf5-2e2379dbd9d6" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">depends_on</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f6cacafe-5d3a-4346-9c65-c66588be307b" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">requires both insured individuals to be alive at time of first death</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="a5054672-b4af-483e-aedf-07b59bfac1b1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="49d76ec4-c1c5-4793-9b01-bffa5e79d1fb">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="12af506a-0bdc-4271-a8d9-d0299cda3146">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="493d9437-ca07-436c-a548-55d34267fd0e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="8094cbc7-8560-45fb-8fb3-3b5b2c90121a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="de886d6c-59cd-447d-9748-a6dbc40acfc2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="53889ee2-d6ea-4f29-b926-7a9c3119d5e9">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="b4070c2e-6358-4de1-b414-fba1c931f952">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="7efe32f5-6329-4c20-816d-169f87c9e803">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="c550ad5a-77bc-4e5d-9a75-b4d5c02ac28d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="5a1c0421-baf1-4c23-a791-8014bad95e9e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="9e8250a7-02ac-4108-9ce0-0cf4d548ffce">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d3">The split option's availability in cases of uncertain simultaneous deaths depends on actuarial and legal conditions unrelated to the set annual premium amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on when the split option may apply does not influence or relate to the requirement that premiums be paid annually on August 20th.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s split option applies only when both insureds die simultaneously under uncertain medical conditions. This exception has no bearing on the continued payment of premiums post-first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">The restriction on the split option to rare cases of uncertain simultaneity of death has no bearing on whether premium waiver benefits exist or do not apply under the policy’s terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">The availability of the split option during ambiguous dual-death events does not influence nor rely upon the existence of a 60-day grace period for missed premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">While the split provision requires sufficient cash value to support it, the availability of this option hinges on extreme events such as uncertain simultaneous deaths, not on the presence of guaranteed cash value alone.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">The split option applies only in highly unusual situations involving ambiguous cause-of-death scenarios, independent of the policy’s projected cash value growth.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">The availability of the split option during rare simultaneous-death scenarios does not affect or rely upon the cash value growth trajectory outlined in the projection.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">The split provision applies exclusively when both insureds die simultaneously and the cause of death cannot be determined medically—a highly unusual case unrelated to the standard two-year waiting period required before policy loans may be taken.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">The availability of the split option during ambiguous dual-death scenarios has no bearing on the percentage of cash surrender value that can be borrowed against through policy loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">Whether the policy can be split based on rare dual-death scenarios has no bearing on the applicable interest rate for policy loans, which remains independent of such structural options.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy is restricted to unusual situations involving simultaneous deaths with unclear causes, independent of whether loans have been taken out that affect the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">The split option's narrow applicability—limited to rare instances of uncertain simultaneity of death—is distinct from the general rule allowing loans anytime post-issuance. There is no direct causal or sequential link between them.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">The availability of the split option during uncertain simultaneous deaths does not depend on whether withdrawals are allowed. Instead, it hinges on survival status and proof of insurability, making its applicability independent of withdrawal rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">While the policy allows splitting after the first death, this right is restricted to exceptional situations involving uncertain cause or order of death, making the condition highly conditional.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEPTION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the split be exercised within two years of the first death applies only if the situation meets stringent criteria, including medical ambiguity around simultaneous deaths, making the window effectively unusable in most cases.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEPTION_TO_RULE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">The split option's limited availability ensures that actuarial allocation is only relevant in exceptional cases, not generally applicable across all splits.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 limits the split option to unusual circumstances such as uncertain simultaneous deaths, fact_sentence_1 imposes a broader precondition requiring both parties' survival at the moment of the first death. This creates inconsistency, suggesting the split may not apply even under those rare conditions unless additional criteria are met.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.1</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">The split option's availability during uncertain simultaneous deaths provides an exception to its typical use in divorce or trust adjustments, highlighting specialized application beyond standard estate planning.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCEPTION_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">The availability of the split option during uncertain simultaneous deaths does not influence the consequence of suicide within two years. These are independent clauses addressing different risk conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 defines a very specific scenario where the split option may apply, contributing to its low utilization. Fact_sentence_2 notes that the option is seldom used, consistent with it being limited to exceptional circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">The split option requires documentation proving continued insurability, meaning applicants must demonstrate they meet health standards despite uncertain causes of death. This ensures risk assessment remains viable post-split.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_REQUIREMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5a1c0421-baf1-4c23-a791-8014bad95e9e" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">governed_by</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9e8250a7-02ac-4108-9ce0-0cf4d548ffce" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">enables_condition_for</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="48d387bd-d247-4ad0-93a2-511737d45761">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="6c6304c6-f755-453e-992f-b191a97284b3">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="07d52d6e-5d6e-4a09-ac80-1e74e422997c">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">DATE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="e9870dd1-5766-4cce-bff7-89f9a0bd572b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="2a525733-b3a4-4ae8-a88d-6b39f7aedf76">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="6d600bb4-69e4-4ea4-8c89-05e2462d8139">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="e976856d-bee2-4515-aa41-7f0253853488">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="1ccecc45-de7c-44a2-baa6-be331166b216">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">MONETARY_VALUE</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="ac167ef1-f7ea-475c-b224-87d4b74c87ea">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="00bbf226-dd42-4b82-bdc5-0ee83530983c">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="9a69de57-6659-4e60-a7bf-58c5132f6289">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="b5d09cd6-b30f-4e98-8e00-e02ee67ce3f4">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">EXCLUSION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d3">While the need for evidence of insurability pertains to a future administrative step (policy splitting), it relies on the existence of an active policy maintained through regular payments, including the stated annual premium of $48,600.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">The condition requiring evidence of insurability applies only when attempting to split the policy after the first death; without prior compliance with premium obligations, such an action would not be possible.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability arises specifically when considering the policy split after the first death, which only becomes relevant once premiums continue at the original rate beyond that point.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">Requiring evidence of insurability when splitting the policy ensures that surviving parties meet health standards to qualify for new individual coverage. This condition exists independently of whether premium waivers apply, as it relates to underwriting rules post-split rather than ongoing premium obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">Providing evidence of insurability is necessary when splitting the policy, so consistent premium payments—even through a grace period—are important to maintain active status and avoid lapses that could jeopardize eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSARY FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">Requiring evidence of insurability to split the policy implies that the policy’s built-up cash value must meet certain thresholds, reinforcing its role in supporting long-term guarantees.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">The necessity of providing evidence of insurability arises when attempting to split the policy, typically triggered by events like the first death. While unrelated to immediate cash value projections, this requirement aligns with the longer-term structural design that includes milestones such as year 10 valuation.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability when splitting the policy underscores a conditionality linked to underwriting standards; it does not affect the calculation or validity of the cash value projection made at year 20.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.4</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">Requiring evidence of insurability for the split option implies that underwriting checks occur early, possibly affecting whether borrowers qualify for loans simultaneously.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL ON TIME</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">Requiring evidence of insurability ensures eligibility for splitting the policy, independent of how much one can borrow against the cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">While evidence of insurability is necessary to exercise the split feature, it does not affect the existing loan interest rate, which operates independently based on market conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.25</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability during the split process ensures continued coverage validity, regardless of any previous loans reducing the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_REQUIREMENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">The need for evidence of insurability occurs only when splitting the policy after the first death, which is unrelated to the general availability of policy loans, even though both relate to post-first-death actions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">Requiring evidence of insurability for the split option reflects an administrative safeguard consistent with restrictions like prohibiting partial withdrawals, ensuring only qualified parties can modify coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">RELATED_TO</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">Providing evidence of insurability enables the policyholder to exercise the right to split the policy post-first-death.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_ACTION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">Providing evidence of insurability is contingent upon acting within the specified window after the first death, ensuring compliance with the policy’s conditions for splitting.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">Providing evidence of insurability is a prerequisite that allows the split to proceed, enabling the subsequent actuarial allocation of face amounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">Providing evidence of insurability is contingent upon both individuals surviving the first death, as this prerequisite determines whether the split process can even begin.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">The need for evidence of insurability adds a barrier to using the split option, potentially contributing to its infrequent exercise.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability ensures that the split option can be exercised safely under circumstances such as divorce or trust changes, aligning procedural conditions with real-world applications.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXEMPLIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">Since the split option is limited to exceptional situations such as ambiguous simultaneous deaths, requiring evidence of insurability adds an administrative safeguard during high-risk claims processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS_APPLICABILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability during the split option ensures continued coverage validity post-split, whereas the suicide clause prevents payouts if death occurs by suicide early in the policy term. These provisions operate independently but contribute to overall policy risk management.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for evidence of insurability during a policy split could affect decisions about taking loans, as accumulated debt reduces available death benefits and might jeopardize qualification for favorable split outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">Evidence of insurability is needed to split the policy after the first death—a scenario that precedes the final payout condition outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECONDITION_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">The need for evidence of insurability during the split process ensures that the policy maintains viability for estate tax liquidity objectives even after one insured passes.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">Estate planning uses include splitting the policy after the first death, contingent on providing evidence of insurability, ensuring continued financial flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
