<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="a9e7f4af-ec56-47d8-ac60-93deb168dbf1">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a split option tailored for divorce or trust changes underscores the need for substantial, stable funding—such as the consistent $48,600 annual premium—to maintain coverage integrity post-split.</data>
  <data key="d4">FINANCIAL_SUPPORT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="2461f012-1c2a-4b80-84ff-a70ea9af51ba">
  <data key="d3">The existence of the split option supports complex estate planning needs, including divorce or trust adjustments, which rely on consistent premium payments maintaining policy validity over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="1ec93897-4582-467c-9df8-bc0d20aec783">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy after the first death serves practical purposes in estate planning, including divorce or trust adjustments, which relies on continued premium payments to maintain policy validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">PURPOSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="3b80d1cc-14b1-44a5-b6e4-b4d970384d8d">
  <data key="d3">While the split option enables adjustments during major life events like divorce or trust changes, it operates independently of whether premium waivers apply, meaning its existence isn't contingent upon that provision being present.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="3e0929d5-298d-4dde-8125-af7d9ada617a">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy supports major life event planning, including divorce or trust changes. Such strategic uses rely on maintaining active coverage, making timely premium payments—and thus grace periods—important safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="76304af0-638b-4ac0-813d-d9e1573697f3">
  <data key="d3">While the split option exists primarily for legal transitions like divorce or trust changes, its functionality relies on the underlying cash value being sufficient and accessible through loan provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="6dc8ff62-eea3-490e-8bcb-f8de9a7857c7">
  <data key="d3">The split option exists primarily to accommodate significant personal or legal changes, such as divorce or trust adjustments, making it relevant when considering how the policy’s accumulated cash value might be reallocated.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES USE CASE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="c572616e-c975-4080-b949-ca3f8247c18e">
  <data key="d3">The split option exists primarily to facilitate major life transitions such as divorce or trust restructuring, making it relevant when considering long-term financial goals supported by substantial cash value growth, including the projected $712,000 after 20 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">STRATEGIC RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="09895f11-033a-47ca-8643-e10cf716e712">
  <data key="d3">The split option serves specific estate planning purposes like divorce or trust modifications, often triggered around the second year post-issuance when sufficient cash value exists, making it relevant that loans are already available by then.</data>
  <data key="d4">PURPOSE_CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="d94c663a-259e-482b-a866-3027a5c20ec9">
  <data key="d3">The split option’s design for divorce or trust changes reflects practical application where access to cash through policy loans could support transitional financial arrangements, making the loan limit relevant to implementation feasibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLING_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.55</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="344050b8-4052-4992-8796-fb1bb3c2e00a">
  <data key="d3">The split option exists primarily to allow reconfiguration of coverage in major life transitions like divorce or trust adjustments, whereas the loan interest rate influences how costly it may be to access funds during those periods, indirectly supporting long-term plan adaptability.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDIRECTLY_RELATED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="9c47d13a-d692-4392-baa2-0c2fae92d3d2">
  <data key="d3">The split option’s utility in estate planning contexts justifies careful management of benefits, including understanding that loans directly diminish the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="0ac06249-c2b3-4788-84f9-796a3b669e1f">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a split option for divorce or trust modifications does not affect whether policy loans are permitted before or after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="0df8a60d-2dd5-49e0-a026-86763abbc127">
  <data key="d3">The availability of the split option allows beneficiaries to adjust coverage without accessing cash, circumventing the need for withdrawals—which are otherwise disallowed by policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">The split option exists so that beneficiaries can manage assets independently post-first-death, particularly useful during major life events like divorce or trust reorganization.</data>
  <data key="d4">SERVES USE CASE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">The need for prompt action within two years stems from its use in sensitive legal transitions where delayed decisions could jeopardize estate plans.</data>
  <data key="d4">PURPOSE_DRIVES_TIMING</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="c0978b9e-d3be-4833-93c7-b90a6f87d86b">
  <data key="d3">The need to modify estate plans via divorce or trust changes drives the requirement for an equitable division of benefits through actuarial allocation when splitting the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">DRIVES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">Because the split option is primarily designed for divorce or trust changes, it includes the requirement that both parties remain alive at the time of the first death to maintain validity under those circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">PURPOSE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="6423aae2-3458-45ed-a68e-9f42cae005bf">
  <data key="d3">While designed mainly for divorce or trust changes, the split option may occasionally apply when multiple deaths occur simultaneously and cause medical ambiguity, extending its utility beyond routine estate restructuring.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRIMARY_PURPOSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">Since the split option is primarily used during major life events like divorce or trust adjustments, it logically requires documentation proving continued eligibility, hence the necessity of evidence of insurability.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="47f15981-6589-47fa-8b46-dc246096d7cb">
  <data key="d3">Because the split option is designed specifically for high-stakes legal transitions like divorce or trust changes, its limited real-world need results in infrequent use.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="7de08c0f-b0ef-4ad9-9926-43321fd05070">
  <data key="d3">The split option allows for policy restructuring under specific legal circumstances such as divorce or trust changes. This feature operates independently of the suicide exclusion clause, which applies regardless of how the policy is later modified.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="69f86d86-8dc3-4e5c-963e-490edef23e72">
  <data key="d3">The split option enables dividing the policy after the first death, making the impact of existing loans on the reduced death benefit particularly important during such legal or estate adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">AFFECTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a split option supports the operational framework outlined in fact_sentence_1 by providing a mechanism to restructure the policy after the first death, ensuring continued financial utility even without immediate payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy after the first death enables adaptive estate planning, directly supporting liquidity needs tied to estate taxes when beneficiaries change or assets are restructured.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">The split option, intended for divorce or trust changes, supports the broader estate planning function emphasized in fact_sentence_1 by allowing flexible reconfiguration of coverage after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c">
  <data key="d3">The split option's applicability depends on ownership status defined by the trust, meaning it only triggers if one or both parties hold ownership rights as specified in the trust document.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="dc5e7101-a50d-4b25-8d7d-9d2fc8fab9fc">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy post-first-death aligns with trust modification purposes, reinforcing why external assignment requires trustee consent to maintain proper fiduciary oversight.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5">
  <data key="d3">The split option enables restructuring the policy post-first-death under circumstances like divorce or trust change, while the 30-day cancellation window offers an initial safeguard before commitment, supporting decision-making flexibility during high-stakes transitions.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f" target="510a4351-8c5a-44d4-a731-1c1dea4323a8">
  <data key="d3">The ability to split the policy after the first death supports long-term estate restructuring, whereas the 30-day refund option enables immediate withdrawal without consequence, offering complementary risk mitigation strategies at different lifecycle stages.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
