<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="0e2a9ecc-868a-4aca-b4bf-6a2a9f7aaf67">
  <data key="d3">If suicide occurs within two years of the policy's issue date, the insurer is obligated to limit the death benefit to only the premiums paid, reflecting the terms of the suicide clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="f538df8c-2601-4974-8850-9d2d91ce5a45">
  <data key="d3">If the suicide clause was previously active due to a suicide attempt within two years of issuance, its effect may be nullified by reinstating the policy, effectively resetting the clock on when future suicides would trigger the clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">RESETS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="5ddd660e-ea55-4c09-9860-50f4685212cf">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause governs payout eligibility when suicide occurs within two years of issuance, independent of external perils like war. This statement does not relate to exclusion policies regarding specific events such as war.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="e27a52b8-188d-412d-9f06-85f8d10702af">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause governs payout eligibility when suicide occurs within two years of issuance, independent of exclusion types like aviation. This statement does not relate to whether aviation risks affect claim outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="2f712e42-84e9-4a28-8287-c5f42eb77b74">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes a limitation based on suicidal behavior within two years of issuance, while fact sentence 2 addresses potential invalidation due to false statements made at application. Both apply concurrently during the first two years, creating overlapping grounds for denying benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCURRENTLY APPLIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause restricts benefits if suicide occurs within two years of issuance, regardless of the surviving insured's status. This condition operates separately from contestability rules tied to the living status of both insured individuals.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="680677b4-fab3-4a38-a25f-337b518d62e9">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause governs payout eligibility when suicide occurs within two years of issuance, independent of any exclusion policies like those involving travel. This statement does not reference or rely on information about travel exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="a08544cf-1d57-4a48-8d71-04334028f70e">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause determines payout eligibility if suicide occurs within two years of issuance, independent of ownership. This policy being held in an irrevocable trust governs who controls the policy and how proceeds are distributed, without affecting the suicide clause’s trigger condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause governs payout eligibility based on timing of suicide, independent of the trust’s role in estate exclusion. It does not influence or depend on the reason for using an irrevocable trust.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="cfb8aedd-4fff-4a62-9b3c-d67d3494a301">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause determines whether claims are paid when death occurs by suicide within two years, independent of trust structure. However, the trust’s proper setup affects estate taxation regardless of cause of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="c9ecaa63-c7f5-4e1a-97c6-6bbc471e2191">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause restricts payout eligibility if death occurs by suicide within two years, while the trust structure ensures that even if benefits are payable, they avoid inclusion in the deceased’s taxable estate. These provisions operate independently yet cohesively within the overall risk management and estate planning strategy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="99362e2f-7a54-4ae7-98a5-155295fe1f90">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause defines payout limitations under specific circumstances involving death by suicide within two years, but it does not directly inform the need for legal consultation on Crummey powers during trust transfers.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.3</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="0a3b7fc9-2243-4755-a015-279702ce91e9">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause governs payout eligibility after suicide within two years of issuance, independent of estate planning strategies like annual gifting. This factual statement does not inform nor rely on advice regarding gift planning.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="cd2b5513-fe2d-4b70-b48a-c2748515cd09">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause governs benefit eligibility if one insured dies by suicide within two years of issuance. This scenario is unrelated to simultaneous deaths caused by accidents, where separate rules apply regardless of intent or timeline.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="6855c874-b03e-4cfa-b68c-37e56182aa7f">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause governs payout eligibility based on timing relative to the policy’s issue date, influencing overall coverage validity. This consideration becomes relevant when assessing whether transferring the policy to a trust complies with estate planning regulations like the three-year lookback rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 describes a limitation on payout based on suicide occurring within two years of issuance. This condition operates independently of whether multiple insureds die simultaneously, though it may influence eligibility when combined with other events.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause triggers when suicide occurs within two years of issuance, and since the Trust owns the policy, it manages claim determinations related to this clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTROLS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="2a7bb337-8c7a-449a-afa2-d4bb6e199209">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause governs payout eligibility based on time since issuance but does not affect the trust’s administrative control over beneficiary changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_EFFECT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause determines payout eligibility when suicide occurs within two years of issuance, independent of who holds decision-making power over beneficiaries. This condition does not influence or depend on the trustee’s ability to name beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="115deb5a-9af7-4024-bf11-8dba457cef0b">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause determines benefit eligibility under specific conditions related to time since issuance, whereas the trust’s power to assign the policy arises from its sole ownership status, independent of claim triggers like suicide.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
