<edge source="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659" target="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f">
  <data key="d3">The suicide clause restricts payouts if suicide occurs within two years, while the Trust’s power to surrender allows it to terminate the policy entirely. This means the Trust could prevent any claim arising from suicide by canceling the policy prior to the two-year period expiring.</data>
