<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659">
  <data key="d3">Contestability depends on both insureds being alive at the time of claim, limiting challenges by insurers after one dies. It does not affect how the suicide clause functions, which hinges solely on the timeline relative to the policy start.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="0e2a9ecc-868a-4aca-b4bf-6a2a9f7aaf67">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 outlines the condition under which contestability remains enforceable — specifically, while both insureds are alive. This has no bearing on how the suicide clause determines benefit payouts, which hinges on timing relative to policy issuance rather than survivorship. Therefore, the two statements address separate legal mechanisms without mutual dependence.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="f538df8c-2601-4974-8850-9d2d91ce5a45">
  <data key="d3">Whether contestability ends after one insured dies does not affect how or when the suicide clause resets during reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="2f712e42-84e9-4a28-8287-c5f42eb77b74">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that both insureds must be alive for contestability to apply narrows the effective timeframe of the two-year contestability period originally established in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">LIMITS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="5ddd660e-ea55-4c09-9860-50f4685212cf">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 discusses the timing condition under which contestability applies based on the life status of the insureds. This does not relate to whether war exclusions exist, which is addressed separately in fact sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="e27a52b8-188d-412d-9f06-85f8d10702af">
  <data key="d3">The first statement concerns when contestability periods remain active based on the living status of both insured parties. This does not relate to whether aviation exclusions apply, which is governed by separate underwriting rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="680677b4-fab3-4a38-a25f-337b518d62e9">
  <data key="d3">The statement about contestability during the lifetime of both insureds does not relate to whether travel exclusions exist in the policy. They address separate operational features without causal or sequential connection.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="a08544cf-1d57-4a48-8d71-04334028f70e">
  <data key="d3">The contestability condition depends on the living status of both insured parties but does not directly interact with the policy’s ownership by an irrevocable trust. The trust ownership defines control structures separate from survivorship-based clauses.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="c9ecaa63-c7f5-4e1a-97c6-6bbc471e2191">
  <data key="d3">The condition that contestability ends when either insured dies supports the broader goal of ensuring trust-distributed proceeds remain excluded from estate taxation by confirming clear timing rules around claim validity.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a">
  <data key="d3">Contestability being limited to when both insureds are alive ensures claims cannot be contested after one dies, aligning with the intent to protect beneficiaries. This condition supports the broader goal of using the trust to avoid estate taxes by ensuring clear beneficiary control post-death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="99362e2f-7a54-4ae7-98a5-155295fe1f90">
  <data key="d3">The statement about contestability duration depends on both insureds being alive but does not address the need for legal consultation regarding Crummey powers during trust transfers.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="cd2b5513-fe2d-4b70-b48a-c2748515cd09">
  <data key="d3">The contestability period depends on both individuals being alive, but if they die together under ambiguous circumstances, the immediate payment provision overrides standard claims processing timelines.</data>
  <data key="d4">OVERLAPS WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="cfb8aedd-4fff-4a62-9b3c-d67d3494a301">
  <data key="d3">The applicability of contestability depends on both insureds being alive, ensuring claims cannot be contested post-death unless conditions are met. This does not directly affect the need for proper trust structuring to exclude proceeds from estates.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="0a3b7fc9-2243-4755-a015-279702ce91e9">
  <data key="d3">The contestability period depends on both insureds being alive, but this condition does not influence the need to consult an attorney regarding annual exclusion gifts for policy transfers.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
