<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="6855c874-b03e-4cfa-b68c-37e56182aa7f">
  <data key="d3">The first statement outlines the duration of contestability based on the joint survival of insured parties, whereas the second emphasizes the need for legal guidance regarding the three-year lookback rule when placing the policy in a trust. These statements operate in separate domains—one regulatory (contestability)—and one procedural (trust transfer).</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea">
  <data key="d3">The contestability period depends on both individuals being alive, so when their deaths occur within 30 days, it triggers a special treatment under claims rules, potentially affecting how contestability was enforced prior to death.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
