<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b">
  <data key="d3">Contestability depends on both insureds being alive, but this does not affect the Trust’s ability to designate beneficiaries independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="2a7bb337-8c7a-449a-afa2-d4bb6e199209">
  <data key="d3">Contestability being limited to when both insureds are alive defines a condition affecting claim validity, whereas the Trust’s ability to change beneficiaries reflects ongoing administrative control regardless of insurable interest duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="115deb5a-9af7-4024-bf11-8dba457cef0b">
  <data key="d3">Contestability being limited to when both insureds are alive defines a condition affecting claim validity early in the policy term. This does not directly influence the Trust’s ability to assign the policy, which stems from its role as sole owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
