</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="e3e49333-4660-4170-be0e-750c514619c6">
  <data key="d3">The condition that contestability ends when either insured dies does not affect the requirement for trustee authorization in assigning the policy. Assignment remains governed by trust rules regardless of contestability status.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010" target="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba">
  <data key="d3">The condition that contestability applies only when both insureds are alive operates within a framework where ownership is exclusively held by the trust, meaning individual rights do not override policy rules during the contestability period.</data>
