<edge source="5ddd660e-ea55-4c09-9860-50f4685212cf" target="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a">
  <data key="d3">The lack of war exclusions ensures broad coverage, supporting the use of the policy within an irrevocable trust to protect assets and exclude proceeds from taxable estates by maintaining robust, unrestricted life insurance benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ddd660e-ea55-4c09-9860-50f4685212cf" target="c9ecaa63-c7f5-4e1a-97c6-6bbc471e2191">
  <data key="d3">The absence of war exclusions ensures continuous coverage under extreme circumstances, indirectly supporting the goal of ensuring proceeds are available for distribution via the trust without reduction. This supports the intent behind excluding proceeds from taxable estates.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ddd660e-ea55-4c09-9860-50f4685212cf" target="cfb8aedd-4fff-4a62-9b3c-d67d3494a301">
  <data key="d3">The absence of war exclusions ensures broad coverage under the policy, supporting its utility in diverse scenarios. However, even with comprehensive coverage, the tax treatment of proceeds depends entirely on correct trust structuring, making compliance essential regardless of coverage scope.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
