</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="0e2a9ecc-868a-4aca-b4bf-6a2a9f7aaf67">
  <data key="d3">Holding the policy in an irrevocable trust ensures that death benefits are excluded from the insured’s taxable estate, fulfilling a key estate planning goal. This arrangement does not affect how the suicide clause determines benefit amounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="f538df8c-2601-4974-8850-9d2d91ce5a45">
  <data key="d3">Holding the policy in an irrevocable trust ensures that death benefits are excluded from the insured’s taxable estate, fulfilling estate planning goals. This structural choice has no bearing on whether the suicide clause resets during reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="2f712e42-84e9-4a28-8287-c5f42eb77b74">
  <data key="d3">Holding the policy in an irrevocable trust aims to exclude proceeds from the insured’s taxable estate. This structural choice has no bearing on whether the policy can be contested for misrepresentation during the initial two-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010">
  <data key="d3">Holding the policy in an irrevocable trust prevents inclusion in the insureds’ taxable estates, enabling long-term wealth transfer goals. This structural choice does not affect the timing or applicability of contestability rules based on survivorship.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="5ddd660e-ea55-4c09-9860-50f4685212cf">
  <data key="d3">Holding the policy in an irrevocable trust aims to exclude proceeds from taxable estates, making it essential that coverage remains intact under all circumstances—including those involving war-related risks—thus justifying the absence of war exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="e27a52b8-188d-412d-9f06-85f8d10702af">
  <data key="d3">Holding the policy in an irrevocable trust serves the strategic purpose of estate avoidance, ensuring beneficiaries receive full proceeds free of taxation. This structural choice supports robust coverage, including the lack of aviation exclusions, to preserve asset transfer integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="680677b4-fab3-4a38-a25f-337b518d62e9">
  <data key="d3">Holding the policy in an irrevocable trust prevents inclusion of death benefits in the insured’s taxable estate, independent of whether travel exclusions exist.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="a08544cf-1d57-4a48-8d71-04334028f70e">
  <data key="d3">To achieve exclusion from taxable estates, the policy is intentionally held within an irrevocable trust, removing direct ownership by any individual beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">PURPOSE_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="cfb8aedd-4fff-4a62-9b3c-d67d3494a301">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of proceeds from taxable estates depends entirely on maintaining correct trust structures and adherence to legal requirements such as the three-year lookback rule and Crummey powers.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="c9ecaa63-c7f5-4e1a-97c6-6bbc471e2191">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states the goal of using an irrevocable trust: to prevent estate taxation. This directly supports fact_sentence_2, which affirms that the resulting payout to the trust avoids inclusion in the insureds’ estates.</data>
  <data key="d4">PURPOSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="6855c874-b03e-4cfa-b68c-37e56182aa7f">
  <data key="d3">The use of an irrevocable trust aims to remove policy proceeds from taxable estates, but this requires careful adherence to IRS regulations like the three-year lookback rule, making consultation with an estate planning attorney essential to avoid disqualification.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="99362e2f-7a54-4ae7-98a5-155295fe1f90">
  <data key="d3">The use of an irrevocable trust aims to exclude policy proceeds from taxable estates, but this requires adherence to specific legal mechanisms like Crummey powers. Therefore, consulting an estate planning attorney ensures those conditions are properly met during the transfer process.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="0a3b7fc9-2243-4755-a015-279702ce91e9">
  <data key="d3">The use of an irrevocable trust aims to remove policy proceeds from the insured’s taxable estate, but doing so properly depends on adherence to federal gift tax rules, necessitating consultation with an estate planning attorney for compliant annual gifting strategies.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
