  <data key="d3">The trust's power to designate beneficiaries enables it to manage distribution according to estate planning goals, such as excluding proceeds from the insured’s taxable estate.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea">
  <data key="d3">The use of an irrevocable trust aims to remove policy proceeds from taxable estates, while the simultaneous death provision ensures prompt payment if both insureds die close together. These provisions serve different administrative and legal functions within the policy’s structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="2a7bb337-8c7a-449a-afa2-d4bb6e199209">
  <data key="d3">The trust's ability to change beneficiaries ensures flexibility in estate planning, allowing adjustments to align with current intentions while maintaining exclusion from the insured’s taxable estate.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="115deb5a-9af7-4024-bf11-8dba457cef0b">
  <data key="d3">The trust owns the policy to exclude it from the insured’s taxable estate, and this structural arrangement grants the trust the power to assign the policy as needed to preserve its intended tax treatment.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a" target="f8fdda5e-551c-4714-929d-a06d99b71f24">
  <data key="d3">The trust's authority to take policy loans enables it to manage the policy effectively, supporting the long-term viability of excluding proceeds from taxable estates by preserving the policy’s intended structure under IRS rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
