<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes rules for handling joint deaths by treating them as simultaneous if within 30 days. This determination affects claim disbursement but does not interact directly with the suicide clause’s timing requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="0e2a9ecc-868a-4aca-b4bf-6a2a9f7aaf67">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 specifies conditions under which multiple deaths result in immediate benefit payment. Fact sentence 1 details the reduced payout when suicide triggers a claim during the initial two years.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="f538df8c-2601-4974-8850-9d2d91ce5a45">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 specifies when deaths are considered simultaneous for payout eligibility, independent of any provisions about suicide or policy reinstatement. This scenario has no bearing on whether the suicide clause resets.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="2f712e42-84e9-4a28-8287-c5f42eb77b74">
  <data key="d3">The second fact outlines the condition under which dual deaths are considered simultaneous for benefit distribution. It has no bearing on whether the policy was issued with misrepresented information.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010">
  <data key="d3">When both insureds die within 30 days, their simultaneous death designation overrides ongoing conditions like contestability, meaning the requirement for both to be alive becomes moot once the event occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS_RELEVANCE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="5ddd660e-ea55-4c09-9860-50f4685212cf">
  <data key="d3">The simultaneous death rule determines how claims are processed when lives end closely in time, regardless of cause—including potentially war-related causes. This does not affect whether war exclusions exist.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="e27a52b8-188d-412d-9f06-85f8d10702af">
  <data key="d3">When two insureds die within 30 days, the policy treats their deaths as simultaneous, enabling immediate benefit payment. This provision operates separately from whether certain risks like aviation are excluded.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="680677b4-fab3-4a38-a25f-337b518d62e9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines the rules for determining simultaneous death when two insured individuals pass away close together. This provision operates independently of whether travel exclusions exist.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="a08544cf-1d57-4a48-8d71-04334028f70e">
  <data key="d3">The provision allowing immediate payment when both insureds die within 30 days has no bearing on who owns the policy. It pertains strictly to claim settlement procedures rather than ownership or governance structures.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a">
  <data key="d3">The simultaneous death clause guarantees immediate payout when both insureds die within 30 days, independent of estate planning goals. This outcome complements the trust's role in asset protection by enabling swift distribution per the trust terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIES_WITH</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="c9ecaa63-c7f5-4e1a-97c6-6bbc471e2191">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 outlines the condition under which claims are processed as simultaneous deaths, affecting payout timing. This has no bearing on whether proceeds are included in estates, which depends instead on trust structure and gift rules detailed in fact sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="cfb8aedd-4fff-4a62-9b3c-d67d3494a301">
  <data key="d3">Simultaneous death treatment enables immediate benefit payment regardless of order, irrespective of trust-related requirements for estate exclusion.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="6855c874-b03e-4cfa-b68c-37e56182aa7f">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence explains that concurrent deaths within 30 days result in immediate benefit payment. This outcome is independent of whether the policy was properly structured under the lookback rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="99362e2f-7a54-4ae7-98a5-155295fe1f90">
  <data key="d3">Simultaneous death provisions determine immediate payout eligibility regardless of timing, independent of whether Crummey powers were properly implemented during trust transfer.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="0a3b7fc9-2243-4755-a015-279702ce91e9">
  <data key="d3">The simultaneous death clause governs how benefits are paid when multiple parties die closely in time, independent of gift planning strategies discussed in relation to annual exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="cd2b5513-fe2d-4b70-b48a-c2748515cd09">
  <data key="d3">The rule allowing immediate payout upon simultaneous death relies on determining whether both individuals died within a 30-day period, establishing the basis for treating them as dying at the same time.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b">
  <data key="d3">When both insureds die within 30 days, their deaths are deemed simultaneous, enabling immediate benefit payment. This triggers the need for clear beneficiary designation by the Trust, ensuring timely disbursement according to pre-established terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="2a7bb337-8c7a-449a-afa2-d4bb6e199209">
  <data key="d3">The scenario where both insureds die within 30 days triggers automatic simultaneous-death rules, ensuring prompt payment. This outcome does not influence the Trust’s ability to alter beneficiaries, which remains governed by separate administrative provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af">
  <data key="d3">When both insureds die within 30 days, their deaths are considered simultaneous, triggering immediate benefit payment. This outcome depends on the policy’s terms being enforced by the designated owner—the Trust—which manages disbursement according to its governing provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTROLS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="115deb5a-9af7-4024-bf11-8dba457cef0b">
  <data key="d3">The rule about treating deaths as simultaneous does not affect the Trust’s ability to assign the policy. Assignment rights remain governed by the trust agreement regardless of death timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="f8fdda5e-551c-4714-929d-a06d99b71f24">
  <data key="d3">When both insureds die within 30 days, their deaths are deemed simultaneous, leading to immediate benefit payment. This outcome operates independently of the Trust’s ability to secure policy loans, which remains unaffected by the timing of death events.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f">
  <data key="d3">When both insureds die within 30 days, their deaths are deemed simultaneous, leading to immediate benefit payment. This outcome occurs under the Trust’s complete control, which retains the legal right to surrender the policy at any time, independent of death events.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENTLY SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="e3e49333-4660-4170-be0e-750c514619c6">
  <data key="d3">The simultaneous death rule determines how benefits are paid when multiple insureds pass close together, but it does not affect who may assign the policy. Assignment remains subject to trustee approval regardless of death timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO RELATIONSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea" target="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes how overlapping deaths trigger immediate payout eligibility. This outcome is independent of whether individuals hold ownership rights, making it conditionally relevant but not causally dependent on the ownership status described in sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
