  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="adf6600b-b103-4386-b320-5e6d66274692">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659">
  <data key="d3">Because the Trust is the sole owner of the policy, it determines whether the suicide clause applies during claims handling, particularly regarding timelines post-issue.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="0e2a9ecc-868a-4aca-b4bf-6a2a9f7aaf67">
  <data key="d3">Ownership of the policy by the Trust establishes administrative authority over claim disbursement, ensuring compliance with provisions like the suicide clause, which caps payouts at returned premiums when applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="f538df8c-2601-4974-8850-9d2d91ce5a45">
  <data key="d3">Ownership by the Trust determines control over policy actions like assignments and surrenders but does not affect how the suicide clause behaves when the policy is reinstated.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="2f712e42-84e9-4a28-8287-c5f42eb77b74">
  <data key="d3">The designation of the trust as the policy owner establishes centralized control over the policy’s terms and administration. This arrangement supports enforceability of conditions like contestability, ensuring consistent application across ownership and beneficiary frameworks.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTEXTUAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.35</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010">
  <data key="d3">The fact that the Trust is the policy owner establishes legal control over the policy’s administration, including surrender and assignment, but does not affect the timing or conditions under which contestability applies.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="5ddd660e-ea55-4c09-9860-50f4685212cf">
  <data key="d3">Ownership by the Trust determines who holds decision-making authority over the policy, including surrender and assignment rights. This structural detail does not influence whether war exclusions apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="e27a52b8-188d-412d-9f06-85f8d10702af">
  <data key="d3">Ownership by the trust determines authority over policy provisions such as exclusion clauses. As the designated owner, the trust has the power to maintain inclusive coverages like the absence of aviation exclusions, ensuring consistent application across beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTROLS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="680677b4-fab3-4a38-a25f-337b518d62e9">
  <data key="d3">Ownership by the trust establishes centralized control over the policy, including decisions about coverage and claims. This structural arrangement supports the inclusion of non-exclusionary provisions like no travel restrictions, ensuring consistent application across scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="a08544cf-1d57-4a48-8d71-04334028f70e">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 identifies the trust as the policy owner, which directly aligns with fact sentence 1 stating the policy is held by an irrevocable trust, reinforcing mutual consistency.</data>
  <data key="d4">IDENTICAL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a">
  <data key="d3">Ownership of the policy by the trust is essential to achieve the goal of excluding the death benefit from the insured’s taxable estate, aligning with estate preservation objectives.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="c9ecaa63-c7f5-4e1a-97c6-6bbc471e2191">
  <data key="d3">Because the trust holds ownership of the policy, it ensures that the death benefit does not become part of the insured’s taxable estate, fulfilling estate planning objectives.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSARY_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="cfb8aedd-4fff-4a62-9b3c-d67d3494a301">
  <data key="d3">Since the trust owns the policy, its proper structuring becomes critical to ensure the policy proceeds do not become part of the taxable estate.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="6855c874-b03e-4cfa-b68c-37e56182aa7f">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy is owned by the trust, it necessitates careful legal review—including adherence to the three-year lookback rule—to ensure compliant establishment and avoid adverse tax consequences.</data>
  <data key="d4">TRIGGERS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="99362e2f-7a54-4ae7-98a5-155295fe1f90">
  <data key="d3">Since the policy is owned by the trust, establishing correct Crummey powers becomes essential to maintain tax advantages and avoid disqualification under IRS rules related to gift transfers.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="0a3b7fc9-2243-4755-a015-279702ce91e9">
  <data key="d3">Because the policy is owned by a trust, any transfer-related gifting strategies must involve an estate planning attorney to ensure alignment with federal gift tax rules and proper documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="cd2b5513-fe2d-4b70-b48a-c2748515cd09">
  <data key="d3">Ownership by the Trust enables centralized control over policy functions, including how benefits are distributed, such as in cases of simultaneous death where prompt payout occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea">
  <data key="d3">The Trust is the sole owner of the policy and thus has final authority over claim distributions, including decisions related to simultaneous death scenarios where benefits are paid out promptly based on established clauses.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b">
  <data key="d3">Since the Trust holds sole ownership of the policy, it possesses the authority to determine who receives the death benefit by naming beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">OWNER_CONTROLS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="2a7bb337-8c7a-449a-afa2-d4bb6e199209">
  <data key="d3">As the policy owner, the Trust exercises complete authority over the policy’s terms, including the designation of beneficiaries. This reflects the central role of the Trust in managing the policy's administrative functions.</data>
  <data key="d4">OWNER_CONTROLS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="115deb5a-9af7-4024-bf11-8dba457cef0b">
  <data key="d3">Since the Trust is the designated policy owner, it holds comprehensive control over the policy’s disposition, including the ability to assign it to another party.</data>
  <data key="d4">OWNER_IMPLIES_RIGHT_TO_ASSIGN</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="f8fdda5e-551c-4714-929d-a06d99b71f24">
  <data key="d3">Since the Trust is the designated policy owner, it holds legal authority over all aspects of the policy, including the ability to access loan provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">OWNER_ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f">
  <data key="d3">As the designated policy owner, the Trust possesses comprehensive control over the policy’s lifecycle, including the power to terminate it via surrender.</data>
  <data key="d4">OWNER_IMPLIES_RIGHT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba">
  <data key="d3">Since the Trust owns the policy, it governs who may hold ownership rights. Individual insureds cannot claim such rights without explicit provisions within the trust document.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTROLS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af" target="e3e49333-4660-4170-be0e-750c514619c6">
  <data key="d3">Because the Trust is the sole owner of the policy, it retains control over key actions like assignment. Therefore, any such action must be authorized by the trustee who manages the Trust’s assets.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTROLS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="54c48f0b-f39d-45b0-914b-a5cc38b6d5a4" target="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">policy_owner</data>
</edge>
