  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659">
  <data key="d3">The trust’s authority to designate beneficiaries allows it to determine who receives proceeds regardless of the suicide clause’s terms, but this capability operates independently of whether the suicide event occurred within the exclusion period.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="0e2a9ecc-868a-4aca-b4bf-6a2a9f7aaf67">
  <data key="d3">The Trust possesses the power to designate beneficiaries, ensuring distribution aligns with estate planning goals regardless of whether the suicide clause affects the amount payable.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="f538df8c-2601-4974-8850-9d2d91ce5a45">
  <data key="d3">The trust's power to designate beneficiaries ensures distribution control regardless of claim triggers like suicide. However, this authority operates independently of whether the suicide clause has been reset post-reinstatement.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="2f712e42-84e9-4a28-8287-c5f42eb77b74">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s authority to designate beneficiaries reflects its comprehensive control over the policy, including administrative functions, which remains unaffected by the policy’s contestability period tied to misrepresentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s power to designate beneficiaries operates regardless of whether both insureds are alive, so it is independent of contestability rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="5ddd660e-ea55-4c09-9860-50f4685212cf">
  <data key="d3">The Trust's ability to designate beneficiaries underscores its governance role, whereas the lack of war exclusions defines the scope of covered events. Neither statement influences the validity or function of the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="e27a52b8-188d-412d-9f06-85f8d10702af">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s ability to designate beneficiaries operates independently of whether specific risks like aviation are excluded. Coverage breadth does not determine beneficiary assignment rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="680677b4-fab3-4a38-a25f-337b518d62e9">
  <data key="d3">The Trust's ability to designate beneficiaries stems from its sole ownership of the policy, whereas the lack of travel exclusions relates to risk coverage conditions. Neither statement influences the validity or function of the other.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="a08544cf-1d57-4a48-8d71-04334028f70e">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the trust to designate beneficiaries stems directly from its ownership of the policy, affirming its central role in managing the policy’s distribution provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTROLLED_BY_OWNER</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a">
  <data key="d3">Designating beneficiaries via the trust ensures alignment with estate tax avoidance strategies, fulfilling the core purpose of holding the policy within the trust.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPORTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="c9ecaa63-c7f5-4e1a-97c6-6bbc471e2191">
  <data key="d3">Because the trust controls beneficiary designations, it can ensure payouts bypass probate and estate taxation, thereby fulfilling the condition that proceeds remain excluded from the insured’s estate.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSARY_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="cfb8aedd-4fff-4a62-9b3c-d67d3494a301">
  <data key="d3">The trust’s power to designate beneficiaries is essential for maintaining the policy’s intended legal and tax status, supporting its exclusion from taxable estates.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSARY_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="6855c874-b03e-4cfa-b68c-37e56182aa7f">
  <data key="d3">The trust’s ability to designate beneficiaries reflects its comprehensive control over the policy, reinforcing why professional guidance is needed to navigate rules like the three-year lookback.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="99362e2f-7a54-4ae7-98a5-155295fe1f90">
  <data key="d3">The trust’s right to designate beneficiaries depends on correct structuring involving Crummey powers, making legal counsel essential during the transfer process.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="0a3b7fc9-2243-4755-a015-279702ce91e9">
  <data key="d3">The trust’s authority to designate beneficiaries enables it to fulfill its role in estate planning, particularly by ensuring that distributions comply with tax-exempt structures. This capability depends on prior steps such as correct gift transfers, which require consultation with an attorney.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="cd2b5513-fe2d-4b70-b48a-c2748515cd09">
  <data key="d3">The trust holds exclusive power to name beneficiaries, ensuring alignment with estate planning goals even if multiple deaths occur at once. This governance function supports timely execution of payouts described in case of simultaneous death.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea">
  <data key="d3">The Trust holds exclusive control over beneficiary designations, allowing it to determine who receives the benefit if multiple insureds die simultaneously within 30 days, thereby fulfilling the condition set forth in the simultaneous death provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af">
  <data key="d3">The ability of the Trust to designate beneficiaries stems directly from its role as the exclusive policy owner, granting it comprehensive control over key policy functions.</data>
  <data key="d4">DERIVED_FROM_OWNER</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="f8fdda5e-551c-4714-929d-a06d99b71f24">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s authority to designate beneficiaries ensures proper distribution of proceeds according to estate planning goals. This function operates independently of its capacity to access loan features tied to the policy’s cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="2a7bb337-8c7a-449a-afa2-d4bb6e199209">
  <data key="d3">The Trust's right to designate beneficiaries enables it to establish who receives the policy payout initially. This foundational authority supports its subsequent ability to modify those designations as needed.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="115deb5a-9af7-4024-bf11-8dba457cef0b">
  <data key="d3">The trust’s power to designate beneficiaries enables it to determine who receives the policy's proceeds, which complements its capacity to assign the policy to another party, ensuring alignment in transfer mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba">
  <data key="d3">The Trust's ability to designate beneficiaries stems directly from its exclusive ownership and control over the policy, which excludes any individual insured from holding ownership rights unless specified otherwise.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f">
  <data key="d3">The trust’s power to designate beneficiaries reflects its overarching control over distribution decisions, enabling it to determine who receives the death benefit. This authority complements its broader capacity to manage the policy's lifecycle, including surrendering it when necessary.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b" target="e3e49333-4660-4170-be0e-750c514619c6">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s ability to designate beneficiaries aligns with its broader power to manage policy transfers, requiring trustee approval for assignments to ensure consistent oversight and compliance with estate planning objectives.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="20b99518-51f9-4956-b8be-2ebb85c43c7a" target="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has_right_to_designate_beneficiaries</data>
</edge>
