  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f8fdda5e-551c-4714-929d-a06d99b71f24" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">Trust ownership allows it to manage financial tools such as policy loans, supporting sustained policy viability even when premiums remain fixed after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES_STABILITY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f8fdda5e-551c-4714-929d-a06d99b71f24" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">The trust’s right to take policy loans reflects its exclusive ownership and management power over the policy, allowing it to leverage cash value without affecting the fixed premium period established in the first ten years.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f8fdda5e-551c-4714-929d-a06d99b71f24" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">While the Trust may take policy loans, this capability does not influence or constrain the maximum annual premium set to $48,600 post-Year 10.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.15</data>
</edge>
<edge source="939e133c-1cbb-4e62-bd4e-1d0a9ed87569" target="f8fdda5e-551c-4714-929d-a06d99b71f24">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has_right_to_take_policy_loans</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="e4329806-b4bd-4c25-ac17-c53da1a1059d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="419266b5-1405-4ce3-8706-935db2db5bd3">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="f08691c5-4b30-4d92-b785-fd07f6cee5f0">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="b59d61d8-44f4-4449-8951-8d0963ca3b70">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ORGANIZATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="9b3f5394-748f-4639-a6c4-eb053f5340e7">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="79c1e1b2-f796-46f4-be8e-885fb135132a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="87e1fc59-13e9-4a01-a571-d8ea59ca9a7e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="e069521d-a75a-46d1-a85c-077207863818">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="fa552f08-2405-46ef-bb19-737fdf1eaf2f">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="bd02aad7-cbfd-494e-b854-f05d4320793e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s ability to surrender the policy gives it control over whether the policy remains active long enough for the suicide clause to apply, thereby indirectly influencing whether the clause becomes relevant.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="0e2a9ecc-868a-4aca-b4bf-6a2a9f7aaf67">
  <data key="d3">The trust’s right to surrender the policy exists independently of the suicide clause, meaning even if the clause reduces payouts, the trust retains administrative control over the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">NO_EFFECT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="f538df8c-2601-4974-8850-9d2d91ce5a45">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s authority to surrender the policy allows for potential reinstatement, which triggers the resetting of the suicide clause as specified in the terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="2f712e42-84e9-4a28-8287-c5f42eb77b74">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s ability to surrender the policy stems from its sole ownership, enabling it to manage policy actions without individual involvement. This authority exists regardless of whether the policy was subject to contestability earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="515adf3c-dada-471d-b601-2735aabcc010">
  <data key="d3">While the Trust may surrender the policy at any time per its controlling rights, this action does not affect the contestability period, which remains conditional on the continued existence of both insured individuals.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="5ddd660e-ea55-4c09-9860-50f4685212cf">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s power to surrender the policy enables it to act decisively on behalf of beneficiaries, consistent with the policy’s inclusive coverage features such as no war exclusions.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="e27a52b8-188d-412d-9f06-85f8d10702af">
  <data key="d3">Because the Trust possesses the legal right to surrender the policy, it maintains complete operational autonomy, including managing risk exposure related to activities like aviation, consistent with the policy’s inclusive terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">JUSTIFIED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="680677b4-fab3-4a38-a25f-337b518d62e9">
  <data key="d3">Because the Trust possesses the legal right to surrender the policy, the presence of no travel exclusions ensures such action does not trigger coverage gaps or invalidation related to travel risk.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONED_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="a08544cf-1d57-4a48-8d71-04334028f70e">
  <data key="d3">Because the trust possesses the right to surrender the policy, it confirms that the trust holds formal ownership and decision-making authority over the policy, consistent with being the sole owner.</data>
  <data key="d4">RIGHT_TO_SURRENDER_CONFIRMS_OWNERSHIP</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="09580835-e917-49b8-9fa3-3cd68120d06a">
  <data key="d3">The power to surrender the policy is necessary for the trust to maintain control and ensure that the life insurance proceeds remain outside the taxable estate, supporting the core purpose of the arrangement.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSARY_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="c9ecaa63-c7f5-4e1a-97c6-6bbc471e2191">
  <data key="d3">Because the trust may surrender the policy, it retains full administrative autonomy, allowing it to prevent the policy’s cash value or proceeds from being treated as part of the insured’s taxable estate under IRS guidelines.</data>
  <data key="d4">NECESSITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="cfb8aedd-4fff-4a62-9b3c-d67d3494a301">
  <data key="d3">The trust’s right to surrender the policy depends on being properly established and maintained, as improper structuring could invalidate such powers and jeopardize exclusion from taxable estates.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="6855c874-b03e-4cfa-b68c-37e56182aa7f">
  <data key="d3">The trust’s ability to surrender the policy underscores why it is essential to consult an estate planning attorney beforehand to ensure the transfer complies with rules like the three-year lookback, avoiding potential disallowance of the trust arrangement.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="99362e2f-7a54-4ae7-98a5-155295fe1f90">
  <data key="d3">The trust’s ability to surrender the policy underscores its exclusive ownership and operational control, making adherence to Crummey power requirements essential to maintain the validity of the arrangement.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="0a3b7fc9-2243-4755-a015-279702ce91e9">
  <data key="d3">The trust’s right to surrender the policy underscores why professional advice on annual exclusion gifts is essential—surrender decisions may trigger tax consequences requiring careful coordination with gift planning.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFORMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="cd2b5513-fe2d-4b70-b48a-c2748515cd09">
  <data key="d3">The Trust possesses the legal right to surrender the policy at any time before death. However, this power does not impact the automatic payout triggered by simultaneous death under the specified conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="21987369-76b8-41c2-b7e3-d85ed2ab6cea">
  <data key="d3">The Trust possesses the unilateral right to surrender the policy, reflecting its absolute ownership. This authority remains unaffected by whether the insureds died simultaneously within 30 days, ensuring operational continuity regardless of claim triggers.</data>
  <data key="d4">UNAFFECTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="4f7c58e0-735d-473c-8e8d-8a11b55b58af">
  <data key="d3">The Trust's right to surrender the policy stems directly from its status as the exclusive owner, reflecting its complete administrative and financial authority.</data>
  <data key="d4">RIGHT_FROM_OWNER</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b">
  <data key="d3">Surrendering the policy allows the trust to terminate coverage and access the accumulated cash value, reinforcing its role as the exclusive owner. This operational capability supports the trust’s ability to make beneficiary designations without interference from individuals.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="2a7bb337-8c7a-449a-afa2-d4bb6e199209">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s right to surrender the policy underscores its comprehensive control, enabling it to alter beneficiary designations without external interference.</data>
  <data key="d4">FACILITATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="115deb5a-9af7-4024-bf11-8dba457cef0b">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s right to surrender the policy underscores its complete ownership and operational control, which inherently includes the ability to assign the policy to another party if needed.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_BY</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="f8fdda5e-551c-4714-929d-a06d99b71f24">
  <data key="d3">Surrendering the policy represents a final disposition action enabled by the Trust’s ownership rights, which also include taking loans as interim financial tools during policy tenure.</data>
  <data key="d4">FOLLOWS_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba">
  <data key="d3">Because neither insured holds ownership rights, the Trust retains full control over policy decisions such as surrender. This structural arrangement ensures that only the Trust may exercise legal rights tied to ownership.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="e3e49333-4660-4170-be0e-750c514619c6">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s right to surrender the policy stems from its exclusive ownership and control, which necessitates trustee authorization for any transfer-related action like assignment.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRES_AUTHORIZATION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="c77b94e8-ba17-40c7-a87e-8036edb72fd7">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s requirement that the death benefit be paid only after the second insured passes does not prevent the Trust from surrendering the policy earlier; thus, the surrender right operates independently but may override the future payout conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONTRADICTS_IF_SURRENDERED</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s power to surrender the policy supports its role in estate planning by enabling controlled liquidation or modification without affecting beneficiaries’ inheritance goals.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENHANCES_PURPOSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="bfe9a0f3-fce1-4c16-a4f6-2a78f6d39acf">
  <data key="d3">Since the death benefit is payable only after both insureds die, the Trust’s power to surrender the policy gives it unilateral control over whether that eventuality leads to any payout, effectively allowing it to override the natural outcome dictated by the policy’s terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_CONTROL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s right to surrender the policy ensures operational control necessary to fulfill the policy’s primary purpose of providing estate tax liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">FULFILLS_PURPOSE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="e11b535f-c978-4ee3-a0fb-67b135406066">
  <data key="d3">The trust’s power to surrender the policy is meaningful in light of the delayed payout structure, allowing it to exit the contract before either death occurs, potentially avoiding future premium obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="4f649562-2015-4f25-ae81-7c5444b996c4">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s unilateral right to surrender the policy ensures it can terminate coverage even after the first insured’s death, regardless of the policy’s continued existence.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="9ff1d8f5-8894-4692-b73d-1e4ea24edfc5">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s authority to surrender the policy enables it to terminate coverage even after the first death, potentially affecting ongoing premium obligations despite the fixed rate during the initial term.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="5cdd5a6a-21a2-42b9-9024-4e7d8ff292a2">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s unilateral right to surrender the policy enables it to terminate coverage at any time, regardless of the fixed premium period, allowing strategic exit even before the end of the 10-year guarantee.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f" target="8aef280a-0c9a-40d3-968e-a753e7c3402f">
  <data key="d3">The Trust’s authority to surrender the policy means it can terminate the contract before maturity, potentially avoiding higher future premiums exceeding $48,600 annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b59d61d8-44f4-4449-8951-8d0963ca3b70" target="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has_right_to_surrender</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba" target="30ea5043-6ca4-4fde-ba58-cff8300ba25a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba" target="5b0b1981-0f69-4a15-88cd-eda00ce7ff13">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba" target="73c5c7a6-e3b5-4613-b9d5-59bd132ae12a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba" target="15a5cfca-b970-4aaa-9791-c1187dac955c">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">ORGANIZATION</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba" target="5e9c4a52-a676-410e-88b5-eda24b05207e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">PERSON</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba" target="69264e68-3656-4592-a9ef-0ccf181cdac5">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba" target="77737efe-9d92-4278-a622-dc6a8b7ddd00">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba" target="b5cbc19b-81aa-4da8-b13b-0842b1ee5a2d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba" target="6bd95749-892e-4f42-acce-6e707b014f68">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba" target="d3ff959c-832a-4869-bec2-a0c1c8c305a1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">CONCEPT</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba" target="5acf973b-a6fa-47ab-9191-07ee99127659">
  <data key="d3">Ownership rights are restricted to the trust’s framework, meaning individuals cannot exercise control regardless of claims like those triggered by suicide. The existence of such clauses doesn’t alter ownership limitations.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba" target="0e2a9ecc-868a-4aca-b4bf-6a2a9f7aaf67">
