<edge source="e3e49333-4660-4170-be0e-750c514619c6" target="46633fa0-bf8c-4c98-a98e-6ecc6e3c013b">
  <data key="d3">Since the Trust controls assignments through authorized trustees, it naturally retains the authority to designate beneficiaries, ensuring alignment with the trust's intended distribution goals.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3e49333-4660-4170-be0e-750c514619c6" target="2a7bb337-8c7a-449a-afa2-d4bb6e199209">
  <data key="d3">Since assignments require trustee consent, the Trust retains final authority over such decisions, enabling it to manage beneficiary changes accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENFORCES_CONTROL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3e49333-4660-4170-be0e-750c514619c6" target="115deb5a-9af7-4024-bf11-8dba457cef0b">
  <data key="d3">Authorization by the trustee is required before the Trust may exercise its right to assign the policy, reflecting delegated decision-making within the trust framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">REQUIRED_FOR</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3e49333-4660-4170-be0e-750c514619c6" target="f8fdda5e-551c-4714-929d-a06d99b71f24">
  <data key="d3">Requiring trustee authorization for policy assignment ensures that only actions aligned with trust governance proceed, which complements the Trust’s existing power to take policy loans without restriction.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3e49333-4660-4170-be0e-750c514619c6" target="8a12f494-7f87-46bf-8e19-a11973792e7f">
  <data key="d3">Authorization by the trustee is required for assignment because the Trust maintains sole ownership and operational control, including the power to surrender the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES_CONTROL</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3e49333-4660-4170-be0e-750c514619c6" target="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for trustee authorization to assign the policy stems directly from the absence of individual ownership rights, ensuring centralized control within the trust framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">DERIVES_FROM</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3e49333-4660-4170-be0e-750c514619c6" target="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for trustee authorization to assign the policy supports the assertion that ownership rests solely with the trust unless defined otherwise in its terms, reinforcing the restriction on individual ownership.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e3e49333-4660-4170-be0e-750c514619c6" target="dc5e7101-a50d-4b25-8d7d-9d2fc8fab9fc">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 states that policy assignment requires trustee authorization, which is reinforced and explicitly restated in fact_sentence_2, confirming that no assignment can occur without such consent.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
