<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="dc5e7101-a50d-4b25-8d7d-9d2fc8fab9fc">
  <data key="d3">If ownership is conditional on trust documentation, then any attempt to assign the policy without trustee consent would violate established governance rules, making such an action invalid under the terms outlined.</data>
  <data key="d4">MODIFIES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 defines the condition under which ownership exists, setting a prerequisite for any subsequent action involving the policy. Fact_sentence_2 outlines a procedural right available to the policyholder regardless of ownership status, specifically the ability to cancel within a defined window.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONS_RIGHT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="a81b97c9-146b-4343-9c7c-db9ffafb1f05">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence establishes that ownership depends on explicit wording in the trust document. The second sentence provides geographic information about the insurer but does not relate to ownership rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="510a4351-8c5a-44d4-a731-1c1dea4323a8">
  <data key="d3">Fact 1 defines the condition under which ownership arises, specifically requiring mention in the trust document. Fact 2 outlines a separate benefit related to early termination of the policy, independent of ownership status.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="4bed57f0-9e45-43f0-a325-58c36ead1450">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence concerns legal ownership criteria under a trust agreement. The second sentence describes a corporate leadership role unrelated to those ownership terms.</data>
  <data key="d4"></data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="d1560b93-8e33-4768-9496-b61910e313b4">
  <data key="d3">The statement about ownership rights depends on content within the trust document, but the issuance date provides only contextual timing information unrelated to the rule’s applicability.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="5c3f4413-4b34-4cda-af56-ca0ece4739ca">
  <data key="d3">The condition that no insured holds ownership unless specified in the trust directly explains why the policy’s terms—such as its beneficiaries and premium guarantees—are governed exclusively by the trust, making the issue date relevant to enforcement timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="288469c9-a76a-4bf8-b17b-752662f3a1f6">
  <data key="d3">The absence of ownership rights for the insureds reinforces why the trust—rather than individuals—is designated as the beneficiary, maintaining structural integrity within the estate plan.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="eb6fcda1-6a00-45e2-a278-6ecbfce50c86">
  <data key="d3">Since the trust owns the policy and appoints the trustee, the absence of individual ownership among the insureds is consistent with the trust’s structural intent, as confirmed by its management under First National Bank of Connecticut.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="2c0afdf7-25f1-4c84-88a2-08afcc4de210">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 reinforces the legitimacy of fact_sentence_1 by specifying that ownership depends entirely on the trust’s provisions, thereby validating the trust’s exclusive control over the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONFIRMS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="5f7b886a-0895-4321-a983-5dcc79a03f70">
  <data key="d3">The absence of automatic ownership rights reinforces the policy’s function in estate planning, where coordinated beneficiary outcomes are prioritized over individual control.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="70d6f164-2c6e-4960-9154-c1e13245d12c">
  <data key="d3">Trust-based ownership requirements ensure the policy functions effectively for estate tax liquidity, preventing premature access or mismanagement while maintaining alignment with long-term estate goals.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="30aa32c7-4f8f-42cf-99bf-592ed9d2eaab">
  <data key="d3">While the timing of the death benefit is fixed by the survival clause, actual distribution hinges on whether the rightful owners (as per the trust) are properly identified and authorized to act on behalf of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">INFLUENCES_CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="b0f11a92-dc8a-424a-9605-d53beb6ddfba">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states that ownership depends entirely on the trust document, which aligns directly with the detailed explanation provided in fact_sentence_1 about the trust’s exclusive authority over policy rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="e3e49333-4660-4170-be0e-750c514619c6">
  <data key="d3">Since neither insured holds ownership rights absent explicit trust provisions, assignment of the policy inherently depends on trustee approval, directly supporting the condition stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="a08544cf-1d57-4a48-8d71-04334028f70e">
  <data key="d3">The second fact elaborates on the conditions under which ownership might exist, directly supporting the premise in the first fact that no individual owns the policy unless defined within the trust’s documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">DEPENDS_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">Without explicit ownership rights granted in the trust, the policyholder lacks legal standing to initiate a split even if permitted under policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">Ownership rights, absent explicit mention in the trust, prevent any unilateral action—even timely ones—such as initiating a policy split after the first death, thus rendering the deadline inoperative without proper ownership.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">Ownership rights governed by the trust are essential for managing the policy post-first-death, including triggering the split option only when both insured remain alive.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">Ownership rights governed by the trust affect eligibility to trigger the split option, which requires proof of insurability—a prerequisite tied to the person initiating the action.</data>
  <data key="d4">CONDITIONAL_ON</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">Ownership rights determine eligibility for policy splits, making the split feature conditional on the presence of such rights outlined in the trust agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
