<edge source="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5" target="00066f02-a38b-49d1-abda-4a4d40847e5c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 grants a temporary cancellation privilege independent of ownership claims. Fact_sentence_1 clarifies that ownership itself depends on documentation, meaning even if someone cancels, it does not imply ownership unless stated in the trust.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT_OF</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.45</data>
</edge>
<edge source="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5" target="dc5e7101-a50d-4b25-8d7d-9d2fc8fab9fc">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 30-day free look period allows the policyholder to terminate coverage early if desired. This right does not affect or rely on whether an assignment requires trustee consent.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5" target="510a4351-8c5a-44d4-a731-1c1dea4323a8">
  <data key="d3">The ability to cancel the policy within 30 days allows the policyholder to trigger a full refund of premiums paid. Without the cancellation right, the refund would not apply.</data>
  <data key="d4">CAUSES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5" target="a81b97c9-146b-4343-9c7c-db9ffafb1f05">
  <data key="d3">The policy's cancellation terms do not depend on the physical location of the issuing company. Information about where Estate Planning Life Assurance Ltd. is headquartered does not affect the free look period available to policyholders.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5" target="d1560b93-8e33-4768-9496-b61910e313b4">
  <data key="d3">The 30-day cancellation right applies from the moment the policy is received, but its exact start point depends on external timing information like the issue date.</data>
  <data key="d4">PRECEDES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5" target="4bed57f0-9e45-43f0-a325-58c36ead1450">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence describes a policyholder's right to cancel within 30 days of receiving the policy, based on the free look provision. The second sentence identifies a leadership role within the issuing company but does not relate to that right or its conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">NONE</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5" target="eb6fcda1-6a00-45e2-a278-6ecbfce50c86">
  <data key="d3">While the policy is held by a trust managed by First National Bank of Connecticut, the policyholder retains a limited right to cancel it within 30 days of receipt, reflecting a balance between institutional control and individual flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">SUPPLEMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5" target="2c0afdf7-25f1-4c84-88a2-08afcc4de210">
  <data key="d3">While the trust legally owns the policy, its ability to act on cancellation rights hinges on provisions allowing such action through the trustee, meaning the 30-day option complements rather than contradicts the ownership arrangement.</data>
  <data key="d4">COMPLIMENTS</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5" target="288469c9-a76a-4bf8-b17b-752662f3a1f6">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 30-day free look period allows the policy’s owner—the Hartford Family Irrevocable Life Insurance Trust—to cancel the policy, reinforcing its central role as both owner and beneficiary.</data>
  <data key="d4">CORROBORATES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5" target="5c3f4413-4b34-4cda-af56-ca0ece4739ca">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 30-day free look period, as stated in fact_sentence_2, explains why the issue date specified in fact_sentence_1 is significant—it marks the start of the cancellation window.</data>
  <data key="d4">TIMING_CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5" target="a9741679-16e2-4128-9ef2-70da1404cc14">
  <data key="d3">The 30-day free look period allows cancellation before any obligations arise, including future splitting options after the first death, making it temporally prior and conditionally unrelated to later structural changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5" target="80ae385b-ee9d-4149-9014-5ca0ab9ab203">
  <data key="d3">The 30-day cancellation option exists independently of the later split provision, meaning it has no bearing on whether the policy can be divided after the first death.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5" target="017f6bf7-89af-44fe-8781-e25d1c431f9c">
  <data key="d3">The 30-day cancellation window exists independently of whether both insured persons survive the first death. It applies before any claims or splits occur, making it irrelevant to the conditions governing the split option.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5" target="eead227f-2ad6-4a45-877d-62ba5081b981">
  <data key="d3">The 30-day cancellation window allows withdrawal before any events occur, whereas the split option requires survival past the first death and submission of medical proof—conditions that come later and do not affect initial cancellation rights.</data>
  <data key="d4">INDEPENDENT</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="53c06c8c-e397-4baa-9acf-75ee3c5472d5" target="3438d3e0-d9fb-46af-8d4c-8f979cc55d1f">
  <data key="d3">The 30-day right to cancel allows policyholders to reassess decisions involving major life changes, including those requiring a policy split—for example, in divorce or trust adjustments—as part of estate planning strategy.</data>
  <data key="d4">ENABLES</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
